{"parentUuid":"50a4a599-1cf4-4db5-acf5-e3b456568fc4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNKgc8iYmJkHxDhJp6pM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rnosc1gKjkSqXckJpmcSYk","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix 483 delta-path finding","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix ONE confirmed agent-review finding on an open PR. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize (branch fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize, PR entireio/entire-brain#483). Do NOT touch any other repo/worktree. Do NOT merge, do NOT open PRs, do NOT request review. The branch ALREADY has main merged in (commit \"Merge origin/main into fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize\") — do not merge main again, do not rebase.\n\nTHE FINDING (medium, current, id 01M5R8FS7JTP), verbatim:\n\"The oversize skip is applied to the identity capture, the full index build and `collectHistorySessionDigests`. The short-term delta path in `history_delta.go` also calls `readHistorySessionInventoryFile`, and `shortTermCanonicalInputRefusal` still treats `memory_input_too_large` as a refusal of the entire delta. A single oversize transcript therefore still blocks the overlay for every other session.\"\n\nIt is CORRECT and it is an incompleteness in my own fix. Context:\n- #483's point: ONE transcript too large to read must not refuse the whole history index. I added sentinel `errHistoryTranscriptTooLarge = errors.New(memoryErrInputTooLarge)` + `historyTranscriptTooLargeError(rel)` in internal/cli/history.go, and made three readers SKIP instead of refuse: captureHistoryProjectionIdentityMode, buildBrainHistoryIndexSnapshotContext, collectHistorySessionDigests. `classifyTranscriptReadError` in internal/cli/transcript_store.go also wraps the sentinel for the store/checkpoint-blob path.\n- I found the store path by an anchored search for the error CODE string rather than the Go identifier, which is what caught transcript_store.go. I did NOT sweep history_delta.go. Same miss, one file further.\n- NOTE: the bound is now `base.MaxDocumentTranscriptBytes` (a var in internal/cli/internal/base) after main's COR-2268 refactor; the unqualified `maxDocumentTranscriptBytes` no longer exists.\n\nWHAT TO DO: make the short-term delta path behave like the other three — one oversize transcript is skipped (with a warning naming it), the overlay is still built for every other session. Read `shortTermCanonicalInputRefusal` and its callers before changing anything, and check whether the delta has its OWN notion of partial success you must thread through rather than inventing one. Prefer reusing the existing sentinel over a new error. If the delta genuinely cannot be partial for a sound reason, say so with the evidence instead of forcing it.\n\nBefore you start, run an anchored search for BOTH the identifier and the error-code string across internal/ so you do not repeat my miss — report every call site you found and what you did about each.\n\nNON-NEGOTIABLE verification, in this order:\n1. Targeted tests green: `rtk proxy env GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<your pattern>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`. Confirm with -v that your test NAMES actually ran — a `-run` pattern matching nothing also prints \"ok\".\n2. VERIFIED-BY-WEAKENING: for EACH new/changed guard, patch the production code so it SHOULD fail, run it, confirm RED, restore. Verify your patch applied (unique match) before trusting any green; a weakening that stays green means the test proves nothing.\n3. Full gate: `mise run test:prepush`. Redirect to a file and grep the log for '^FAIL' and the recorded exit — the task is one `set -e` script so only its first line echoes. Never trust a bare exit 0 over an unread log.\n4. The three existing #483 guards MUST still pass: TestHistoryIndexSkipsAnOversizeTranscriptAndIndexesTheRest, TestOversizeTranscriptIsSkippedByEveryInventoryReader, TestStoreSizeRefusalClassifiesAsTheSkippableOversizeError. So must main's TestOverridableProductionBoundsKeepTheirDefaults (it pins that a test's bound override does not leak).\n\nThen `git add` only files you changed, commit (conventional scoped subject; body explains WHY; NO AI/Claude attribution footer of any kind), `git push origin fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize`.\n\nEnv notes: this shell sets FORCE_COLOR=3 and breaks colour-assert tests on correct code — reproduce on main before believing such a failure. Use rtk. Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n\nREPORT BACK caveman-ultra compressed, no padding: every call site your search found + disposition; files+lines changed; each weakening and red/green; prepush exit + FAIL count; commit SHA; anything unverified. If the finding is wrong, say REFUTED with evidence."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2774,"cache_read_input_tokens":217225,"output_tokens":1784,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2774,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1784,"cache_read_input_tokens":217225,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2774},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Rnosc1gKjkSqXckJpmcSYk":{"description":"Fix 483 delta-path finding","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix ONE confirmed agent-review finding on an open PR. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize (branch fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize, PR entireio/entire-brain#483). Do NOT touch any other repo/worktree. Do NOT merge, do NOT open PRs, do NOT request review. The