{"parentUuid":"5cb27820-137d-4b8d-9bfc-63720dc4b63c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNL3g6vQVxYqvydnWnWC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recording the durable lessons while that runs:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_read_input_tokens":237884,"output_tokens":1111,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":764,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1111,"cache_read_input_tokens":237884,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":764},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5d387c7c-6798-418c-89dc-48c58bf8b54f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNL3fXwJLaK23x83LRwm","requestRef":"09d27044-2053-4e16-88d2-ff8120ce6481","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"3e8d12ec-9ce1-454b-98f6-a54f280ad87b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:32:09.017Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"3e8d12ec-9ce1-454b-98f6-a54f280ad87b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNL3g6vQVxYqvydnWnWC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GPY2QhK7bCCutYvujUfCwS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"M=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory; cat > \"$M/trail-findings-wrong-trail-number.md\" <<'EOF'\n---\nname: trail-findings-wrong-trail-number\ndescription: \"A repo-scoped trail URL number is NOT a project trail number; querying by project silently returns a different repo's trail\"\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nThe Entire Gates summary links `entire.com/gh/<org>/<repo>/trails/384` — a **repo-scoped**\nnumber. `entire trail finding list --trail 384 --project gh/<org>` resolves 384 in the\n**project** numbering space, a different trail entirely. I read a dependabot bump on `cli`\nand concluded my own 13 PRs had no findings.\n\nThe symptom is not an error. It is `trail #384 has no open changes`, which reads exactly like\n\"reviewed, nothing found\".\n\n**Why:** I then told a peer session \"0 findings, but I could not corroborate it\". The real answer\nwas **8 open findings across 4 PRs**, including two mediums that were real bugs I had introduced.\nA confident \"couldn't verify\" is still a wrong answer when the query was simply misaddressed.\n\n**How to apply:** query with the `<repo>/<number>` form — `--trail entire-brain/384` — and confirm\nthe returned `trail.title` and `trail.branch` match the PR you think you are looking at before\nbelieving any count. The JSON carries both. Also pass `--status any --freshness any\n--include-dismissed`, then re-query with `--freshness current` to separate live findings from\nstale ones: see [[trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls]].\nEOF\ncat > \"$M/build-failure-is-not-a-weakening-red.md\" <<'EOF'\n---\nname: build-failure-is-not-a-weakening-red\ndescription: \"A weakening that fails to COMPILE proves nothing; [build failed] is not the guard firing\"\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nWeakening a guard by deleting the branch that used a variable left it unused, so Go refused to\ncompile and the run printed `FAIL ... [build failed]`. I read two reds and nearly recorded both\nguards as proven. Neither test had executed.\n\n**Why:** `[build failed]` and `--- FAIL: TestX` both appear under a line starting `FAIL`, so any\ngrep for `^FAIL` scores them the same. The whole value of verified-by-weakening is that the named\ntest runs and objects; a compile error means it never ran.\n\n**How to apply:** a weakening is only proven when the output contains `--- FAIL: <the test you\nexpected>`. Grep for `--- FAIL` and read the test name, not `^FAIL`. If the patch orphans a\nvariable, keep it alive (`_ = definitive`) so the package still builds. Same family as\n[[mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test]] and [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]].\nEOF\necho \"written\"; ls -la \"$M\" | grep -cE \"\\.md$\"","description":"Write the two new memory files"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_read_input_tokens":237884,"output_tokens":1111,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":764,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1111,"cache_read_input_tokens":237884,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":764},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GPY2QhK7bCCutYvujUfCwS":{"command":"M=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory; cat > \"$M/trail-findings-wrong-trail-number.md\" <<'EOF'\n---\nname: trail-findings-wrong-trail-number\ndescription: \"A repo-scoped trail URL number is NOT a project trail number; querying by project silently returns a different repo's trail\"\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nThe Entire Gates summary links `entire.com/gh/<org>/<repo>/trails/384` — a **repo-scoped**\nnumber. `entire trail finding list --trail 384 --project gh/<org>` resolves 384 in the\n**project** numbering space, a different trail entirely. I read a dependabot bump on `cli`\nand concluded my own 13 PRs had no findings.\n\nThe symptom is not an error. It is `trail #384 has no open changes`, which reads exactly like\n\"reviewed, nothing found\".\n\n**Why:** I then told a peer session \"0 findings, but I could not corroborate it\". The real answer\nwas **8 open findings across 4 PRs**, including two mediums that were real bugs I had introduced.\nA confident \"couldn't verify\" is still a wrong answer when the query was simply misaddressed.\n\n**How to apply:** query with the `<repo>/<number>` form — `--trail entire-brain/384` — and confirm\nthe returned `trail.title` and `trail.branch` match the PR you think you are looking at before\nbelieving any count. The JSON carries both. Also pass `--status any --freshness any\n--include-dismissed`, then re-query with `--freshness current` to separate live findings from\nstale ones: see [[trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls]].\nEOF\ncat > \"$M/build-failure-is-not-a-weakening-red.md\" <<'EOF'\n---\nname: build-failure-is-not-a-weakening-red\ndescription: \"A weakening that fails to COMPILE proves nothing; [build failed] is not the guard firing\"\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nWeakening a guard by deleting the branch that used a variable left it unused, so Go refused to\ncompile and the run printed `FAIL ... [build failed]`. I read two reds and nearly recorded both\nguards as proven. Neither test had executed.\n\n**Why:** `[build failed]` and `--- FAIL: TestX` both appear under a line starting `FAIL`, so any\ngrep for `^FAIL` scores them the same. The whole value of verified-by-weakening is that the named\ntest runs and objects; a compile error means it never ran.\n\n**How to apply:** a weakening is only proven when the output contains `--- FAIL: <the test you\nexpected>`. Grep for `--- FAIL` and read the test name, not `^FAIL`. If the patch orphans a\nvariable, keep it alive (`_ = definitive`) so the package still builds. Same family as\n[[mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test]] and [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]].\nEOF\necho \"written\"; ls -la \"$M\" | grep -cE \"\\.md$\"","description":"Write the two new memory files"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5d387c7c-6798-418c-89dc-48c58bf8b54f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNL3fXwJLaK23x83LRwm","requestRef":"09d27044-2053-4e16-88d2-ff8120ce6481","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"1a76716e-d86c-43c6-b8d9-4877e080dba3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:32:24.253Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
