{"parentUuid":"0833b29d-01d8-4f96-8af3-3f4c9e944adf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNL8mNZmsw3ankFf8cby","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QSGqo2M2ai2vtFtZkiLMDc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/fact1.txt\" <<'EOF'\nGuards on a function do not cover its call site. Unwiring checkMCPSurfaceReachable from brainDoctorReadOnlyReport (internal/cli/lifecycle_ops.go) left every test in internal/cli/mcp_reachability_test.go green, because all of them call the function directly. Doctor now calls through the doctorMCPSurfaceCheck var so TestDoctorActuallyRunsTheMCPSurfaceCheck can assert the wiring without spawning a process; deleting the call turns it red. Same var-for-testability idiom as the overridable read bounds in internal/cli/internal/base. When a change adds a call into an existing pipeline, weaken the CALL SITE, not just the function.\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/fact2.txt\" <<'EOF'\nThe trail number in an Entire Gates summary URL (entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/384) is repo-scoped and is NOT a project trail number. Querying it as one (entire trail finding list --trail 384 --project gh/entireio) resolves a different repository's trail and answers \"trail #384 has no open changes\", which reads exactly like a clean review. Use the repo-scoped form --trail entire-brain/384, and verify the returned trail.title and trail.branch match the PR before believing any finding count. This misread hid 8 open findings across 4 brain PRs.\nEOF\nentire brain remember \"$(cat \"$S/fact1.txt\")\" --path workflow.testing.invariant --branch main 2>&1 | tail -3; entire brain remember \"$(cat \"$S/fact2.txt\")\" --path workflow.tooling.gotcha --branch main 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Record both facts in brain"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":427,"cache_read_input_tokens":243828,"output_tokens":1110,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":309},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":427,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1110,"cache_read_input_tokens":243828,"cache_creation_input_tokens":427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":427},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QSGqo2M2ai2vtFtZkiLMDc":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/fact1.txt\" <<'EOF'\nGuards on a function do not cover its call site. Unwiring checkMCPSurfaceReachable from brainDoctorReadOnlyReport (internal/cli/lifecycle_ops.go) left every test in internal/cli/mcp_reachability_test.go green, because all of them call the function directly. Doctor now calls through the doctorMCPSurfaceCheck var so TestDoctorActuallyRunsTheMCPSurfaceCheck can assert the wiring without spawning a process; deleting the call turns it red. Same var-for-testability idiom as the overridable read bounds in internal/cli/internal/base. When a change adds a call into an existing pipeline, weaken the CALL SITE, not just the function.\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/fact2.txt\" <<'EOF'\nThe trail number in an Entire Gates summary URL (entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/384) is repo-scoped and is NOT a project trail number. Querying it as one (entire trail finding list --trail 384 --project gh/entireio) resolves a different repository's trail and answers \"trail #384 has no open changes\", which reads exactly like a clean review. Use the repo-scoped form --trail entire-brain/384, and verify the returned trail.title and trail.branch match the PR before believing any finding count. This misread hid 8 open findings across 4 brain PRs.\nEOF\nentire brain remember \"$(cat \"$S/fact1.txt\")\" --path workflow.testing.invariant --branch main 2>&1 | tail -3; entire brain remember \"$(cat \"$S/fact2.txt\")\" --path workflow.tooling.gotcha --branch main 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Record both facts in brain"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"853772b0-67c9-4303-ae0c-c02dc762a5a7","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgNL8krZ6mRchtBErR5T1","requestRef":"5524f416-5b77-4e1b-afeb-e01b724ee6b0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"676c01a8-f847-4dfa-bb02-9c9e585c4e27","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:33:32.681Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
