{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","prNumber":477,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/477","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:33:56.769Z"}
{"parentUuid":"92c93b74-175b-4a2b-97a7-128f79dfe290","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14477846 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"72765584-497a-4683-9a9d-1e0b04f0a473","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:33:56.669Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14477846 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"72765584-497a-4683-9a9d-1e0b04f0a473","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNLBjkfufr5x8HafwrRX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RZ79LgazborixM7zGsWDes","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix 477 unbounded frame allocation","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix ONE confirmed agent-review finding on an open PR. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach (branch feat/mcp-surface-reachable, PR entireio/entire-brain#477). Do NOT touch any other repo/worktree. Do NOT merge, do NOT open PRs, do NOT request review. The branch ALREADY has main merged in — do not merge main again, do not rebase.\n\nTHE FINDING (low, current, id 01M5QWT2Y3Q1), verbatim:\n\"`readMCPFrame` allocates `make([]byte, length)` from the child's `Content-Length` with no upper bound. A misbehaving binary can make doctor try a multi-GB allocation before the timeout applies. Cap the length (for example a few MiB) and return an error beyond it.\"\n\nIt is CORRECT. Context: #477 adds a doctor check that spawns the brain's own MCP server and asks it for its tool list, to catch the silent failures in this class (claude --safe-mode stripping MCP, a comma in CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS, a plugin path purged from /tmp reported as CONNECTION_CLOSED). `readMCPFrame` parses the LSP-style framing. The child is our own binary, but the whole point of the check is that it runs when something is already wrong, so a malformed or hostile frame is exactly the case it must survive.\n\nWHAT TO DO:\n- Cap the frame length and return a clear error above it, naming the announced length and the cap.\n- Do NOT invent a new constant if this repo already has a suitable bound: look in internal/cli/internal/base (safe_read.go) first — it holds overridable read ceilings (MaxDocumentTranscriptBytes, DefaultMaxReadBytes) declared as VARS specifically so oversize-fixture tests can lower a bound instead of materialising a huge input, and there is a TestOverridableProductionBoundsKeepTheirDefaults that pins their production values. If you add a bound there, that pin test must be updated; if you add a local const instead, justify why in your report.\n- There is also an existing `base.SafeReadAll(r, max, source)` helper and a `base.ReadBoundExceededError{Source, Max}` typed error. Prefer reusing them over hand-rolling, if they fit the framed-read shape.\n- Check whether the NEGATIVE / zero / missing Content-Length cases are already handled; if not, handle them in the same change (a negative length is the other half of the same defect).\n\nNON-NEGOTIABLE verification, in this order:\n1. Targeted tests green: `rtk proxy env GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<your pattern>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`. Run with -v and confirm your test NAMES actually appear — a `-run` pattern that matches nothing also prints \"ok\".\n2. VERIFIED-BY-WEAKENING, for EACH new/changed guard: patch the production code so the guard SHOULD fail, run it, confirm you see `--- FAIL: <your test name>`, then restore. CRITICAL: `[build failed]` is NOT a red — if your patch orphans a variable the package stops compiling and the test never runs. Keep the package building (e.g. `_ = x`) and grep for `--- FAIL` with the test name, never bare `^FAIL`.\n3. Full gate: `mise run test:prepush`. Redirect to a file, then grep the log for '^FAIL' and the recorded exit code. The task is one `set -e` script so only its first line echoes; gofmt and vet run inside it silently. Never trust a bare exit 0 over an unread log.\n4. These must still pass: TestMCPSurfaceCheckIsOptIn, TestMCPSurfaceCheckNeverSpawnsTheTestBinary, TestDoctorActuallyRunsTheMCPSurfaceCheck, TestOverridableProductionBoundsKeepTheirDefaults.\n\nIMPORTANT HAZARD specific to this file: never let a test spawn `os.Executable()`. Under `go test` that IS the test binary, and running it re-runs the whole package, recursively — it has already forked this machine until it gave up. Tests here inject a fake server path instead (see `mcpFakeServer` and the `exe func() (string, error)` parameter).\n\nThen `git add` only files you changed, commit (conventional scoped subject; body explains WHY; NO AI/Claude attribution footer of any kind), `git push origin feat/mcp-surface-reachable`.\n\nEnv notes: this shell sets FORCE_COLOR=3 and breaks colour-assert tests on correct code — reproduce on main before believing such a failure. Use rtk. Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n\nREPORT BACK caveman-ultra compressed, no padding: the bound you chose + where it lives + why; whether you reused base helpers or not and why; negative/zero-length handling; each weakening with the exact `--- FAIL` line you saw; prepush exit + FAIL count; commit SHA; anything unverified. If the finding is wrong, say REFUTED with evidence."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1499,"cache_read_input_tokens":245471,"output_tokens":1855,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1499,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1855,"cache_read_input_tokens":245471,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1499},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RZ79LgazborixM7zGsWDes":{"description":"Fix 477 unbounded frame allocation","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix ONE confirmed agent-review finding on an open PR. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach (branch feat/mcp-surface-reachable, PR entireio/entire-brain#477). Do NOT touch any other repo/worktree. Do NOT merge, do NOT open PRs, do NOT request review. The branch ALREADY has main merged in — do not merge main again, do not rebase.\n\nTHE FINDING (low, current, id 01M5QWT2Y3Q1), verbatim:\n\"`readMCPFrame` allocates `make([]byte, length)` from the child's `Content-Length` with no upper bound. A misbehaving binary can make doctor try a multi-GB allocation before the timeout applies. Cap the length (for example a few MiB) and return an error beyond it.\"\n\nIt is CORRECT. Context: #477 adds a doctor check that spawns the brain's own MCP server and asks it for its tool list, to catch the silent failures in this class (claude --safe-mode stripping MCP, a comma in CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS, a plugin path purged from /tmp reported as CONNECTION_CLOSED). `readMCPFrame` parses the LSP-style framing. The child is our own binary, but the whole point of the check is that it runs when something is already wrong, so a malformed or hostile frame is exactly the case it must survive.\n\nWHAT TO DO:\n- Cap the frame length and return a clear error above it, naming the announced length and the cap.\n- Do NOT invent a new constant if this repo already has a suitable bound: look in internal/cli/internal/base (safe_read.go) first — it holds overridable read ceilings (MaxDocumentTranscriptBytes, DefaultMaxReadBytes) declared as VARS specifically so oversize-fixture tests can lower a bound instead of materialising a huge input, and there is a TestOverridableProductionBoundsKeepTheirDefaults that pins their production values. If you add a bound there, that pin test must be updated; if you add a local const instead, justify why in your report.\n- There is also an existing `base.SafeReadAll(r, max, source)` helper and a `base.ReadBoundExceededError{Source, Max}` typed error. Prefer reusing them over hand-rolling, if they fit the framed-read shape.\n- Check whether the NEGATIVE / zero / missing Content-Length cases are already handled; if not, handle them in the same change (a negative length is the other half of the same defect).\n\nNON-NEGOTIABLE verification, in this order:\n1. Targeted tests green: `rtk proxy env GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<your pattern>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`. Run with -v and confirm your test NAMES actually appear — a `-run` pattern that matches nothing also prints \"ok\".\n2. VERIFIED-BY-WEAKENING, for EACH new/changed guard: patch the production code so the guard SHOULD fail, run it, confirm you see `--- FAIL: <your test name>`, then restore. CRITICAL: `[build failed]` is NOT a red — if your patch orphans a variable the package stops compiling and the test never runs. Keep the package building (e.g. `_ = x`) and grep for `--- FAIL` with the test name, never bare `^FAIL`.\n3. Full gate: `mise run test:prepush`. Redirect to a file, then grep the log for '^FAIL' and the recorded exit code. The task is one `set -e` script so only its first line echoes; gofmt and vet run inside it silently. Never trust a bare exit 0 over an unread log.\n4. These must still pass: TestMCPSurfaceCheckIsOptIn, TestMCPSurfaceCheckNeverSpawnsTheTestBinary, TestDoctorActuallyRunsTheMCPSurfaceCheck, TestOverridableProductionBoundsKeepTheirDefaults.\n\nIMPORTANT HAZARD specific to this file: never let a test spawn `os.Executable()`. Under `go test` that IS the test binary, and running it re-runs the whole package, recursively — it has already forked this machine until it gave up. Tests here inject a fake server path instead (see `mcpFakeServer` and the `exe func() (string, error)` parameter).\n\nThen `git add` only files you changed, commit (conventional scoped subject; body explains WHY; NO AI/Claude attribution footer of any kind), `git push origin feat/mcp-surface-reachable`.\n\nEnv notes: this shell sets FORCE_COLOR=3 and breaks colour-assert tests on correct code — reproduce on main before believing such a failure. Use rtk. Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n\nREPORT BACK caveman-ultra compressed, no padding: the bound you chose + where it lives + why; whether you reused base helpers or not and why; negative/zero-length handling; each weakening with the exact `--- FAIL` line you saw; prepush exit + FAIL count; commit SHA; anything unverified. If the finding is wrong, say REFUTED with evidence."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"82f6b046-6971-484a-838c-104f811356bc","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNLBjT4XL3qULeKghNeN","requestRef":"8c49d1c7-e3ba-4ddd-8f7c-176e9c148713","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"c43371c4-022c-4c71-8d3d-7d418e673b6a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:34:21.761Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
