{"parentUuid":"bcb1e29d-ee68-41ed-a20d-bcf356af334e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNLQUQoDhtCHxrXxFPRb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B7M71bLhpij87GreWiW1Fo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; gh pr view 484 --repo entireio/entire-brain --json body --jq .body > \"$S/pr484b.md\"; python3 - \"$S/pr484b.md\" <<'PY'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p).read()\nadd = \"\"\"## Two review findings, both correct\n\n**The probe memoized its own failures.** `probeGraphAncestorSupport` returned a\nbare bool, so \"ran, feature absent\" and \"did not run at all\" were the same\nanswer — and the memo cached both. One timed-out probe marked a provider\nunsupported for the life of the process, and a provider that *does* support\nancestor queries was never asked again. It now reports whether its answer is\ndefinitive, and only a definitive answer is stored: a binary that rejects the\n`graph` verb is definitive (wrong kind of binary, same answer every time), while\na timeout or a spawn failure is not, and malformed JSON could be a truncated\nread as easily as a binary that cannot speak JSON. It still fails closed in\nevery case. Two weakenings — cache everything, cache nothing — turn the two new\nguards red in turn.\n\n**`unreliable` is structurally empty, which made it misleading on its own.** It\ncan only name paths the answer actually returned records for, and an ancestor\nstore has already dropped the records for changed files — *exactly* those paths.\nSo it is empty in the common case even when the answer is incomplete, and a\nreader would take that as \"nothing to worry about\". The provider sends\n`excluded_records` for precisely this reason; brief was re-emitting four of its\nfive fields and dropping the one that separates an incomplete answer from a\ncomplete one. Now carried through, with a guard pinning the combination that\nmatters: empty `unreliable`, non-zero `excluded_records`.\n\nThe provider side is unchanged, so this needs nothing from graph #380.\n\n\"\"\"\nmarker = \"🤖 Generated with\"\nassert s.count(marker)==1\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s.replace(marker, add+marker))\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\ngh pr edit 484 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body-file \"$S/pr484b.md\" >/dev/null && echo \"body updated\"; cat > \"$S/b4.json\" <<'JSON'\n[{\"id\":\"finding-484-probe-memo\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"done\",\n  \"title\":\"#484 DONE+pushed: cache only a DEFINITIVE probe answer (host-verb rejection is definitive, timeout/malformed are not) + excluded_records now reaches the emitted block. 2 weakenings red, prepush green. Graph confirms #380 needs nothing\"}]\nJSON\npython3 \"$S/board_update.py\" \"$S/b4.json\"","description":"Update 484's body and board row"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":787,"cache_read_input_tokens":271351,"output_tokens":1134,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":59},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":787,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1134,"cache_read_input_tokens":271351,"cache_creation_input_tokens":787,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":787},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01B7M71bLhpij87GreWiW1Fo":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; gh pr view 484 --repo entireio/entire-brain --json body --jq .body > \"$S/pr484b.md\"; python3 - \"$S/pr484b.md\" <<'PY'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p).read()\nadd = \"\"\"## Two review findings, both correct\n\n**The probe memoized its own failures.** `probeGraphAncestorSupport` returned a\nbare bool, so \"ran, feature absent\" and \"did not run at all\" were the same\nanswer — and the memo cached both. One timed-out probe marked a provider\nunsupported for the life of the process, and a provider that *does* support\nancestor queries was never asked again. It now reports whether its answer is\ndefinitive, and only a definitive answer is stored: a binary that rejects the\n`graph` verb is definitive (wrong kind of binary, same answer every time), while\na timeout or a spawn failure is not, and malformed JSON could be a truncated\nread as easily as a binary that cannot speak JSON. It still fails closed in\nevery case. Two weakenings — cache everything, cache nothing — turn the two new\nguards red in turn.\n\n**`unreliable` is structurally empty, which made it misleading on its own.** It\ncan only name paths the answer actually returned records for, and an ancestor\nstore has already dropped the records for changed files — *exactly* those paths.\nSo it is empty in the common case even when the answer is incomplete, and a\nreader would take that as \"nothing to worry about\". The provider sends\n`excluded_records` for precisely this reason; brief was re-emitting four of its\nfive fields and dropping the one that separates an incomplete answer from a\ncomplete one. Now carried through, with a guard pinning the combination that\nmatters: empty `unreliable`, non-zero `excluded_records`.\n\nThe provider side is unchanged, so this needs nothing from graph #380.\n\n\"\"\"\nmarker = \"🤖 Generated with\"\nassert s.count(marker)==1\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s.replace(marker, add+marker))\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\ngh pr edit 484 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body-file \"$S/pr484b.md\" >/dev/null && echo \"body updated\"; cat > \"$S/b4.json\" <<'JSON'\n[{\"id\":\"finding-484-probe-memo\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"done\",\n  \"title\":\"#484 DONE+pushed: cache only a DEFINITIVE probe answer (host-verb rejection is definitive, timeout/malformed are not) + excluded_records now reaches the emitted block. 2 weakenings red, prepush green. Graph confirms #380 needs nothing\"}]\nJSON\npython3 \"$S/board_update.py\" \"$S/b4.json\"","description":"Update 484's body and board row"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b9dd2fcd-455f-4890-b85e-deff83e697bc","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgNLQU5T5AP8CfqMeiA56","requestRef":"97284c31-b0e4-4b73-8cb1-e6902bc16ba8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"7a46fd2c-579b-4ada-b84e-7da82e83c1aa","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:37:02.669Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
