{"parentUuid":"d7f349e0-a1b5-43d0-b74c-9441adf6bb72","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNM7RLPgw1TA3jAUbNSD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recording the lesson — it's a sharper instance of a class I already track:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2359,"cache_read_input_tokens":293688,"output_tokens":1326,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":272},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2359,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1326,"cache_read_input_tokens":293688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2359},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d7f1e623-b805-4d45-98e1-9538b96f4441","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNM7QwaQBtNLjh3xBUUL","requestRef":"4d5ea030-f2bf-4435-9c26-7dcdb80d1f57","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"bece9208-633e-49ea-9740-e21aa6156b78","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:46:10.967Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"bece9208-633e-49ea-9740-e21aa6156b78","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNM7RLPgw1TA3jAUbNSD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FAGYy42FZ7qe719L4sDG6c","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"M=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory; cat >> \"$M/containment-for-exactness.md\" <<'EOF'\n\n**The renamed-test variant (2026-10-25, entire-brain #483).** A subagent correctly narrowed a\nbehaviour — one oversize transcript should no longer refuse the whole short-term delta — and in\ndoing so renamed `TestShortTermDeltaBoundFailurePreservesPriorOverlay` to assert the opposite\ncontract. It reported that the old general property \"survives in\" two other named tests, and that\nboth exist and pass.\n\nBoth claims were true and together still misleading. The two tests do assert\n`bytes.Equal(after, before)` on the published overlay — but for *different error classes* (a\ndegraded inventory, a membership race). Neither involves a bound breach. A sweep of every\noverlay-preservation assertion in the three relevant test files found none for\n`memoryErrInputTooLarge`. The replacement it did add tests the **classifier's boolean**\n(`shortTermCanonicalInputRefusal(err)`), not that the build declines to publish — a classifier\nstanding in for the behaviour its predecessor asserted.\n\n**Why:** \"the property survives in X and Y\" is the single easiest claim to accept, because X and Y\nreally do exist, really do pass, and really are about the same subsystem. Reading their names is\nnot verification; the error class they exercise is the thing that matters.\n\n**How to apply:** when a test is renamed or its contract inverted, grep every assertion of the old\nproperty and check which *input class* each one drives. If the only survivor tests a predicate\nrather than the observable effect, the guarantee is unguarded even though the suite is green. See\nalso [[ours-resolution-deletes-features]] and [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]]; the overruled\nrecord here was [[verified-by-weakening-doctrine]]'s sibling — a prior session had withdrawn this\nvery change, and that withdrawal deserved re-examination but its *coverage* concern was real.\nEOF\necho appended; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/b6.json\" <<'JSON'\n[{\"id\":\"finding-483-delta-path\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"doing\",\n  \"title\":\"#483 delta fix PUSHED (46afe735) + it OVERRULED a recorded withdrawal (accepted). BUT I verified its 'property survives elsewhere' claim and it FAILS: the 2 named tests guard other error classes; NO test now covers overlay-preservation on a bound breach. Sent back for 1 behavioural guard\"}]\nJSON\npython3 \"$S/board_update.py\" \"$S/b6.json\"","description":"Record the lesson and update the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2359,"cache_read_input_tokens":293688,"output_tokens":1326,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":272},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2359,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1326,"cache_read_input_tokens":293688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2359},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FAGYy42FZ7qe719L4sDG6c":{"command":"M=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory; cat >> \"$M/containment-for-exactness.md\" <<'EOF'\n\n**The renamed-test variant (2026-10-25, entire-brain #483).** A subagent correctly narrowed a\nbehaviour — one oversize transcript should no longer refuse the whole short-term delta — and in\ndoing so renamed `TestShortTermDeltaBoundFailurePreservesPriorOverlay` to assert the opposite\ncontract. It reported that the old general property \"survives in\" two other named tests, and that\nboth exist and pass.\n\nBoth claims were true and together still misleading. The two tests do assert\n`bytes.Equal(after, before)` on the published overlay — but for *different error classes* (a\ndegraded inventory, a membership race). Neither involves a bound breach. A sweep of every\noverlay-preservation assertion in the three relevant test files found none for\n`memoryErrInputTooLarge`. The replacement it did add tests the **classifier's boolean**\n(`shortTermCanonicalInputRefusal(err)`), not that the build declines to publish — a classifier\nstanding in for the behaviour its predecessor asserted.\n\n**Why:** \"the property survives in X and Y\" is the single easiest claim to accept, because X and Y\nreally do exist, really do pass, and really are about the same subsystem. Reading their names is\nnot verification; the error class they exercise is the thing that matters.\n\n**How to apply:** when a test is renamed or its contract inverted, grep every assertion of the old\nproperty and check which *input class* each one drives. If the only survivor tests a predicate\nrather than the observable effect, the guarantee is unguarded even though the suite is green. See\nalso [[ours-resolution-deletes-features]] and [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]]; the overruled\nrecord here was [[verified-by-weakening-doctrine]]'s sibling — a prior session had withdrawn this\nvery change, and that withdrawal deserved re-examination but its *coverage* concern was real.\nEOF\necho appended; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/b6.json\" <<'JSON'\n[{\"id\":\"finding-483-delta-path\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"doing\",\n  \"title\":\"#483 delta fix PUSHED (46afe735) + it OVERRULED a recorded withdrawal (accepted). BUT I verified its 'property survives elsewhere' claim and it FAILS: the 2 named tests guard other error classes; NO test now covers overlay-preservation on a bound breach. Sent back for 1 behavioural guard\"}]\nJSON\npython3 \"$S/board_update.py\" \"$S/b6.json\"","description":"Record the lesson and update the board"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d7f1e623-b805-4d45-98e1-9538b96f4441","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgNM7QwaQBtNLjh3xBUUL","requestRef":"4d5ea030-f2bf-4435-9c26-7dcdb80d1f57","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"c8358079-8efc-493b-9fee-22c43bbbb319","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:46:26.522Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
