{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","id":"5f55a6d6-7351-470a-8797-a7c1a33c49c6","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:46:27.270Z","version":"2.1.310","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"24017389debf7cd8bde5028ecf29c4ee6405c6fe767d12c483cd96a0e96b3788","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","context-1m-2025-08-07","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":64000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"4d5ea030-f2bf-4435-9c26-7dcdb80d1f57","keep":428,"tail":["2e428456185f7b4679b00859def745dbf63181158a6ee18452cdde4b0b9084c6","7fc0024f4635e6e9a3bdf331e32cbb508c21222864048d4adf1c41ab5ee5cdc1","b2a8909424c1d68e568bd9d4397ffa536464d14eacb4e95f24f1e540335d17f9"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",430,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"4458447c54243948ccfdbc0302f0442aa680d204ee7509ca523fe642af375c3c"}
{"parentUuid":"f131ef88-8895-45fc-a51c-3ea98c5aa42d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14427266 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1d97ba4e-0c2b-46d7-8e17-0da8840160d8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:46:27.239Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14427266 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"1d97ba4e-0c2b-46d7-8e17-0da8840160d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNM94a2oU8BwrKAfyKm9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#483's fix is in, but I sent one thing back.** Worth being precise about what was right and what wasn't.\n\nThe agent did strong work: an anchored sweep that found **six** readers of this condition, not the one in the finding — including a fifth it correctly left alone as dead code (verified via graph `neighbors`), and a sixth in the cache-retention sweep it deliberately left refusing, because an unreadable cached copy means it *cannot prove deletion is safe*, and failing safe in a destructive path is right. It also caught its own weakening matching two sites, and recognised that the green run which followed proved nothing.\n\nIt also **overruled a recorded prior decision** — a previous session had withdrawn this exact change. I checked the record. The withdrawal's stated reason was that a test asserted the opposite, and the agent's read is correct: that was deference to a test *name* which encoded the defect. Overrule accepted.\n\nBut its defence of that overrule doesn't hold, and I verified rather than accepted it. It claimed the old general property \"survives in\" two other tests, and that both exist and pass. Both true — and together misleading. Those two assert overlay preservation for a **degraded inventory** and a **membership race**. Neither involves a bound breach. I swept every overlay-preservation assertion across the three relevant test files: none covers `memoryErrInputTooLarge`. The replacement it added tests the classifier's *boolean*, not that the build declines to publish.\n\nSo the behaviour change is right; the guard for the remaining case lapsed. That's precisely what the recorded invariant was about — and the withdrawal's *coverage* concern was real even though its reasoning wasn't. Sent back for one behavioural test, with instructions to prove it by weakening the publish path.\n\n\"The property survives in X and Y\" is the easiest claim to wave through, because X and Y do exist and do pass. The error class they exercise is the part that matters.\n\n#489 and #477 still running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":296047,"output_tokens":634,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":296047,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e3312bce-25be-4079-ab97-d251defac823","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNM94ESq76QMaiFRS1vA","requestRef":"5f55a6d6-7351-470a-8797-a7c1a33c49c6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"733f35e9-2a5e-4552-b056-7d14c8e96fc0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:46:37.194Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
