{"parentUuid":"01f8a1e0-84a4-4e60-ae8b-55978cf8198f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNNYyagQ1AY62NLyrCSy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The caller only propagates, so no current `errors.Is` breaks — but the identity loss compounds the very bug being fixed. Sending that to the #489 agent:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":520,"cache_read_input_tokens":311769,"output_tokens":1230,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":363},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":520,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1230,"cache_read_input_tokens":311769,"cache_creation_input_tokens":520,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":520},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5316493e-d5ff-455c-b2d2-0faa01dd3bd2","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNNYyFqes4X7XGWNp8Bx","requestRef":"4f7f125e-e88f-4b0d-9f0b-029aebc93b05","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"fcd28c70-791d-4c12-b074-a7e242d33e29","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:05:05.745Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"fcd28c70-791d-4c12-b074-a7e242d33e29","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNNYyagQ1AY62NLyrCSy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DJW8t5pf5mH7rSnCYLHopE","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"abf958ce8ef8f7ff3","summary":"Add error-identity requirement to 489","message":"Addition to your brief, from reading the current code on your branch — it strengthens the fix and is in scope.\n\nMy refactor flattened error identity, and that compounds the bug you are fixing. Two places:\n\n1. In `partitionLocalTranscriptSessions`, the unreadable-chunk case used to be\n   `fmt.Errorf(\"...: %w\", ..., err)` and is now `fmt.Sprintf(\"...: %v\", ..., err)` collected into a\n   []string. So the underlying git error's identity is gone.\n2. `validateLocalTranscriptSessions`, the thin all-or-nothing wrapper, then does\n   `errors.New(unavailable[0])` — a bare string. The message survives; `errors.Is` does not.\n\nWhy it matters for your finding specifically: if the object probe fails because the context was\ncancelled, the OLD code propagated something an upstream `errors.Is(err, context.Canceled)` could\nstill match. Flattened to a string, a cancellation is indistinguishable from any other failure\nupstream — which is the same conflation you are removing one layer down. Fixing the classification\nwhile leaving the identity flattened would only move the problem.\n\nSo: when you return a runner/context failure as an error rather than as \"unavailable\", preserve\nits identity with `%w` so cancellation and timeout remain matchable upstream. Check whether the\nall-or-nothing wrapper can keep identity too; if the []string design makes that impossible, say so\nand propose the smallest change that keeps it (for example carrying the error alongside the\nmessage rather than formatting it in).\n\nGuard it: a test asserting `errors.Is(err, context.Canceled)` holds through\n`partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` when the probe is cancelled. Then weaken by swapping that `%w`\nfor `%v` and confirm you see `--- FAIL: <your test>` — that is a one-character weakening, exactly\nthe kind worth having.\n\nOne correction to something I may have implied: I have NOT seen a push from you. db2d4ff9 is my own\nearlier commit, not yours. Nothing is lost — just don't assume I have reviewed anything of yours.","type":"message","recipient":"abf958ce8ef8f7ff3","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Addition to your brief, from reading the current …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":520,"cache_read_input_tokens":311769,"output_tokens":1230,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":363},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":520,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1230,"cache_read_input_tokens":311769,"cache_creation_input_tokens":520,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":520},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DJW8t5pf5mH7rSnCYLHopE":{"to":"abf958ce8ef8f7ff3","summary":"Add error-identity requirement to 489","message":"Addition to your brief, from reading the current code on your branch — it strengthens the fix and is in scope.\n\nMy refactor flattened error identity, and that compounds the bug you are fixing. Two places:\n\n1. In `partitionLocalTranscriptSessions`, the unreadable-chunk case used to be\n   `fmt.Errorf(\"...: %w\", ..., err)` and is now `fmt.Sprintf(\"...: %v\", ..., err)` collected into a\n   []string. So the underlying git error's identity is gone.\n2. `validateLocalTranscriptSessions`, the thin all-or-nothing wrapper, then does\n   `errors.New(unavailable[0])` — a bare string. The message survives; `errors.Is` does not.\n\nWhy it matters for your finding specifically: if the object probe fails because the context was\ncancelled, the OLD code propagated something an upstream `errors.Is(err, context.Canceled)` could\nstill match. Flattened to a string, a cancellation is indistinguishable from any other failure\nupstream — which is the same conflation you are removing one layer down. Fixing the classification\nwhile leaving the identity flattened would only move the problem.\n\nSo: when you return a runner/context failure as an error rather than as \"unavailable\", preserve\nits identity with `%w` so cancellation and timeout remain matchable upstream. Check whether the\nall-or-nothing wrapper can keep identity too; if the []string design makes that impossible, say so\nand propose the smallest change that keeps it (for example carrying the error alongside the\nmessage rather than formatting it in).\n\nGuard it: a test asserting `errors.Is(err, context.Canceled)` holds through\n`partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` when the probe is cancelled. Then weaken by swapping that `%w`\nfor `%v` and confirm you see `--- FAIL: <your test>` — that is a one-character weakening, exactly\nthe kind worth having.\n\nOne correction to something I may have implied: I have NOT seen a push from you. db2d4ff9 is my own\nearlier commit, not yours. Nothing is lost — just don't assume I have reviewed anything of yours."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5316493e-d5ff-455c-b2d2-0faa01dd3bd2","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgNNYyFqes4X7XGWNp8Bx","requestRef":"4f7f125e-e88f-4b0d-9f0b-029aebc93b05","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"2751fb12-f638-4404-871d-8a26660b46f9","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:05:16.720Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Us