{"parentUuid":"7e0b58f5-74f2-4a01-a413-08e0a7df0046","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNPdAMoW4Zb3u1HB1UvA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Test's own fixture is load-bearing — not lowering the ceiling turns it red, so it genuinely exercises the bound. **#483 is complete and verified.** Recording the contention finding, which generalizes beyond this PR:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1041,"cache_read_input_tokens":322530,"output_tokens":1319,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":283},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1041,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1319,"cache_read_input_tokens":322530,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1041},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"70af9c4c-b3c6-4b83-b942-7f58e8c5b214","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNPdA2i6RkbQueYj11Qa","requestRef":"adc640dc-d932-4d45-839f-0f4c6c375ac3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"264e479b-6349-4874-899e-86abc3bb3f6c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:19:07.805Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"264e479b-6349-4874-899e-86abc3bb3f6c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNPdAMoW4Zb3u1HB1UvA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WxMRBSQzQfzDwz8PPX7GFN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"M=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory; cat >> \"$M/macos-race-suite-at-timeout.md\" <<'EOF'\n\n**The local, non-race variant (2026-10-25).** `internal/cli` runs **232s idle** and **805s under\n6-way contention** — 3.5x, measured on the same commit. The package's default `go test` alarm is\n**10m**, so a prepush gate on correct code fails with `panic: test timed out after 10m0s` whenever\nseveral suites are live, and the panic names whichever test happened to be running at the alarm\n(in one case a test that had been going 2 seconds). That reads exactly like a flaky test in a file\nyou just touched.\n\n**Why:** three parallel agents each running the gate is now a normal state here, so this is not an\nedge case. Twice in one session a red gate was contention, not the diff — and the second time the\nagent correctly refused to blame its own change and went looking at `ps` instead.\n\n**How to apply:** before believing a `test timed out` red, run `ps` for other `cli.test` binaries\nand check their elapsed times. Re-run with `GOFLAGS=-timeout=30m` rather than editing the gate\nscript. Quote the idle duration beside the contended one whenever reporting a timing. Related:\n[[cpu-and-bridge-discipline]], [[load-pressure-is-an-arm-confound]].\nEOF\nS=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/b7.json\" <<'JSON'\n[{\"id\":\"finding-483-delta-path\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"done\",\n  \"title\":\"#483 DONE+VERIFIED (201fe6eb): delta skips an oversize transcript into FailedFiles; the coverage gap I returned is closed with a REAL ceiling (bounded tombstone read), not a seam. I re-ran all 3 guards + weakened the test's OWN fixture -> red, so it keys on the ceiling\"},\n {\"id\":\"cli-suite-timeout-under-contention\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"done\",\n  \"title\":\"MEASURED: internal/cli is 232s idle vs 805s under 6-way contention (3.5x) and the default go-test alarm is 10m - so a correct diff fails the gate and the panic names whatever test was running. Use GOFLAGS=-timeout=30m, never edit the gate script\"}]\nJSON\npython3 \"$S/board_update.py\" \"$S/b7.json\"","description":"Record the timeout finding and close 483"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1041,"cache_read_input_tokens":322530,"output_tokens":1319,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":283},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1041,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1319,"cache_read_input_tokens":322530,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1041},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WxMRBSQzQfzDwz8PPX7GFN":{"command":"M=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory; cat >> \"$M/macos-race-suite-at-timeout.md\" <<'EOF'\n\n**The local, non-race variant (2026-10-25).** `internal/cli` runs **232s idle** and **805s under\n6-way contention** — 3.5x, measured on the same commit. The package's default `go test` alarm is\n**10m**, so a prepush gate on correct code fails with `panic: test timed out after 10m0s` whenever\nseveral suites are live, and the panic names whichever test happened to be running at the alarm\n(in one case a test that had been going 2 seconds). That reads exactly like a flaky test in a file\nyou just touched.\n\n**Why:** three parallel agents each running the gate is now a normal state here, so this is not an\nedge case. Twice in one session a red gate was contention, not the diff — and the second time the\nagent correctly refused to blame its own change and went looking at `ps` instead.\n\n**How to apply:** before believing a `test timed out` red, run `ps` for other `cli.test` binaries\nand check their elapsed times. Re-run with `GOFLAGS=-timeout=30m` rather than editing the gate\nscript. Quote the idle duration beside the contended one whenever reporting a timing. Related:\n[[cpu-and-bridge-discipline]], [[load-pressure-is-an-arm-confound]].\nEOF\nS=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/b7.json\" <<'JSON'\n[{\"id\":\"finding-483-delta-path\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"done\",\n  \"title\":\"#483 DONE+VERIFIED (201fe6eb): delta skips an oversize transcript into FailedFiles; the coverage gap I returned is closed with a REAL ceiling (bounded tombstone read), not a seam. I re-ran all 3 guards + weakened the test's OWN fixture -> red, so it keys on the ceiling\"},\n {\"id\":\"cli-suite-timeout-under-contention\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"done\",\n  \"title\":\"MEASURED: internal/cli is 232s idle vs 805s under 6-way contention (3.5x) and the default go-test alarm is 10m - so a correct diff fails the gate and the panic names whatever test was running. Use GOFLAGS=-timeout=30m, never edit the gate script\"}]\nJSON\npython3 \"$S/board_update.py\" \"$S/b7.json\"","description":"Record the timeout finding and close 483"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"70af9c4c-b3c6-4b83-b942-7f58e8c5b214","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgNPdA2i6RkbQueYj11Qa","requestRef":"adc640dc-d932-4d45-839f-0f4c6c375ac3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f5fb53e-ce32-4593-8f9d-3688e36fae9