{"parentUuid":"05ddb0b1-0757-49ce-bee7-895c872b512c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNPug3C5PDzjk1fcev5r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014QHMPk3UrAYaJ3bZEeuv4K","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach; git add internal/cli/mcp_reachability_test.go && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest(doctor): make the cap's position load-bearing, not just its presence\n\nThe oversize cases announced 4 MiB + 1 and 16 MiB. Both are refused identically\nwhether the cap is checked before or after the allocation, because 16 MiB\nallocates harmlessly -- so moving `make` above the cap check left this test and\nthe probe's end-to-end test green while restoring exactly the multi-GB\nallocation the finding was about. The tests proved the error, and the one named\nfor not allocating proved nothing about not allocating.\n\nAdding math.MaxInt fixes that: it cannot be allocated on any platform, so\nreaching `make` panics with \"makeslice: len out of range\" and the test goes\nred. Verified by re-running that reordering weakening, which was green before\nthis and is red after.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1; git push -q origin feat/mcp-surface-reachable && echo pushed","description":"Commit and push the ordering guard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_read_input_tokens":339124,"output_tokens":433,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":339124,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014QHMPk3UrAYaJ3bZEeuv4K":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach; git add internal/cli/mcp_reachability_test.go && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest(doctor): make the cap's position load-bearing, not just its presence\n\nThe oversize cases announced 4 MiB + 1 and 16 MiB. Both are refused identically\nwhether the cap is checked before or after the allocation, because 16 MiB\nallocates harmlessly -- so moving `make` above the cap check left this test and\nthe probe's end-to-end test green while restoring exactly the multi-GB\nallocation the finding was about. The tests proved the error, and the one named\nfor not allocating proved nothing about not allocating.\n\nAdding math.MaxInt fixes that: it cannot be allocated on any platform, so\nreaching `make` panics with \"makeslice: len out of range\" and the test goes\nred. Verified by re-running that reordering weakening, which was green before\nthis and is red after.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1; git push -q origin feat/mcp-surface-reachable && echo pushed","description":"Commit and push the ordering guard"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2eecdfc8-711d-4d48-b145-4adbc33bbf68","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNPufgcCTLQvDzSsaB6p","requestRef":"8c4a51b0-51d5-4672-bdcb-7c4e0c87ccb7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"669be238-7577-4f76-a53c-6f93b727d227","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:22:52.699Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
