{"parentUuid":"6fd89210-d8f1-4b96-84a0-28608bc444e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNQge68CkU1yCwbVY8Ln","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the material finding from the skeptic pass, and it needs stating precisely.\n\nThe threshold is `usable == 0 && unavailable > 0` → refuse; otherwise warn and publish. **There is no partial-shrink guard.** Combined with the promisor behaviour, on a partial clone under no-egress a recoverable-but-unfetched blob reads as confirmed-gone, so a previously larger published corpus gets replaced by a smaller one with only a warning.\n\nThat configuration is live: earlier in this session, `cli`'s brain was stuck precisely because transcript/metadata blobs were promisor-absent — I fixed it by fetching 422 of them.\n\nRecording it rather than patching it, because the obvious fix is wrong:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":763,"cache_read_input_tokens":356056,"output_tokens":3125,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1697},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":763,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3125,"cache_read_input_tokens":356056,"cache_creation_input_tokens":763,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":763},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"871ef643-2637-4065-ad09-5efdf1b9ca85","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNQgdkn5DLCPoggEZcJd","requestRef":"a8460aa6-cd9b-4baa-9f81-63747b20e39c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"62d12855-6338-42b4-89ab-571e9fd85798","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:33:25.424Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"62d12855-6338-42b4-89ab-571e9fd85798","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNQge68CkU1yCwbVY8Ln","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015TaepCsz142W14XxXNJHhC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/fact3.txt\" <<'EOF'\nUnder no-egress on a PARTIAL (promisor) clone, \"absent locally\" is genuinely ambiguous between \"destroyed forever\" and \"not fetched yet\", and export cannot tell them apart without egress. localObjectMissingConfirmed runs cat-file -e through runCheckpointGitLocal, which sets GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1; measured on git 2.54.0, a promisor-absent but fetchable blob then exits 1 silent, identical to a pruned object that is gone for good. With lazy fetch allowed the same probe exits 0 because it fetches. PR #489 resolves the ambiguity toward \"gone\" and SKIPS the session; unavailableSessionsAreFatal refuses only when usable==0, so there is no partial-shrink guard and a previously larger published corpus can be replaced by a smaller one with only a warning. This configuration is live: cli's brain was frozen because transcript and metadata blobs were promisor-absent until 422 of them were fetched by hand. Do NOT \"fix\" this by treating an absent object as fetchable whenever a promisor remote exists: that re-breaks #489 exactly where it was needed, since cli IS a promisor clone and its squash-destroyed commits are unfetchable. And do NOT add a naive refuse-if-smaller guard: privacy exclude legitimately shrinks the corpus via tombstones, which is what PR #488 is about. A correct guard must exempt tombstoned sessions, so this is a design call, not a patch.\nEOF\nentire brain remember \"$(cat \"$S/fact3.txt\")\" --path architecture.export.constraint --branch main 2>&1 | tail -2; cat > \"$S/b8.json\" <<'JSON'\n[{\"id\":\"finding-489-transient-git\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"done\",\n  \"title\":\"#489 DONE+VERIFIED (ce563535): classifies missing by cat-file -e EXIT CODE (no stderr matching), 9 weakenings red, adopted my errors.Is/%w point ([]error not []string). I reproduced the exit codes on real git 2.54.0 myself\"},\n {\"id\":\"export-shrink-on-partial-clone\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"user\",\"status\":\"blocked\",\n  \"title\":\"DESIGN CALL from my skeptic pass on #489: under no-egress on a PROMISOR clone, a fetchable-but-unfetched blob exits 1 silent = indistinguishable from gone-forever, so #489 SKIPS it and there is no partial-shrink guard -> a larger published corpus can be replaced by a smaller one with only a warning. cli IS such a clone (422 blobs fetched by hand this session). Both obvious fixes are WRONG: promisor-means-fetchable re-breaks #489 where it was needed; refuse-if-smaller breaks privacy exclude (#488). Needs a tombstone-aware guard\"}]\nJSON\npython3 \"$S/board_update.py\" \"$S/b8.json\"","description":"Record the design finding"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":763,"cache_read_input_tokens":356056,"output_tokens":3125,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1697},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":763,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3125,"cache_read_input_tokens":356056,"cache_creation_input_tokens":763,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":763},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015TaepCsz142W14XxXNJHhC":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/fact3.txt\" <<'EOF'\nUnder no-egress on a PARTIAL (promisor) clone, \"absent locally\" is genuinely ambiguous between \"destroyed forever\" and \"not fetched yet\", and export cannot tell them apart without egress. localObjectMissingConfirmed runs cat-file -e through runCheckpointGitLocal, which sets GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1; measured on git 2.54.0, a promisor-absent but fetchable blob then exits 1 silent, identical to a pruned object that is gone for good. With lazy fetch allowed the same probe exits 0 because it fetches. PR #489 resolves the ambiguity toward \"gone\" and SKIPS the session; unavailableSessionsAreFatal refuses only when usable==0, so there is no partial-shrink guard and a previously larger published corpus can be replaced by a smaller one with only a warning. This configuration is live: cli's brain was frozen because transcript and metadata blobs were promisor-absent until 422 of them were fetched by hand. Do NOT \"fix\" this by treating an absent object as fetchable whenever a promisor remote exists: that re-breaks #489 exactly where it was needed, since cli IS a promisor clone and its squash-destroyed commits are unfetchable. And do NOT add a naive refuse-if-smaller guard: privacy exclude legitimately shrinks the corpus via tombstones, which is what PR #488 is about. A correct guard must exempt tombstoned sessions, so this is a design call, not a patch.\nEOF\nentire brain remember \"$(cat \"$S/fact3.txt\")\" --path architecture.export.constraint --branch main 2>&1 | tail -2; cat > \"$S/b8.json\" <<'JSON'\n[{\"id\":\"finding-489-transient-git\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"done\",\n  \"title\":\"#489 DONE+VERIFIED (ce563535): classifies missing by cat-file -e EXIT CODE (no stderr matching), 9 weakenings red, adopted my errors.Is/%w point ([]error not []string). I reproduced the exit codes on real git 2.54.0 myself\"},\n {\"id\":\"export-shrink-on-partial-clone\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"user\",\"status\":\"blocked\",\n  \"title\":\"DESIGN CALL from my skeptic pass on #489: under no-egress on a PROMISOR clone, a fetchable-but-unfetched blob exits 1 silent = indistinguishable from gone-forever, so #489 SKIPS it and there is no partial-shrink guard -> a larger published corpus can be replaced by a smaller one with only a warning. cli IS such a clone (422 blobs fetched by hand this session). Both obvious fixes are WRONG: promisor-means-fetchable re-breaks #489 where it was needed; refuse-if-smaller breaks privacy exclude (#488). Needs a tombstone-aware guard\"}]\nJSON\npython3 \"$S/board_update.py\" \"$S/b8.json\"","description":"Record the design finding"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"871ef643-2637-4065-ad09-5efdf1b9ca85","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgNQgdkn5DLCPoggEZcJd","requestRef":"a8460aa6-cd9b-4baa-9f81-63747b20e39c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"3cae568e-7871-468d-9f43-d770667e5556","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:33:39.169Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
