{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","id":"c68090aa-2408-4192-ab0c-e4290919b21e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:38:53.184Z","version":"2.1.310","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"24017389debf7cd8bde5028ecf29c4ee6405c6fe767d12c483cd96a0e96b3788","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","context-1m-2025-08-07","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":64000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"f53f709e-8fa2-4602-b0c6-4ef34f8f71f7","keep":626,"tail":["7f8883b28d314c6cf1ea3313b9f02b608bc0567b6cada9e804fbda1a5f3cd934","0c1591268679f583a09c671cddce123f2d5e8bd3f7d45df2a706917baba844ba","e3282014a678d1568a3feca4b5e7c7ca70acbb2d7374cf1aad85e48dea4f7bbe"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",628,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"8452e4b2b91293d9c99c2dcc4d37ebe3c32033aeb99946a8e4bebc8dcdc078a1"}
{"parentUuid":"11aa59da-e1b7-40f5-b7ee-67df7efc286b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14340994 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"224bd2c1-7f9b-4083-b92f-6547de1e4876","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:38:53.143Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14340994 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"224bd2c1-7f9b-4083-b92f-6547de1e4876","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNR8xZqrpn74jVZvs8NA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015yP7xcSgBpNBAaKog9hTcd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv; python3 - <<'PY'\np=\"DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md\"; s=open(p).read()\nadd = '''\n## 7. Shrinking republish on a partial clone — the one real design call from the findings round (2026-10-25)\n\nFound by my own skeptic pass on **#489**, not by the review. #489 is still a clear\nimprovement on what it replaced, so this does not hold it — but it needs your call.\n\n**The measurement.** `#489` decides \"this object is gone\" from `git cat-file -e`'s exit\ncode, which I reproduced on real git 2.54.0: present = 0, resolved-but-absent = 1 silent,\nunresolvable = 128. Sound. But the probe runs under `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1`, and on a\n**promisor partial clone** a blob that is merely *not fetched yet* also exits **1 silent** —\nbyte-identical to one destroyed forever. With lazy fetch allowed the same probe exits 0,\nbecause it fetches.\n\nSo under no-egress on a partial clone, \"absent\" is genuinely ambiguous and the code\n**cannot** tell the two apart without egress. #489 resolves it toward \"gone\" and skips the\nsession; `unavailableSessionsAreFatal` refuses only when *nothing* is servable. There is no\npartial-shrink guard, so a previously larger published corpus can be replaced by a smaller\none with only a warning.\n\n**This configuration is live.** `cli`'s brain was frozen for ten days precisely because\ntranscript and metadata blobs were promisor-absent; I unfroze it by fetching 422 of them by\nhand. Same promisor shape as graph #372.\n\n**Why I did not just fix it.** Both obvious fixes are wrong, and I checked both:\n- *\"a promisor remote exists, so absent might be fetchable → refuse\"* re-breaks #489 exactly\n  where it was needed: `cli` IS a promisor clone, and its squash-destroyed commits are\n  unfetchable anywhere.\n- *\"refuse if the new corpus is smaller\"* breaks `privacy exclude`, which legitimately\n  shrinks via tombstones — that is what **#488** does. It would also break #489's own\n  purpose, since genuinely destroyed sessions legitimately shrink the corpus too.\n\n**The actual question, which is a CLI-contract call and therefore yours:** should an export\nthat would drop previously-published sessions require explicit opt-in (a flag / a prompt),\nor keep publishing with a warning? That changes the command's contract, which is why I am\nnot deciding it. Recorded in brain at `architecture.export.constraint`.\n\n## 8. `internal/cli`'s prepush gate cannot pass under load (not a decision, a heads-up)\n\nMeasured independently by two agents and me: `internal/cli` runs **232s idle** and\n**805–855s under contention**, against `go test`'s **10m default**, which `test:prepush`\nnever raises (CI uses `-timeout 20m` in nightly/release). Under parallel load the gate fails\non correct code, and the panic names whichever test happened to be running at the alarm — it\nreads exactly like a flake in the file you just touched. Workaround is\n`GOFLAGS=-timeout=30m`; the real fix is a `-timeout` in the task, which I have not changed\nbecause it is your gate script.\n'''\nif \"## 7. Shrinking republish\" not in s:\n    s = s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + add\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"appended sections 7 and 8\")\nPY\nrtk proxy grep -n \"^## \" DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md | tail -4","description":"Append the new decisions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_read_input_tokens":382318,"output_tokens":1306,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1306,"cache_read_input_tokens":382318,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015yP7xcSgBpNBAaKog9hTcd":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv; python3 - <<'PY'\np=\"DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md\"; s=open(p).read()\nadd = '''\n## 7. Shrinking republish on a partial clone — the one real design call from the findings round (2026-10-25)\n\nFound by my own skeptic pass on **#489**, not by the review. #489 is still a clear\nimprovement on what it replaced, so this does not hold it — but it needs your call.\n\n**The measurement.** `#489` decides \"this object is gone\" from `git cat-file -e`'s exit\ncode, which I reproduced on real git 2.54.0: present = 0, resolved-but-absent = 1 silent,\nunresolvable = 128. Sound. But the probe runs under `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1`, and on a\n**promisor partial clone** a blob that is merely *not fetched yet* also exits **1 silent** —\nbyte-identical to one destroyed forever. With lazy fetch allowed the same probe exits 0,\nbecause it fetches.\n\nSo under no-egress on a partial clone, \"absent\" is genuinely ambiguous and the code\n**cannot** tell the two apart without egress. #489 resolves it toward \"gone\" and skips the\nsession; `unavailableSessionsAreFatal` refuses only when *nothing* is servable. There is no\npartial-shrink guard, so a previously larger published corpus can be replaced by a smaller\none with only a warning.\n\n**This configuration is live.** `cli`'s brain was frozen for ten days precisely because\ntranscript and metadata blobs were promisor-absent; I unfroze it by fetching 422 of them by\nhand. Same promisor shape as graph #372.\n\n**Why I did not just fix it.** Both obvious fixes are wrong, and I checked both:\n- *\"a promisor remote exists, so absent might be fetchable → refuse\"* re-breaks #489 exactly\n  where it was needed: `cli` IS a promisor clone, and its squash-destroyed commits are\n  unfetchable anywhere.\n- *\"refuse if the new corpus is smaller\"* breaks `privacy exclude`, which legitimately\n  shrinks via tombstones — that is what **#488** does. It would also break #489's own\n  purpose, since genuinely destroyed sessions legitimately shrink the corpus too.\n\n**The actual question, which is a CLI-contract call and therefore yours:** should an export\nthat would drop previously-published sessions require explicit opt-in (a flag / a prompt),\nor keep publishing with a warning? That changes the command's contract, which is why I am\nnot deciding it. Recorded in brain at `architecture.export.constraint`.\n\n## 8. `internal/cli`'s prepush gate cannot pass under load (not a decision, a heads-up)\n\nMeasured independently by two agents and me: `internal/cli` runs **232s idle** and\n**805–855s under contention**, against `go test`'s **10m default**, which `test:prepush`\nnever raises (CI uses `-timeout 20m` in nightly/release). Under parallel load the gate fails\non correct code, and the panic names whichever test happened to be running at the alarm — it\nreads exactly like a flake in the file you just touched. Workaround is\n`GOFLAGS=-timeout=30m`; the real fix is a `-timeout` in the task, which I have not changed\nbecause it is your gate script.\n'''\nif \"## 7. Shrinking republish\" not in s:\n    s = s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + add\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"appended sections 7 and 8\")\nPY\nrtk proxy grep -n \"^## \" DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md | tail -4","description":"Append the new decisions"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ec5667f0-60a7-4dcb-9179-55af6162edf5","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNR8xDG4nbQgt996QDUU","requestRef":"c68090aa-2408-4192-ab0c-e4290919b21e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"4a7e2233-045a-4ef9-b7