{"parentUuid":"71accce9-4c6e-4aed-bcd1-e9c0d0a42731","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14324481 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3d406ed1-66d7-49c0-8f4a-44cdf817c633","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:44:21.896Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14324481 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"3d406ed1-66d7-49c0-8f4a-44cdf817c633","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNRZC57bJ5VF9sSt3oDu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R1EfdYdwCTwvpRy8bZFfZz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/integ-pr-body.md\" <<'EOF'\n## DO NOT MERGE\n\nThis is a verification branch, not a change. It exists so CI runs the **combined** tree of\nall thirteen open brain PRs in their intended merge order. It should be closed, never merged;\nthe thirteen PRs merge individually.\n\n## Why it exists\n\nEach of the thirteen was green on its own, and each merged cleanly against `main`\n**pairwise**. That is not the same as being safe to land in sequence: merging one changes\n`main` for the next, and a semantic break needs no textual conflict at all. The\nentire-graph session hit exactly that on its own integration branch — a test asserting a\nfile another PR had deliberately stopped writing. Nothing in a per-PR gate can see it.\n\nUpstream drift proved the point again while this was being prepared: `#490`\n(workspace extraction) and `#491` landed on `main` mid-session, and `#473` — clean two hours\nearlier — began conflicting in `internal/cli/workspace.go`.\n\n## Merge order\n\nTwo hard constraints, both literal git ancestry; everything else is independent:\n\n```\n#479 → #481          (479 is an ancestor of 481)\n#488 → #489          (488 is an ancestor of 489)\n```\n\nOrder used here:\n\n| | PR | |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | #473 | fix(watch) per-sweep attribution |\n| 2 | #476 | perf(history) normalize once per call |\n| 3 | #482 | fix(setup) every agent's hook config exempt from the first-run gate |\n| 4 | #478 | perf(patterns) per-branch fact freshness |\n| 5 | #474 | fix(export) one divergent cached transcript must not refuse the run |\n| 6 | #480 | fix(export) say \"all\" in a way the host honours |\n| 7 | #479 | perf(export) routed checkpoint details concurrently |\n| 8 | #481 | perf(export) checkpoint metadata from the local store |\n| 9 | #488 | fix(export) an excluded session must not block the export |\n| 10 | #489 | fix(export) a checkpoint whose commit no longer exists |\n| 11 | #477 | feat(doctor) prove the MCP tool surface is reachable |\n| 12 | #483 | fix(history) one oversize transcript must not refuse the index |\n| 13 | #484 | feat(brief) carry graph's ancestor staleness |\n\nSix of these touch `internal/cli/export.go` (#474, #479, #480, #481, #488, #489), which is\nwhy the sequence matters rather than the set.\n\n## Result\n\nAll thirteen merge clean in that order against `main@20eb1207`. Locally on the combined tree:\n\n- `go test ./... -count=1` — exit 0, **19 packages ok**, 3 with no test files, 22 of 22\n  accounted for, zero `--- FAIL`\n- `gofmt -l -s .` — no output\n- `go vet ./...` — exit 0\n\nThree branches needed `main` merged in first, each a mechanical collision with COR-2268's\nextractions, each re-proved by weakening rather than assumed green:\n\n- **#473** `workspace.go` — `loadWorkspaceManifest` is gone; resolved to keep `pass++` and\n  take the manifest from `workspaceStore(...).LoadManifest`. Deleting `pass++` turns\n  `TestWorkspaceWatchStampsEveryLineWithClockAndRepo` red, so the attribution this PR exists\n  for is still load-bearing.\n- **#477** `lifecycle_ops.go` — `resolveLocalTargetRepoDir` moved to `internal/base`.\n- **#483** `history.go` — the read bounds and the size-refusal error moved to\n  `internal/base` and were exported.\n\n## What this run does NOT cover\n\n`-race` and Windows, which is the point of pushing it: CI owns both, and no local run in this\nsession could reach them. The 10m default `go test` alarm is also worth knowing about here —\n`internal/cli` is 232s idle but 805–855s under parallel load, and `test:prepush` passes no\n`-timeout` while CI uses 20m.\nEOF\ngh pr create --repo entireio/entire-brain --draft --base main --head integration/brain-13-do-not-merge --title \"DO NOT MERGE: CI run of all 13 open brain PRs combined, in merge order\" --body-file \"$S/integ-pr-body.md\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open the draft integration PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":652,"cache_read_input_tokens":399592,"output_tokens":1654,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":652,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1654,"cache_read_input_tokens":399592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":652,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":652},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01R1EfdYdwCTwvpRy8bZFfZz":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/integ-pr-body.md\" <<'EOF'\n## DO NOT MERGE\n\nThis is a verification branch, not a change. It exists so CI runs the **combined** tree of\nall thirteen open brain PRs in their intended merge order. It should be closed, never merged;\nthe thirteen PRs merge individually.\n\n## Why it exists\n\nEach of the thirteen was green on its own, and each merged cleanly against `main`\n**pairwise**. That is not the same as being safe to land in sequence: merging one changes\n`main` for the next, and a semantic break needs no textual conflict at all. The\nentire-graph session hit exactly that on its own integration branch — a test asserting a\nfile another PR had deliberately stopped w