{"parentUuid":"d663c5c6-ce33-4cd3-942e-f136236f1079","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b37bbc2a-8b7b-416c-9761-9c5f45ea7d0e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G5a9X9zyMnxq4Y3FsHuykV","type":"tool_result","content":"=== localObjectType + sentinel area ===\nfunc catFileBatchType(ctx context.Context, gitDir, spec string, localOnly bool) (string, error) {\n\t_, objType, err := catFileBatchRequest(ctx, gitDir, spec, localOnly, true)\n\treturn objType, err\n}\n\n// localObjectType answers `git cat-file -t` under the local-only policy,\n// batched for batch-capable runners and per-exec for every other runner.\n// A batch \"missing\" answer is definitive; other batch errors fall back.\n//\n// Either path reports a definitively absent object as errGitObjectMissing and\n// everything else as a plain error, so a caller can tell git's ANSWER from a\n// failure to ask it. partitionLocalTranscriptSessions depends on exactly that\n// distinction: it skips a session on the former and refuses the export on the\n=== imports of git_catfile_batch.go ===\npackage cli\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"runtime\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// git_catfile_batch.go routes repeated object reads through one long-lived\n// `git cat-file --batch` child per (gitDir, policy) instead of one `git\n// cat-file` exec per blob. A cold export/distill on a ~1,000-checkpoint repo\n// spawned ~5,000 git processes at ~30ms each (COR-2182); the same reads","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"20804f94-9cb4-4cd9-874b-79f407ae2c0d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:47:10.175Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== localObjectType + sentinel area ===\nfunc catFileBatchType(ctx context.Context, gitDir, spec string, localOnly bool) (string, error) {\n\t_, objType, err := catFileBatchRequest(ctx, gitDir, spec, localOnly, true)\n\treturn objType, err\n}\n\n// localObjectType answers `git cat-file -t` under the local-only policy,\n// batched for batch-capable runners and per-exec for every other runner.\n// A batch \"missing\" answer is definitive; other batch errors fall back.\n//\n// Either path reports a definitively absent object as errGitObjectMissing and\n// everything else as a plain error, so a caller can tell git's ANSWER from a\n// failure to ask it. partitionLocalTranscriptSessions depends on exactly that\n// distinction: it skips a session on the former and refuses the export on the\n=== imports of git_catfile_batch.go ===\npackage cli\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"runtime\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// git_catfile_batch.go routes repeated object reads through one long-lived\n// `git cat-file --batch` child per (gitDir, policy) instead of one `git\n// cat-file` exec per blob. A cold export/distill on a ~1,000-checkpoint repo\n// spawned ~5,000 git processes at ~30ms each (COR-2182); the same reads","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8af17c19-3d9c-4e2a-be64-87f998751dbc","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","branch":"fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","r