{"parentUuid":"c4131c9f-29a1-4e21-81d6-460d6a2c6730","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNS244ApD32WfRcDsQgF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":873,"cache_read_input_tokens":428766,"output_tokens":1204,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":118},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":873,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1204,"cache_read_input_tokens":428766,"cache_creation_input_tokens":873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":873},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1902,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"976e2c5d-c1cc-4d44-9d15-a76b7a5c0b50","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNS23jpQoSKT4n5TykV3","requestRef":"358dff7e-61eb-41a6-8ce2-d86d662eb172","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"727c9c57-34ca-42ba-a084-1104a18ea553","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:50:29.405Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"727c9c57-34ca-42ba-a084-1104a18ea553","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNS244ApD32WfRcDsQgF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CsecYPX6cm3VppCDnr7v9S","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"489 head changing; closed the shrink hole","message":"Heads-up before you freeze the page: #489 is getting one more commit, and the shrink item moves OFF the decisions table. I was wrong that it needed a product decision.\n\nWHAT I GOT WRONG. I told you a tombstone-aware guard was needed and that the two obvious fixes were both wrong. The second half holds; the first was based on a mistake. I claimed \"promisor remote exists, so absent might be fetchable → refuse\" would re-break #489 where it was needed. It does not, because the two cases take DIFFERENT paths through the partition:\n\n  - a checkpoint whose COMMIT was destroyed has no snapshot entry and no chunks, so it is\n    classified from DATA (`!ok || len(chunks) == 0`) and never reaches git at all. That is\n    #489's actual target case.\n  - the git probe only ever sees a chunk the snapshot DOES name whose bytes are absent\n    locally. That is precisely the fetchable case.\n\nSo tightening the probe branch costs #489 nothing. The agent's own report had the clue and I underweighted it: its vanished-checkpoint fixture \"never reaches the git probe at all\".\n\nTHE FIX, now on the branch: in the confirmed-missing branch, if the source repository has a promisor remote, the absence is not definitive and the export fails instead of dropping the session. A full clone is unaffected — absent there is absent for good, and it still partitions.\n\nDetection is one local config read, `config --get-regexp \\.promisor$`, matched by SUFFIX across every remote. That detail matters and is the reason I pinned it against real git: cli's checkpoint repository names its promisor remote by URL (remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git.promisor) and does NOT set extensions.partialclone, so a detector written against remote.origin.promisor or against that extension would pass every fake-runner test and miss the only repository the guard exists for. I verified both facts on cli's real config.\n\nFour weakenings, each a real `--- FAIL` and not a build failure:\n  - drop the promisor condition  -> RED on the partial-clone test\n  - detector always true         -> RED on the full-clone test AND on the agent's #489 test\n                                    (so the guard is provably narrow)\n  - pattern narrowed to origin   -> RED on the real-git url-named subtest, while the\n                                    fake-runner tests stay GREEN. That is the point: the\n                                    fakes could not have caught it.\n\nTwo consequences for your page:\n1. #489's head changes once the gate passes. I will send the SHA.\n2. #493 then holds a stale #489. I will re-push the integration branch and re-run its suite.\n3. DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md §7 stops being a decision. I will rewrite it as \"closed, here is what\n   it was\", so the combined table should drop that row rather than carry it to Suhaan.\n\nNothing in your lane is affected.","type":"message","recipient":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Heads-up before you freeze the page: #489 is gett…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":873,"cache_read_input_tokens":428766,"output_tokens":1204,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":118},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":873,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1204,"cache_read_input_tokens":428766,"cache_creation_input_tokens":873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":873},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CsecYPX6cm3VppCDnr7v9S":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"489 head changing; closed the shrink hole","message":"Heads-up before you freeze the page: #489 is getting one more commit, and the shrink item moves OFF the decisions table. I was wrong that it needed a product decision.\n\nWHAT I GOT WRONG. I told you a tombstone-aware guard was needed and that the two obvious fixes were both wrong. The second half holds; the first was based on a mistake. I claimed \"promisor remote exists, so absent might be fetchable → refuse\" would re-break #489 where it was needed. It does not, because the two cases take DIFFERENT paths through the partition:\n\n  - a checkpoint whose COMMIT was destroyed has no snapshot entry and no chunks, so it is\n    classified from DATA (`!ok || len(chunks) == 0`) and never reaches git at all. That is\n    #489's actual target case.\n  - the git probe only ever sees a chunk the snapshot DOES name whose bytes are absent\n    locally. That is precisely the fetchable case.\n\nSo tightening the probe branch costs #489 nothing. The agent's own report had the clue and I underweighted it: its vanished-checkpoint fixture \"never reaches the git probe at all\".\n\nTHE FIX, now on the branch: in the confirmed-missing branch, if the source repository has a promisor remote, the absence is not definitive and the export fails instead of dropping the session. A full clone is unaffected — absent there is absent for good, and it still partitions.\n\nDetection is one local config read, `config --get-regexp \\.promisor$`, matched by SUFFIX across every remote. That detail matters and is the reason I pinned it against real git: cli's checkpoint repository names its promisor remote by URL (remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git.promisor) and does NOT set extensions.partialclone, so a detector written against remote.origin.promisor or against that extension would pass every fake-runner test and miss the only repository the guard exists for. I verified both facts on cli's real config.\n\nFour weakenings, each a real `--- FAIL` and not a build failure:\n  - drop the promisor condition  -> RED on the partial-clone test\n  - detector always true         -> RED on the full-clone test AND on the agent's #489 test\n                                    (so the guard is provably narrow)\n  - pattern narrowed to origin   -> RED on the real-git url-named subtest, while the\n                                    fake-runner tests stay GREEN. That is the point: the\n                                    fakes could not have caught it.\n\nTwo consequences for your page:\n1. #489's head changes once the gate passes. I will send the SHA.\n2. #493 then holds a stale #489. I will re-push the integration branch and re-run its suite.\n3. DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md §7 stops being a decision. I will rewrite it as \"closed, here is what\n   it was\", so the combined table should drop that row rather than carry it to Suhaan.\n\nNothing in your lane is affected."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"976e2c5d-c1cc-4d44-9d15-a76b7a5c0b50","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNS23jpQoSKT4n5TykV3","requestRef":"358dff7e-61eb-41a6-8ce2-d86d662eb172","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"0dc24800-ede0-4894-bec8-a8f10b263224","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:50:44.552Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
