{"parentUuid":"4ea0d3bd-cd65-4507-a9af-c26d672ea1a7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNS5raiSBbtAVkRNTftr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Gate still on `internal/cli`. Meanwhile, rewriting §7 from a decision you owe me into a closed item:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":398,"cache_read_input_tokens":432229,"output_tokens":1270,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":72},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":398,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1270,"cache_read_input_tokens":432229,"cache_creation_input_tokens":398,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":398},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0d6ed6b4-55af-4bb8-ac0d-4f39c8802d1d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNS5rE8te43YhGkTSk4C","requestRef":"7fc2723e-7d76-4a12-9c2f-f365b906e37d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"56a05b31-6f72-49ab-a9d1-1a70722b4f83","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:51:20.987Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"56a05b31-6f72-49ab-a9d1-1a70722b4f83","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNS5raiSBbtAVkRNTftr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RHVNGXBVwa8PwFJiUvB8R1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv; python3 - <<'PY'\np=\"DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md\"; s=open(p).read()\nstart = s.index(\"## 7. Shrinking republish on a partial clone\")\nend = s.index(\"## 8. `internal/cli`'s prepush gate\")\nnew7 = '''## 7. ~~Shrinking republish on a partial clone~~ — CLOSED, no decision needed (2026-10-25)\n\n**I put this on your list and then took it off. It is fixed; nothing here needs you.**\nKept for the record because the reasoning is worth having.\n\n**The hole.** `#489` decides \"this object is gone\" from `git cat-file -e`'s exit code\n(reproduced on git 2.54.0: present 0, resolved-but-absent 1 silent, unresolvable 128). But\nthe probe runs under `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1`, and in a **partial clone** a blob that is merely\n*unfetched* also exits 1 silent — identical to one destroyed forever. #489 skipped the\nsession, and `unavailableSessionsAreFatal` refuses only when *nothing* is servable, so a\nlarger published corpus could be replaced by a smaller one with just a warning. Live risk:\n`cli`'s brain was frozen for ten days on exactly this, and I unfroze it by fetching 422\nblobs by hand.\n\n**Why I first called it a product decision, and why that was wrong.** I believed the obvious\nfix — \"a promisor remote exists, so absent might be fetchable → refuse\" — would re-break\n#489 exactly where it was needed. It does not. The two cases take different paths:\n\n- a checkpoint whose **commit** was destroyed has no snapshot entry and no chunks, so it is\n  classified **from data** and never reaches git. That is #489's actual target case.\n- the git probe only ever sees a chunk the snapshot **does** name whose bytes are absent\n  locally — precisely the fetchable case.\n\nSo tightening the probe branch costs #489 nothing, and no CLI-contract change is required.\n\n**The fix.** In the confirmed-missing branch, if the source repository has a promisor remote\nthe absence is not definitive and the export **fails** instead of dropping the session. Full\nclones are unaffected: absent there is absent for good, and they still partition.\n\n**The detail worth keeping.** Detection is one local config read matched by **suffix** across\nevery remote (`config --get-regexp \\\\.promisor$`), because `cli`'s checkpoint repository names\nits promisor remote by URL — `remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git.promisor`\n— and does **not** set `extensions.partialclone`. A detector written against\n`remote.origin.promisor` or that extension passes every fake-runner test and misses the only\nrepository the guard exists for. Pinned against real git for that reason: narrowing the\npattern to `origin` turns the real-git test red while the fake-runner tests stay green.\n\n'''\ns = s[:start] + new7 + s[end:]\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"section 7 rewritten as closed\")\nPY\nrtk proxy grep -n \"^## \" DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md | tail -3","description":"Rewrite section 7 as closed"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":398,"cache_read_input_tokens":432229,"output_tokens":1270,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":72},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":398,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1270,"cache_read_input_tokens":432229,"cache_creation_input_tokens":398,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":398},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_manag