{"parentUuid":"7f848cbc-ea01-498d-b087-1391dfda5fc6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNSRU1hhk8qPavAyLTRH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XfY12b5TV44hfFSzZEEuQ4","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Merge main into 478","model":"sonnet","prompt":"Resolve ONE mechanical merge conflict on an open PR. Work ONLY in the worktree holding branch `perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint` (PR entireio/entire-brain#478) — find it with `git worktree list` from /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished and `cd` there. Touch no other repo or worktree. Do NOT merge to main, do NOT open a PR, do NOT request review, do NOT rebase.\n\nTASK: `git fetch origin main` then `git merge origin/main`. It conflicts in `internal/cli/pattern_corpus.go`.\n\nWHY, so you resolve it correctly: main is taking a refactor series (COR-2268) that EXTRACTS code into subpackages and deletes the old unqualified helpers. The newest is commit 4cfff3ce \"refactor(cli): extract pattern candidates and dossiers\". Earlier ones moved things into `internal/cli/internal/base` and `internal/cli/workspace`. So the conflict is almost certainly: your branch's logic on one side, the same code calling a newly-extracted package on the other.\n\nTHE RULE: keep THIS BRANCH'S behaviour, adopt MAIN'S names and call shapes. If a helper your side calls no longer exists on main, find what replaced it (`git grep -n \"<name>\" origin/main -- internal/cli/` and look in the new subpackage) and call that instead. Never resolve by taking main's side wholesale — that silently deletes this PR's feature, which is what this PR exists for. #478's subject is \"perf(patterns): scope fact freshness per branch\", so per-branch fact-freshness scoping MUST survive.\n\nNote `go build ./...` does NOT compile test files. Use `go vet ./internal/cli/` to catch broken test references, and expect to follow the same rename in `*_test.go`. Check an import alias before inventing one: a file may already import the new package under a local alias.\n\nVERIFY, in order:\n1. `go vet ./internal/cli/` exits 0. Capture its status directly — `go vet ... | head` reports head's status, not vet's, which has bitten me twice today.\n2. Run this PR's own tests: `rtk proxy env GOMAXPROCS=4 go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<pattern matching the per-branch fact freshness tests>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1 -timeout 20m -v` and confirm the test NAMES appear — a `-run` matching nothing also prints \"ok\".\n3. PROVE THE RESOLUTION KEPT THE FEATURE: pick the one line that is this PR's point, break it, confirm you see `--- FAIL: <a specific test name>`, restore it. A `[build failed]` is NOT a red — if your patch orphans a variable, keep the package compiling. Verify your patch applied as a unique match before trusting any result.\n4. Full gate: `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m mise run test:prepush > /tmp/g478.log 2>&1; echo \"EXIT=$?\" >> /tmp/g478.log`. The `-timeout` is REQUIRED: internal/cli is 232s idle but 805-855s under parallel load, against go test's 10m default, and other agents are running suites right now. Then grep the log for `--- FAIL` and the recorded EXIT. Never trust a bare exit code over an unread log.\n\nThen commit (conventional subject; body states what main extracted, what you kept, and the weakening you ran; NO AI/Claude attribution footer) and `git push origin perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint`.\n\nEnv: this shell sets FORCE_COLOR=3, which fails colour-assert tests on correct code — reproduce on main before believing one. Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n\nREPORT caveman-ultra compressed: conflicted hunks + how resolved; any renames followed in tests; the weakening and its exact `--- FAIL` line; gate EXIT + FAIL count + package count; commit SHA; anything unverified."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,