{"parentUuid":"7aab7a7d-9073-48f3-9c70-8f3cb64f1e26","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNTj2HGb8CKC7sTLarM3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the classifier is blocking `SendMessage` too — it's a broad failure, not Bash-specific. I'll stop attempting gated actions and preserve the handoff in a file instead, since `Write` still works:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":489163,"output_tokens":1833,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":326},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1738,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1833,"cache_read_input_tokens":489163,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1738,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1738},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8be96ec4-3950-4d21-bd42-1c2f45972aeb","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNTj1kGvefaX5WwgCfry","requestRef":"9ac5836b-b18f-4252-b4db-d41073139514","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"e5519d47-aa24-41d8-8a3e-62e8abdbdca6","timestamp":"2026-10-25T06:12:56.295Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"e5519d47-aa24-41d8-8a3e-62e8abdbdca6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNTj2HGb8CKC7sTLarM3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UW9i11Rd46xG8WkfkD58PR","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/BRAIN-HANDOFF-STATE.md","content":"# Brain handoff state — final, 2026-10-25\n\nWritten to a file because the Bash **and** SendMessage safety classifier began returning no\nverdict and did not recover, so I could not message the graph session or run git. The graph\nsession's handoff page should be corrected from this. Nothing here is lost work; two actions\nremain, both one command each.\n\n## The 13 heads\n\n| PR | branch | head | note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #473 | fix/distill-pipeline-v2 | `1f461e47` | main merged |\n| #474 | fix/export-divergent-transcript | unchanged | |\n| #476 | perf/history-terms-normalize-once | unchanged | |\n| #477 | feat/mcp-surface-reachable | `906e8ad3` | main merged |\n| #478 | perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint | `67d3321c` | main merged |\n| #479 | perf/export-detail-fanout | unchanged | ancestor of #481 |\n| #480 | fix/routed-checkpoint-list-cap | unchanged | |\n| #481 | perf/local-checkpoint-metadata | unchanged | |\n| #482 | fix/firstrun-agent-hook-paths | unchanged | |\n| #483 | fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize | `201fe6eb` | **STALE — commit pending, see below** |\n| #484 | feat/brief-ancestor-staleness | `8d3f4ce8` | |\n| #488 | fix/export-honours-session-tombstones | unchanged | ancestor of #489 |\n| #489 | fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints | `c0117710` | partial-clone guard, gate green |\n\nMerge order and the two stacks (`#479→#481`, `#488→#489`) are unchanged. I checked a suspicion\nthat #477 and #478 were a hidden third stack — they conflicted in the same file over the same\nper-branch fact code — and `merge-base --is-ancestor` says **#478 is not an ancestor of #477**.\nTwo stacks only.\n\n## Two things still to do\n\n1. **Finish #483's commit.** See `RESUME-483-UNCOMMITTED.md` — resolved and fully verified in\n   the worktree, uncommitted only because the classifier failed. Do not quote `201fe6eb` as its\n   final head.\n2. **Refresh #493** (the DO-NOT-MERGE integration PR). It holds the older #483 *and* the older\n   #489, and its passing suite predates both. Treat its result as a snapshot against\n   `main@20eb1207`, not a current one.\n\n## Carry this into the merge\n\nMain is taking the COR-2268 extraction series — #490 workspace, #491 semantic, #492 patterns —\nlanding roughly every 25 minutes. Each extraction collides with whichever branch touches the\nsame file, and it invalidated a clean full-order simulation **twice in one session with none of\nmy branches changing**. So \"all 13 merge clean\" is only ever true of a named `main` SHA. Re-run\nthe simulation immediately before the real merges.\n\nWhen resolving one of these: keep the branch's behaviour, adopt main's names. Taking main's side\non an extraction conflict compiles, passes most tests, and silently deletes the PR's feature.\nProve each resolution by weakening the one line that is the PR's point and confirming a named\n`--- FAIL`; a `[build failed]` is not a red.\n\nAlso: `internal/cli` is 232s idle but 805–855s under parallel load, against `go test`'s 10m\ndefault which `test:prepush` never raises. Use `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m`.\n\n## Still the user's, not blocked on anything technical\n\nApprovals on the 13 (plus closing #493, which must never be merged); the transcript-mode\nre-distill, which spends money; and the 37 GB brain-store delete. The #489 shrink question is\n**closed** — see `DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md` §7, rewritten as a closed item, not a decision.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":489163,"output_tokens":1833,"output_tokens_details":{"th