nel skip in the identity reader turns two of them red. I re-read all three hunks myself before committing.\n\nTwo things unchanged from my last message and worth keeping on the page:\n- Two stacks only. I checked whether #477 and #478 were a hidden third — they conflicted in the same file over the same per-branch fact code — and `merge-base --is-ancestor` says #478 is NOT an ancestor of #477.\n- Main is still taking the COR-2268 series (#490, #491, #492) roughly every 25 minutes, and it invalidated a clean full-order simulation twice in one session with none of my branches changing. \"All 13 merge clean\" is only true of a named main SHA, so the re-simulation step you put on the page is load-bearing, not ceremony.\n\nAlso, in case they are useful beside the three you copied: #477, #478 and #483 each needed a SECOND main-merge after that earlier set, so there are three further resolutions on those branches that are not in ~/devenv-worktrees/handoff/brain-patches/."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"90170716-0488-45e7-b54c-3625e6b9ba75","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNU3MnnFJ8odKG8bGkgh","requestRef":"1c7280cb-8322-4da9-8919-f0e834e4276e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"96f0b3b2-4f49-4d63-aa2f-c553e6baf0e0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T06:17:13.618Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
