{"parentUuid":"ed1c65d1-cc86-4c6c-a855-72c43054e078","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNURFA2qCrDKSvYC7oAD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything in my hands is now complete.\n\n**The two blocked actions finished once the classifier recovered:**\n- **#483** committed and pushed (`fbc2946a`) — I re-read all three resolved hunks before committing rather than trusting the agent's report.\n- **#493** re-simulated against `main@ab575071`, force-pushed (`4654e994`), body updated. Combined tree: `go test ./...` exit 0, **20 ok + 5 no-test-files = 25 of 25** packages, zero `--- FAIL`, gofmt silent, vet exit 0.\n\nI deleted `RESUME-483-UNCOMMITTED.md` and rewrote `BRAIN-HANDOFF-STATE.md` to say nothing is pending — leaving stale \"unfinished work\" notes in the repo would have been its own small untruth.\n\n**The session's substance**, since it ran long:\n\nFour review findings fixed, all mine, including #489's — where I'd over-corrected a refusal into partition-and-warn and made a transient git failure silently publish a shrunken corpus. I then found my *reason for deferring* the fix was wrong too: destroyed commits and unfetched blobs take different code paths, so no product decision was needed. That one came off your list rather than onto it.\n\nFour main-merge conflicts resolved against a refactor series that landed every ~25 minutes, each resolution proved by weakening the one line that is the PR's point — because taking main's side on an extraction conflict compiles, passes, and silently deletes the feature.\n\nOne class recurred three times and is worth remembering: a test asserting a *proxy* for the property its name claims. A classifier boolean standing in for publish behaviour, my own construction-layer check standing in for emitted JSON, and an error-returned check standing in for an allocation-avoided claim. All three were green suites.\n\nAnd the thing you opened with — \"doesn't seem like you're using graph\" — had a mechanical cause: `devenv` and `cli` had no `SubagentStart` hook, so Explore and Plan subagents never saw the guidance. Fixed, and the graph session measured 2/2 graph-first on both main sessions and subagents.\n\n**Yours alone:** Approvals on the 13 (and close #493 — never merge it), transcript mode, the 37 GB delete."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":828,"cache_read_input_tokens":506679,"output_tokens":755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":828,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":755,"cache_read_input_tokens":506679,"cache_creation_input_tokens":828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":828},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c9ef22ee-f9b4-4c07-92ec-332479c38bb0","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNUREoTECVxWr1EcDYea","requestRef":"e2d9980a-6ffe-410f-a11d-a471e8c4632a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"5bcc95be-8856-4836-8e49-697c78b50ac9","timestamp":"2026-10-25T06:22:05.948Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
