{"parentUuid":"292d4f92-6e92-4e5b-accc-9d2d9fc996a4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPEpxaRiexxHVAMZ4eTQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TcRXWcsyi12JU72qPeejMn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/pr-carried-another-prs-feature.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: pr-carried-another-prs-feature\ndescription: A PR silently contained another PR's whole feature; merge-base ancestry said no stack, so only diff --stat vs main found it\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nbrain #477 (MCP surface) contained **all** of #478 (per-branch fact fingerprint) as content:\n`pattern_corpus.go` +92 and `pattern_corpus_branch_facts_test.go` +174, added by a commit\nlabelled \"fix(doctor): the MCP probe's stderr sink must be safe to read before Wait\". Almost\ncertainly my own earlier conflict resolution pulling the file from the wrong worktree.\n\n**Why I missed it:** I suspected a hidden stack and checked `git merge-base --is-ancestor`.\nIt said no — correctly, and I read that as \"the PRs are independent\". Ancestry answers\n*history*, not *content*. Two branches with no ancestor relation can hold byte-identical\nblobs; here the two files' blob SHAs matched exactly.\n\n**Why:** a reviewer opening #477 meets an unexplained fingerprint rewrite inside an MCP PR\nand bounces it, and merging both double-applies the change.\n\n**How to apply:** per PR, run `git diff --stat origin/main...<branch>` and read the file list\nagainst the PR's stated subject. Any file outside that subject is either an explained\ndependency, a stack parent, or contamination. Do this after *every* conflict resolution, not\njust when a stack is suspected. Note that stacked PRs legitimately show the parent's files\n(#481 shows #479's, #489 shows #488's), and a changed call signature legitimately ripples\nthrough unrelated-looking test files (#480 moved 8 fake-runner fixtures to a shared key\nhelper) — so read the diff, don't just count files. See [[pairwise-clean-has-a-shelf-life]]\nand [[ours-resolution-deletes-features]].\nEOF\nprintf '%s\\n' '- [A PR carried another PR'\"'\"'s feature](pr-carried-another-prs-feature.md) — merge-base ancestry says \"no stack\" while the blobs are identical; audit `diff --stat` vs main per PR' >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\ntail -2 /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md","description":"Record the contamination lesson in memory"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":478,"cache_read_input_tokens":149453,"output_tokens":1090,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":132},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":478,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1090,"cache_read_input_tokens":149453,"cache_creation_input_tokens":478,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":478},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TcRXWcsyi12JU72qPeejMn":{"command":"cat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/pr-carried-another-prs-feature.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: pr-carried-another-prs-feature\ndescription: A PR silently contained another PR's whole feature; merge-base ancestry said no stack, so only diff --stat vs main found it\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nbrain #477 (MCP surface) contained **all** of #478 (per-branch fact fingerprint) as content:\n`pattern_corpus.go` +92 and `pattern_corpus_branch_facts_test.go` +174, added by a commit\nlabelled \"fix(doctor): the MCP probe's stderr sink must be safe to read before Wait\". Almost\ncertainly my own earlier conflict resolution pulling the file from the wrong worktree.\n\n**Why I missed it:** I suspected a hidden stack and checked `git merge-base --is-ancestor`.\nIt said no — correctly, and I read that as \"the PRs are independent\". Ancestry answers\n*history*, not *content*. Two branches with no ancestor relation can hold byte-identical\nblobs; here the two files' blob SHAs matched exactly.\n\n**Why:** a reviewer opening #477 meets an unexplained fingerprint rewrite inside an MCP PR\nand bounces it, and merging both double-applies the change.\n\n**How to apply:** per PR, run `git diff --stat origin/main...<branch>` and read the file list\nagainst the PR's stated subject. Any file outside that subject is either an explained\ndependency, a stack parent, or contamination. Do this after *every* conflict resolution, not\njust when a stack is suspected. Note that stacked PRs legitimately show the parent's files\n(#481 shows #479's, #489 shows #488's), and a changed call signature legitimately ripples\nthrough unrelated-looking test files (#480 moved 8 fake-runner fixtures to a shared key\nhelper) — so read the diff, don't just count files. See [[pairwise-clean-has-a-shelf-life]]\nand [[ours-resolution-deletes-features]].\nEOF\nprintf '%s\\n' '- [A PR carried another PR'\"'\"'s feature](pr-carried-another-prs-feature.md) — merge-base ancestry says \"no stack\" while the blobs are identical; audit `diff --stat` vs main per PR' >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\ntail -2 /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md","description":"Record the contamination lesson in memory"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"763618c2-9f03-42c9-8787-dc23140398e2","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPEpxELgarMa3GHRJYMW","requestRef":"0a95ec6f-dc3c-4c5d-802b-9d82199dfe66","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0e3ed86-a46f-403b-9d07-b6bb027379f5","