{"parentUuid":"86c793fc-94a1-48ba-a7bf-4da697de8fb8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1414f770-8e13-418f-9c53-d9d83d22efd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HjgsQdi659zJqWdWvySLXE","type":"tool_result","content":"    5200 /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/pr493.md\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2539/changes/entire-brain/404\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\n## DO NOT MERGE\n\nThis is a verification branch, not a change. It exists so CI runs the **combined** tree of\nall thirteen open brain PRs in their intended merge order. It should be closed, never merged;\nthe thirteen PRs merge individually.\n\n## Why it exists\n\nEach of the thirteen was green on its own, and each merged cleanly against `main`\n**pairwise**. That is not the same as being safe to land in sequence: merging one changes\n`main` for the next, and a semantic break needs no textual conflict at all. The\nentire-graph session hit exactly that on its own integration branch — a test asserting a\nfile another PR had deliberately stopped writing. Nothing in a per-PR gate can see it.\n\nUpstream drift proved the point again while this was being prepared: `#490`\n(workspace extraction) and `#491` landed on `main` mid-session, and `#473` — clean two hours","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8e7e5a31-e542-466d-8eca-bb54dee18e98","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:04:46.358Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"    5200 /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/pr493.md\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2539/changes/entire-brain/404\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\n## DO NOT MERGE\n\nThis is a verification branch, not a change. It exists so CI runs the **combined** tree of\nall thirteen open brain PRs in their intended merge order. It should be closed, never merged;\nthe thirteen PRs merge individually