{"parentUuid":"5ec4c3a2-a8f7-4105-a70a-6f9cfd883181","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"48505276-424b-4311-9824-04b880049694","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V4BeeyAHGsQfoGtzNfzAQv","type":"tool_result","content":"############ trail entire-brain/384 ############\n  id: 01M5RS21DZA20NW7JMZVAVG1FT\n  status: open\n  severity: low\n  body: `watchLogPrefixWriter.Write` mutates `midLine` and builds the prefix with no mutex. `watchStepCommand` now hands this one writer to distill/refresh/seed as both stdout and stderr, and distill runs concurrent goroutines (`--jobs`) that can write warnings directly to it. That is a data race and can interleave or mis-stamp lines. Guard `Write` with a `sync.Mutex`.\n  reviewId: 01M5RS21DE4Z40Q322NF20ZW9E\n  ---\n############ trail entire-brain/394 ############\n  id: 01M5RQX5QH01ENPCDCYRRRVNWC\n  status: open\n  severity: medium\n  body: The early `errors.Is(err, errHistoryTranscriptTooLarge)` return runs before the containment, source-race and cancellation checks. Readers return `errors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr)`, so an oversize error joined with a degraded or source-race error is now treated as a per-file failure and the delta publishes. Check the refusal conditions first, or skip only when the sentinel is the sole error. The `errors.Is` skips in `buildBrainHistoryIndexSnapshotContext` and `captureHistoryProjectionIdentityMode` have the same masking problem.\n  reviewId: 01M5RQX5Q4TKKPTCJR0GCQVPS7\n  ---\n############ trail entire-brain/395 ############\n  id: 01M5RPR8P9VFA3R0GQ21JEJM5A\n  status: open\n  severity: medium\n  body: `Semantic.Staleness` is only copied into the `--json` projection. The compact-v1 renderer (`brain_brief_compact.go`) prints symbols, relations and tests but not `staleness`. An ancestor-served answer in that format therefore looks exact, and a missing result for a changed file reads as no consumers. Emit a staleness record (ancestor commit, `commits_behind`, `unreliable`, `excluded_records`) in the compact output as well.\n  reviewId: 01M5RPR8P0QK0QHZC5PYCEKXRV\n  ---\n############ trail entire-brain/400 ############\n  id: 01M5RT28DSE2SAVPEZTC3MKVR5\n  status: open\n  severity: medium\n  body: `gitDirHasPromisorRemote` caches `false` in `promisorRemoteAnswers` even when the `git config` probe itself failed (cancelled context, deadline, spawn error). In a partial clone that cached `false` makes later missing-object probes for that gitDir count as definitively gone, so `partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` skips sessions instead of refusing. Only cache definitive answers (success, or exit code 1 meaning no match), and treat other errors as unknown without storing them.\n  reviewId: 01M5RT28DB9CSXD2RPJPABCZH2\n  ---","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"11af8ad5-e244-4c3d-9418-8b375cf23195","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:15:59.237Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"############ trail entire-brain/384 ############\n  id: 01M5RS21DZA20NW7JMZVAVG1FT\n  status: open\n  severity: low\n  body: `watchLogPrefixWriter.Write` mutates `midLine` and builds the prefix with no mutex. `watchStepCommand` now hands this one writer to distill/refresh/seed as both stdout and stderr, and distill runs concurrent goroutines (`--jobs`) that can write warnings directly to it. That is a data race and can interleave or mis-stamp lines. Guard `Write` with a `sync.Mutex`.\n  reviewId: 01M5RS21DE4Z40Q322NF20ZW9E\n  ---\n############ trail entire-brain/394 ############\n  id: 01M5RQX5QH01ENPCDCYRRRVNWC\n  status: open\n  severity: medium\n  body: The early `errors.Is(err, errHistoryTranscriptTooLarge)` return runs before the containment, source-race and cancellation checks. Readers return `errors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr)`, so an oversize error joined with a degraded or source-race error is now treated as a per-file failure and the delta publishes. Check the refusal conditions first, or skip only when the sentinel is the sole error. The `errors.Is` skips in `buildBrainHistoryIndexSnapshotContext` and `captureHistoryProjectionIdentityMode` have the same masking problem.\n  reviewId: 01M5RQX5Q4TKKPTCJR0GCQVPS7\n  ---\n############ trail entire-brain/395 ############\n  id: 01M5RPR8P9VFA3R0GQ21JEJM5A\n  status: open\n  severity: medium\n  body: `Semantic.Staleness` is only copied into the `--json` projection. The compact-v1 renderer (`brain_brief_compact.go`) prints symbols, relations and tests but not `staleness`. An ancestor-served answer in that format therefore looks exact, and a missing result for a changed file reads as no consumers. Emit a staleness record (ancestor commit, `commits_behind`, `unreliable`, `excluded_records`) in the compact output as well.\n  reviewId: 01M5RPR8P0QK0QHZC5PYCEKXRV\n  ---\n############ trail entire-brain/400 ############\n  id: 01M5RT28DSE2SAVPEZTC3MKVR5\n  status: open\n  severity: medium\n  body: `gitDirHasPromisorRemote` caches `false` in `promisorRemoteAnswers` even when the `git config` probe itself failed (cancelled context, deadline, spawn error). In a partial clone that cached `false` makes later missing-object probes for that gitDir count as definitively gone, so `partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` skips sessions instead of refusing. Only cache definitive answers (success, or exit code 1 meaning no match), and treat other errors as unknown without storing them.\n  reviewId: 01M5RT28DB9CSXD2RPJPABCZH2\n  ---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"df4cc6fa-ee53-4936-9393-76d103730101","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","branch":"tmp/integ4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","