{"parentUuid":"c6b8f02a-3f02-4d51-be4a-89cd2cb3e838","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPFka9K3wgdx9k8TCwHi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KLc8RzieCAzQE9ish2uxs7","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix PR 484 compact staleness gap","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix one agent-review finding in the entire-brain repo. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness (branch feat/brief-ancestor-staleness, PR #484). Do not touch any other worktree or branch.\n\nCAVEMAN-ULTRA COMPRESSED OUTPUT. Use rtk (token-saving CLI proxy) for git/shell where it applies. Your tool output never reaches me — only your final report — so make the report dense and factual.\n\nTHE FINDING (trail entire-brain/395, id 01M5RPR8P9VFA3R0GQ21JEJM5A, severity medium), verbatim:\n\"`Semantic.Staleness` is only copied into the `--json` projection. The compact-v1 renderer (`brain_brief_compact.go`) prints symbols, relations and tests but not `staleness`. An ancestor-served answer in that format therefore looks exact, and a missing result for a changed file reads as no consumers. Emit a staleness record (ancestor commit, `commits_behind`, `unreliable`, `excluded_records`) in the compact output as well.\"\n\nContext you need: PR #484 adds ancestor-staleness disclosure to `brain brief`. When graph answers from an ancestor commit rather than HEAD, the answer can be stale and a missing result must NOT read as \"no consumers\". The staleness record carries ancestor commit, commits_behind, unreliable, and excluded_records. `excluded_records` exists because `unreliable` is structurally empty in the common case — so a reader seeing no unreliable entries would wrongly conclude the answer was complete. That is the whole point of the feature, and the compact renderer silently dropping it defeats it.\n\nTreat the finding as a hypothesis to verify first. Confirm: (a) the compact-v1 renderer exists and does not emit staleness; (b) it is a real user-facing path for `brain brief` (not dead code) — check who selects compact-v1. If the finding is wrong, say so with evidence and stop.\n\nIf real, emit the staleness record in the compact output too, matching that renderer's existing format conventions exactly (read how it renders symbols/relations/tests and follow it; do not invent a new shape). Include all four fields the finding names.\n\nMANDATORY VERIFICATION, report each command and its real result:\n1. `go build ./...` exit 0.\n2. A test that asserts staleness IS in the compact output. CRITICAL — this exact trap already bit this PR once: the existing JSON-emission test is `strings.Contains`-based, so ADDING a field passes silently AND dropping it would also pass. Your test must be a real guard: assert at the compact-emission layer, then PROVE it by weakening — drop the staleness emission from the compact renderer (or retag it) and confirm a NAMED `--- FAIL` with your test's name. `[build failed]` is NOT a red; keep the package compiling and grep `--- FAIL`.\n3. Restore; green.\n4. `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<your tests>|TestBrief|Staleness|Compact' -count=1` green.\n5. `$(go env GOROOT)/bin/gofmt -l -s .` silent (use the GOROOT gofmt; PATH's is an older Go).\n6. `go vet ./...` exit 0 — capture status directly, never through a pipe.\n7. Commit (NO AI attribution footer, no Co-Authored-By — repo rule) and push to origin feat/brief-ancestor-staleness. Report new head SHA.\n8. Resolve the finding: `entire trail finding resolve --trail entire-brain/395 --finding 01M5RPR8P9VFA3R0GQ21JEJM5A --json` (check `--help` for exact flags first). A 404 means a stale local `entire` binary — report it, don't guess.\n\nNote: `internal/cli` is huge (232s idle, 805s+ under load) vs go test's 10m default — always GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m, and scope -run to your tests.\n\nReport: finding confirmed? (evidence, incl. who selects compact-v1), what you changed, the exact weakening red (test name), each verification result, new head SHA, finding-resolve outcome. If anything failed, say so plainly — do not report success you did not observe."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1944,"cache_read_input_tokens":172778,"output_tokens":3077,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1944,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3077,"cache_read_input_tokens":172778,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1944,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1944},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KLc8RzieCAzQE9ish2uxs7":{"description":"Fix PR 484 compact staleness gap","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix one agent-review finding in the entire-brain repo. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness (branch feat/brief-ancestor-staleness, PR #484). Do not touch any other worktree or branch.\n\nCAVEMAN-ULTRA COMPRESSED OUTPUT. Use rtk (token-saving CLI proxy) for git/shell where it applies. Your tool output never reaches me — only your final report — so make the report dense and factual.\n\nTHE FINDING (trail entire-brain/395, id 01M5RPR8P9VFA3R0GQ21JEJM5A, severity medium), verbatim:\n\"`Semantic.Staleness` is only copied into the `--json` projection. The compact-v1 renderer (`brain_brief_compact.go`) prints symbols, relations and tests but not `staleness`. An ancestor-served answer in that format therefore looks exact, and a missing result for a changed file reads as no consumers. Emit a staleness record 