{"parentUuid":"1ca37577-3599-4e83-85ef-8998e41985ac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPG39LHgfL2a36SR6XqV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KX91eEo16FzvYRpRo98yz6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add internal/cli/git_catfile_batch.go internal/cli/export_vanished_checkpoint_test.go && git commit -q -m \"fix(export): only cache a promisor probe that actually got an answer\n\ngitDirHasPromisorRemote cached its result per git directory, including the\nfalse it returned when the config read itself failed. A cancelled context, a\ndeadline or a spawn failure therefore pinned that git directory to \\\"no\npromisor remote\\\" for the life of the process, and every later absent object\nthere read as destroyed rather than unfetched -- so partitionLocalTranscriptSessions\ndropped the sessions instead of refusing, which is the corpus shrink the\nsurrounding guard exists to prevent, reached through the cache instead of\nthrough the probe.\n\nThe probe now reports whether its answer is definitive. config succeeding, and\nconfig exiting 1 for \\\"nothing matched\\\", are both real answers and are cached.\nAnything else is not an answer: it reports \\\"may be fetchable\\\" so the caller\nrefuses, and is not stored, so the next call asks again. Refusing is the\nrecoverable direction -- an export that stops can be retried after a sync,\nwhile a corpus republished without those sessions has already lost them.\" && echo \"head=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"; git push origin HEAD:fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Commit and push the PR 489 fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":515,"cache_read_input_tokens":196568,"output_tokens":556,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch