{"parentUuid":"dda1864f-6df2-4430-8619-d0584cfbee47","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPGZPhZvoeatWcqb2ZrR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ENwCMvA3hzXF8fuWvUGhZk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add internal/cli/history.go internal/cli/history_delta.go internal/cli/history_oversize_tolerance_test.go && git commit -q -m \"fix(history): the oversize sentinel may excuse only itself\n\nThe reader built its oversize error as fmt.Errorf(\\\"%w: %w\\\", sentinel,\nerrors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr)) whenever the read breached the size\nbound, regardless of what else was in that join. All three inventory readers\nskip a file on errors.Is of the sentinel, so a source race or containment\nbreach reported by validateAfterRead -- a transcript swapped mid-read, a path\nthat became a symlink out of the brain root -- or a failed Close was discarded\nsilently and the generation published.\n\nThe classification is now a named truth table, oversizeIsTheSoleFault, because\nthe answer is the whole contract rather than a detail: only readErr alone, and\nonly when it is the size breach, is a statement about one file. Reaching the\njoined case needs a writer appending during the read (the inventory's own\npre-read check rejects a file that grew beforehand), which is why it is tested\nas a table and not through a fixture that cannot make it deterministic.\n\nshortTermCanonicalInputRefusal had the mirror image of the same bug: it asked\nabout the sentinel before the other refusal reasons, so a degraded inventory or\na cancelled context arriving joined with an oversize transcript answered\n\\\"skip\\\" for the whole join. Every other refusal is now tested first.\n\nOne oversize transcript alone still costs only its own session, which is the\npoint of the change this sits on.\" && echo \"head=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"; git push origin HEAD:fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Commit and push the PR 483 fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":557,"cache_read_input_tokens":235706,"output_tokens":687,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":557,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":687,"cache_read_input_tokens":235706,"cache_creation_input_tokens":557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":557},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ENwCMvA3hzXF8fuWvUGhZk":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize && git add internal/cli/history.go internal/cli/history_delta.go internal/cli/history_oversize_tolerance_test.go && git commit -q -m \"fix(history): the oversize sentinel may excuse only itself\n\nThe reader built its oversize error as fmt.Errorf(\\\"%w: %w\\\", sentinel,\nerrors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr)) whenever the read breached the size\nbound, regardless of what else was in that join. All three inventory readers\nskip a file on errors.Is of the sentinel, so a source race or containment\nbreach reported by validateAfterRead -- a transcript swapped mid-read, a path\nthat became a symlink out of the brain root -- or a failed Close was discarded\nsilently and the generation published.\n\nThe classification is now a named truth table, oversizeIsTheSoleFault, because\nthe answer is the whole contract rather than a detail: only readErr alone, and\nonly when it is the size breach, is a statement about one file. Reaching the\njoined case needs a writer appending during the read (the inventory's own\npre-read check rejects a file that grew beforehand), which is why it is tested\nas a table and not through a fixture that cannot make it deterministic.\n\nshortTermCanonicalInputRefusal had the mirror image of the same bug: it asked\nabout the sentinel before the other refusal reasons, so a degraded inventory or\na cancelled context arriving joined with an oversize transcript answered\n\\\"skip\\\" for the whole join. Every other refusal is now tested first.\n\nOne oversize transcript alone still costs only its own session, which is the\npoint of the change this sits on.\" && echo \"head=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"; git push origin HEAD:fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Commit and push the PR 483 fix"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01ENwCMvA3hzXF8fuWvUGhZk":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"bd996d29-7d27-4ac3-b761-db65c526e881","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPGZPLjEVvFqQJ93dKD4","requestRef":"f92d58a8-68f5-4a4e-9dd7-7d53d6573774","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"459972f7-35fd-4fd6-a9d1-10d1efa456df","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:27:07.997Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
