{"parentUuid":"6d9bc75d-85a4-412c-8554-9c8b77138a74","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPGccHCK4wCHqmTPknry","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012KrjofR6m3dQNkgUoNjKqf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"entire trail finding resolve 01M5RQX5QH01ENPCDCYRRRVNWC --trail entire-brain/394 -m \"Fixed at 515a85a1, at the root rather than the three call sites. readHistorySessionInventoryFile built the sentinel-wrapped error whenever the read breached the size bound, regardless of what else was in errors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr) -- so validateAfterRead's source-race and containment errors, and a failed Close, were discarded by the readers' errors.Is skip. Classification is now oversizeIsTheSoleFault: only readErr alone, and only the size breach, is a statement about one file. That fixes all three errors.Is sites at once, including the two you named. shortTermCanonicalInputRefusal had the mirror bug and now tests every other refusal first. Two weakenings, each a named red with the package compiling: letting the size breach win with finishErr set (4 subtests red), and restoring the sentinel-first ordering in the delta (4 subtests red). One honest limitation: the joined readErr+finishErr case needs a writer appending DURING the read -- the inventory's pre-read check rejects a file that grew beforehand -- so it is pinned as a truth table on the extracted rule, not through a filesystem fixture. My first attempt asserted it through a fixture, the weakening did not fire, and that is how I found the fixture was passing for the wrong reason.\" 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Resolve the PR 483 finding"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4515,"cache_read_input_tokens":236263,"output_tokens":1282,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":337},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4515,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1282,"cache_read_input_tokens":236263,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4515},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012KrjofR6m3dQNkgUoNjKqf":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize && entire trail finding resolve 01M5RQX5QH01ENPCDCYRRRVNWC --trail entire-brain/394 -m \"Fixed at 515a85a1, at the root rather than the three call sites. readHistorySessionInventoryFile built the sentinel-wrapped error whenever the read breached the size bound, regardless of what else was in errors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr) -- so validateAfterRead's source-race and containment errors, and a failed Close, were discarded by the readers' errors.Is skip. Classification is now oversizeIsTheSoleFault: only readErr alone, and only the size breach, is a statement about one file. That fixes all three errors.Is sites at once, including the two you named. shortTermCanonicalInputRefusal had the mirror bug and now tests every other refusal first. Two weakenings, each a named red with the package compiling: letting the size breach win with finishErr set (4 subtests red), and restoring the sentinel-first ordering in the delta (4 subtests red). One honest limitation: the joined readErr+finishErr case needs a writer appending DURING the read -- the inventory's pre-read check rejects a file that grew beforehand -- so it is pinned as a truth table on the extracted rule, not through a filesystem fixture. My first attempt asserted it through a fixture, the weakening did not fire, and that is how I found the fixture was passing for the wrong reason.\" 2>&1 | tail -2",