{"parentUuid":"eef0308a-a3fb-4819-ad64-f5265588dd7f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14726675 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"db1a8089-145a-449b-81f5-d5193529ede2","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:35:58.512Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14726675 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"db1a8089-145a-449b-81f5-d5193529ede2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPHFBzECsz9jtHxFUfnH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hook was right, and I was wrong to call the work finished. **Four open agent-review findings** were sitting on the trails — all four real, and two of them were my own mistakes.\n\n| PR | finding | outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#489** | promisor probe cached `false` even when the probe *failed* | `9113d4fc` — a cancelled context pinned a partial clone to \"no promisor remote\" for the process, so later absent objects read as destroyed and sessions were dropped instead of refused. **This is the exact bug I fixed in #484's probe memoization and then reintroduced here.** |\n| **#483** | oversize sentinel ran before the containment/source-race checks | `515a85a1` — fixed at the constructor, not the three call sites: it wrapped the sentinel around `errors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr)` whenever the size bound broke, so `validateAfterRead`'s **containment and source-race refusals were silently discarded** and the generation published. |\n| **#484** | staleness only in `--json` | `971b9dae` + `9a3aac28` — it was missing from **3 of 5 formats**, and the agent's v2 schema turned out to be mandatory, not optional. I then closed the gap it flagged: the **default** `brain brief` output was silent too, which is the surface most answers are read through. |\n| **#473** | unsynchronised `Write` is a data race | `8f693073` — **mechanism refuted.** Nothing writes from a second goroutine: workers return over channels, subprocesses get capped buffers, and the only progress goroutine is gated behind a TTY check requiring `*os.File`. I verified that myself rather than take the agent's word. The lock landed anyway, framed as the writer's concurrency contract — one writer really is shared by three subsystems and both guards are implicit. |\n\nEvery fix is weakening-proved with a named `--- FAIL`, and two proofs are worth naming because they caught me:\n\n- My first #483 test passed, then the weakening **didn't fire** — the fixture was green for the wrong reason (a pre-read check caught the race before the path I was testing). I extracted the rule into a truth table instead and reported the limitation rather than hiding it.\n- My #484 ordering weakening **silently failed to apply**, and the \"ok\" that followed was the unmodified tree. I caught it and re-ran it properly.\n\nCurrent state: main `a4942dd9`, all 13 **MERGEABLE**, all 13 merge clean in order, combined tree builds and gofmt-clean at `879cac2d`, pushed for CI. The local full suite is running.\n\nYour five items are unchanged — and this is why I don't treat \"the engineering is done\" as the same claim as \"nothing is left\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_read_input_tokens":272768,"output_tokens":903,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":903,"cache_read_input_tokens":272768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"770d7818-8eb5-4212-a1a4-a0d370ec25ee","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPHFBWxNG2ii8pSAVeGW","requestRef":"82cbde2e-afd4-49a4-858d-1cf58fc93763","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"461c590e-a059-4172-998c-06540a13ad4b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:36:12.194Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
