{"parentUuid":"446247bb-19c0-48c9-acaa-65675d845ddd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPHz7U56PGo2gifyLjMi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VRarecW4TitJkHV2XSmh1L","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add internal/cli/history.go internal/cli/transcript_store.go internal/cli/history_oversize_tolerance_test.go && git commit -q -m \"fix(history): close the other two sentinel-masking sites\n\nThe previous commit fixed readHistorySessionInventoryFile and claimed that\ncovered every reader. It did not: the sentinel has three producers, not one.\n\ndigestHistorySessionInventoryFile joined the sentinel onto its read error\nwhenever the byte count passed the cap, before consulting validateAfterRead.\ncaptureHistoryProjectionIdentityMode skips on\nerrors.Is(errHistoryTranscriptTooLarge), so a transcript swapped mid-read, or\nwhose path became a symlink out of the brain root, was dropped from the content\nidentity with the generation published.\n\nclassifyTranscriptReadError was the same shape with more at stake.\ntranscriptStore.Read hands it errors.Join(readErr, finishErr) and finish()\nvalidates file identity and the current privacy gate; errors.As walks a join,\nso a bound breach anywhere in the chain labelled the whole error skippable and\nthose refusals were swallowed by a per-file skip.\n\nEach rule is now a named function with its own table -- oversizeIsTheSoleFault,\noversizeMayBeAttributedToTheFile, everyFaultIsABoundBreach -- because two paths\nsilently drifting apart is precisely what happened, and a condition inline in a\nreader is not something a test can hold.\" && echo \"head=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the two further PR 483 fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319,"cache_read_input_tokens":302409,"output_tokens":