{"parentUuid":"4b5d9089-bd19-45c1-b963-0bc4f00ddb18","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPJ76D6x5UH4kTqWMBt9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B9fXUChATYrXd18mYLntya","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/run-filter-hid-the-breakage.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: run-filter-hid-the-breakage\ndescription: A -run regex scoped to the feature's own test names missed the two existing tests the change broke\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nI changed `gitDirHasPromisorRemote` and verified with\n`go test -run 'Promisor|Vanished|Tombstone|Export|Transcript|GitObject|CatFile'`. Green. The\nchange had broken `TestConfirmedMissingObjectCostsOnlyItsOwnSession` and\n`TestUnavailableDiagnosticsKeepTheirErrorIdentity` — **neither name matches any of those\npatterns.** It surfaced only in the combined-tree full run, after I had already pushed and\ntold the user the work was verified.\n\n**Why:** a `-run` filter is written from the feature's vocabulary, and the tests a behaviour\nchange breaks are the ones that depended on the OLD behaviour — named after their own\nconcern, not after mine. The filter is blind in exactly the direction that matters.\n\n**How to apply:** scope `-run` while iterating, but before committing a behaviour change\n(not a pure addition) run the whole package with no filter: `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m go test\n./... -count=1`. Budget ~240s for `internal/cli` idle. If that is too slow to run often, it\nis still not optional before the push.\n\nThe breakage itself was also instructive: both tests asserted full-clone behaviour with a\nfake that left the promisor probe *unhandled*, which the fake answers with a plain\n`errors.New` carrying no exit code. They passed only because the old code read every error as\n\"no promisor remote\". See [[fixtures-miss-seeded-fields]] and\n[[green-suite-is-not-evidence]].\nEOF\nprintf '%s\\n' '- [A -run filter hid the breakage](run-filter-hid-the-breakage.md) — the tests a behaviour change breaks are named after THEIR concern, not yours; full package before pushing' >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/one-sentinel-three-producers.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: one-sentinel-three-producers\ndescription: Fixed a sentinel-masking bug at one producer and claimed it covered all readers; there were three producers\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nbrain #483: a skippable sentinel (`errHistoryTranscriptTooLarge`) was being wrapped around\n`errors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr)`, so containment and source-race refusals were\ndiscarded by readers that skip on `errors.Is(sentinel)`. I fixed\n`readHistorySessionInventoryFile` and wrote in the commit and the finding-resolve that this\n\"fixes all three errors.Is sites at once\". An agent reviewer then found\n`digestHistorySessionInventoryFile` with the identical bug, and chasing that I found a third,\n`classifyTranscriptReadError` — where `finish()` validates file identity **and the privacy\ngate**, so a size breach was masking those.\n\n**Why:** I counted the sentinel's *consumers* (three `errors.Is` skips) and assumed one\nproducer fed them. Fixing the producer is the right instinct; assuming there is one is the\nerror. `errors.As`/`errors.Is` walk joins, so any producer that attaches a skippable sentinel\nto a joined error has the bug independently.\n\n**How to apply:** when a sentinel's presence grants permission (skip, ignore, downgrade),\ngrep for every site that CONSTRUCTS or attaches it, not just the sites that test it — then\nmake the attach rule a named, table-tested function so two paths cannot drift. The drift is\nthe failure mode: the read path was fixed first and the digest path kept the bug.\nSee [[containment-for-exactness]] and [[logic-in-the-call-site]].\nEOF\nprintf '%s\\n' '- [One sentinel, three producers](one-sentinel-three-producers.md) — counted the errors.Is consumers and assumed one producer; grep the ATTACH sites, name the rule' >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\ntail -2 /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md","description":"Record both lessons in memory"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":531,"cache_read_input_tokens":305283,"output_tokens":1628,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":531,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1628,"cache_read_input_tokens":305283,"cache_creation_input_tokens":531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":531},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01B9fXUChATYrXd18mYLntya":{"command":"cat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/run-filter-hid-the-breakage.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: run-filter-hid-the-breakage\ndescription: A -run regex scoped to the feature's own test names missed the two existing tests the change broke\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nI changed `gitDirHasPromisorRemote` and verified with\n`go test -run 'Promisor|Vanished|Tombstone|Export|Transcript|GitObject|CatFile'`. Green. The\nchange had broken `TestConfirmedMissingObjectCostsOnlyItsOwnSession` and\n`TestUnavailableDiagnosticsKeepTheirErrorIdentity` — **neither name matches any of those\npatterns.** It surfaced only in the combined-tree full run, after I had already pushed and\ntold the user the work was verified.\n\n**Why:** a `-run` filter is written from the feature's vocabulary, and the tests a behaviour\nchange breaks are the ones that depended on the OLD behaviour — named after their own\nconcern, not after mine. The filter is blind in exactly the direction that matters.\n\n**How to apply:** scope `-run` while iterating, but before committing a behaviour change\n(not a pure addition) run the whole package with no filter: `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m go test\n./... -count=1`. Budget ~240s for `internal/cli` idle. If that is too slow to run often, it\nis still not optional before the push.\n\nThe breakage itself was also instructive: both tests asserted full-clone behaviour with a\nfake that left the promisor probe *unhandled*, which the fake answers with a plain\n`errors.New` carrying no exit code. They passed only because the old code read every error as\n\"no promisor remote\". See [[fixtures-miss-seeded-fields]] and\n[[green-suite-is-not-evidence]].\nEOF\nprintf '%s\\n' '- [A -run filter hid the breakage](run-filter-hid-the-breakage.md) — the tests a behaviour change breaks are named after THEIR concern, not yours; full package before pushing' >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/one-sentinel-three-producers.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: one-sentinel-three-producers\ndescription: Fixed a sentinel-masking bug at one producer and claimed it covered all readers; there were three producers\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nbrain #483: a skippable sentinel (`errHistoryTranscriptTooLarge`) was being wrapped around\n`errors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr)`, so containment and source-race refusals were\ndiscarded by readers that skip on `errors.Is(sentinel)`. I fixed\n`readHistorySessionInventoryFile` and wrote in the commit and the finding-resolve that this\n\"fixes all three errors.Is sites at once\". An agent reviewer then found\n`digestHistorySessionInventoryFile` with the identical bug, and chasing that I found a third,\n`classifyTranscriptReadError` — where `finish()` validates file identity **and the privacy\ngate**, so a size breach was masking those.\n\n**Why:** I counted the sentinel's *consumers* (three `errors.Is` skips) and assumed one\nproducer fed them. Fixing the producer is the right instinct; assuming there is one is the\nerror. `errors.As`/`errors.Is` walk joins, so any producer that attaches a skippable sentinel\nto a joined error has the bug independently.\n\n**How to apply:** when a sentinel's presence grants permission (skip, ignore, downgrade),\ngrep for every site that CONSTRUCTS or attaches it, not just the sites that test it — then\nmake the attach rule a named, table-tested function so two paths cannot drift. The drift is\nthe failure mode: the read path was fixed first and the digest path kept the bug.\nSee [[containment-for-exactness]] and [[logic-in-the-call-site]].\nEOF\nprintf '%s\\n' '- [One sentinel, three producers](one-sentinel-three-producers.md) — counted the errors.Is consumers and assumed one producer; grep the ATTACH sites, name the rule' >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\ntail -2 /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md","description":"Record both lessons in memory"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4ab42300-0713-49bb-8574-705507ece486","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPJ75r2Jak9t54VrNvzD","requestRef":"e8953cd6-6027-4b8b-aea2-69b264306511","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"506a31ab-8c4d-4ca2-b868-3b2b36dc525e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:47:37.281Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
