{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"500d2495900942b006c896a76bf986c23d8ac6fd8d2b4906edae8df1e544b88f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PjPW31a4vdwVc84Ugj3aR9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished && entire brain remember \"A -run filter written from the feature's vocabulary is blind in the direction that matters: the tests a behaviour change breaks are the ones that depended on the OLD behaviour, named after their own concern. Changing gitDirHasPromisorRemote passed -run 'Promisor|Vanished|Tombstone|Export|Transcript|GitObject|CatFile' while breaking TestConfirmedMissingObjectCostsOnlyItsOwnSession and TestUnavailableDiagnosticsKeepTheirErrorIdentity, which match none of those. Before committing a behaviour change, run the whole package unfiltered (GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m go test ./... -count=1; internal/cli is ~240s idle).\" --path workflow.testing.invariant --branch main --json 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Record the run-filter lesson as a brain fact"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LW5ud4JxYbykxNZ6S6g72X","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished && entire brain remember \"When a sentinel error grants permission (skip, ignore, downgrade), fixing the site that ATTACHES it is right but assuming there is only one is the bug. brain #483 had three producers of errHistoryTranscriptTooLarge - readHistorySessionInventoryFile, digestHistorySessionInventoryFile and classifyTranscriptReadError - and I fixed one, then claimed it covered all three errors.Is consumers. errors.As and errors.Is walk errors.Join, so every attach site has the masking bug independently. Grep the construct/attach sites, not just the test sites, and make the attach rule a named table-tested function: the read path being fixed while the digest path kept the bug is exactly the drift that happened.\" --path workflow.review.gotcha --branch main --json 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Record the sentinel-producers lesson as a brain fact"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
