{"parentUuid":"496d96aa-8d88-4db2-8aeb-4aa4dd1234de","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14691638 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"86b064bb-a549-4953-9de2-7c8c913f990e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:47:48.841Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14691638 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"86b064bb-a549-4953-9de2-7c8c913f990e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01PjPW31a4vdwVc84Ugj3aR9","copy":"wire"},{"id":"toolu_01LW5ud4JxYbykxNZ6S6g72X","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8f48ba13-8ed5-446f-9ad5-b9118a70f40e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:48:01.012Z","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"8f48ba13-8ed5-446f-9ad5-b9118a70f40e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPJ9YrnrUcndroRbGTgz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both lessons are recorded in the brain and in memory. Reporting honestly where this stands:\n\n**My \"all green\" earlier was wrong, and the combined tree is what caught it.** Two `#489` tests failed — `TestConfirmedMissingObjectCostsOnlyItsOwnSession` and `TestUnavailableDiagnosticsKeepTheirErrorIdentity`. Neither name matches any pattern in the `-run` filter I verified with. A filter written from the feature's vocabulary can't see the tests that depended on the *old* behaviour, because they're named after their own concern. Both asserted full-clone behaviour with a fake that left the promisor probe **unhandled** — they passed only because the old code read every error as \"no promisor remote\". Fixed by stating the full clone in the fixture, plus a new test pinning the unanswered-probe case so it can't drift again. `#489`'s full unfiltered suite: **exit 0, 18/18, zero named failures**, pushed as `5f15accf`.\n\n**The reviewer then caught a second bug of mine, and chasing it found a third.** I'd written that my `#483` fix \"fixes all three `errors.Is` sites at once\". Wrong — the sentinel has **three producers**, not one:\n\n- `digestHistorySessionInventoryFile` joined the sentinel before consulting `validateAfterRead`, so a swapped or escaped transcript dropped out of the content identity. *(the reviewer's catch)*\n- `classifyTranscriptReadError` was worse: `transcriptStore.Read` hands it `errors.Join(readErr, finishErr)`, and `finish()` validates file identity **and the privacy gate**. Since `errors.As` walks a join, a size breach anywhere in the chain made those refusals skippable. *(mine, found by sweeping after the reviewer's catch)*\n\nEach of the three rules is now a named function with its own truth table — `oversizeIsTheSoleFault`, `oversizeMayBeAttributedToTheFile`, `everyFaultIsABoundBreach` — precisely because two paths drifting silently is what happened. All three weakening-proved with named reds.\n\n`#483`'s full unfiltered suite is running; I'll push once it's clean, then re-sim and re-run CI on the combined tree.\n\nI counted the sentinel's consumers and assumed one producer fed them. That's the mistake worth keeping, and it's why the hook pushing past my \"done\" was correct both times."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":952,"cache_read_input_tokens":307596,"output_tokens":820,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":952,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":307596,"cache_creation_input_tokens":952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":952},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a1478fc7-72df-4134-b840-ce5c2ce04658","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPJ9Y7ti5kXHmi6a4C81","requestRef":"f18c567e-3468-4ef6-b360-bd2598cb0417","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"f61fa392-f2be-4adf-80c6-016b75b0f62f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:48:01.011Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
