{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","prNumber":493,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/493","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:08:28.677Z"}
{"parentUuid":"63f33d3b-a012-40e6-b50d-f136c54943cb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_012qjXQwmyTce9b8WcPeTLNK","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk read /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/brain-facts-are-branch-scoped.md\",\"description\":\"Read the existing branch-scope memory\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":26},"type":"attachment","uuid":"03019283-595a-4d15-b53b-5a86487a22b0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:08:28.008Z","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"63f33d3b-a012-40e6-b50d-f136c54943cb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0c347b0e-8d44-40df-af73-0cd57680873c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012qjXQwmyTce9b8WcPeTLNK","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: brain-facts-are-branch-scoped\ndescription: A branch's facts file is a FORK-TIME COPY of main's, so a fact written to main later is invisible from that branch\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nMeasured, not inferred. On entire-brain, same query `planTranscriptCacheSweep`:\n\n- `recall --branch main` → my fact at **rank 1**\n- `recall --branch <feature>` → **absent entirely**\n\nMechanism: the feature branch's `facts.ndjson` held **1899 records labelled\n`branch: main`** out of 1931, against main's 1934. So a branch file is a\n**fork-time copy** of main's facts, each record keeping its original branch\nlabel — not a live union with main. Facts written to `main` after the fork are\ninvisible from that branch forever. `entire brain memories promote` exists\nprecisely to carry them across.\n\nControl, which settles it: a canary recorded on the **current** branch is\nrecallable from that branch at **rank 1, immediately**. There is no index lag.\n\n**Why:** I wasted a chunk of a session on this and, worse, told a teammate it\nwas an indexing bug — they began republishing an artifact and planning an\n\"incremental index append\" for a defect that did not exist. I had passed\n`--branch main` on every write (from an older note of my own) and then recalled\nfrom the feature branch I was standing on.\n\n**How to apply:** record on the branch you are working on, or pass `--branch`\nand then `recall --branch` the same value. Before reporting a retrieval miss as\na bug, run the same-branch canary first — write one, recall it, check the rank.\nThis is the same partitioning that killed the COR-2177 fix\n([[distill-cache-stores-hashes-not-facts]]): facts are per-branch copies, not a\nshared store. Related: [[unseen-is-not-impossible]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5861f2a8-80f9-45ac-b25a-7d7a49cc5c85","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:08:30.582Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: brain-facts-are-branch-scoped\ndescription: A branch's facts file is a FORK-TIME COPY of main's, so a fact written to main later is invisible from that branch\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nMeasured, not inferred. On entire-brain, same query `planTranscriptCacheSweep`:\n\n- `recall --branch main` → my fact at **rank 1**\n- `recall --branch <feature>` → **absent entirely**\n\nMechanism: the feature branch's `facts.ndjson` held **1899 records labelled\n`branch: main`** out of 1931, against main's 1934. So a branch file is a\n**fork-time copy** of main's facts, each record keeping its original branch\nlabel — not a live union with main. Facts written to `main` after the fork are\ninvisible from that branch forever. `entire brain memories promote` exists\nprecisely to carry them across.\n\nControl, which settles it: a canary recorded on the **current** branch is\nrecallable from that branch at **rank 1, immediately**. There is no index lag.\n\n**Why:** I wasted a chunk of a session on this and, worse, told a teammate it\nwas an indexing bug — they began republishing an artifact and planning an\n\"incremental index append\" for a defect that did not exist. I had passed\n`--branch main` on every write (from an older note of my own) and then recalled\nfrom the feature branch I was standing on.\n\n**How to apply:** record on the branch you are working on, or pass `--branch`\nand then `recall --branch` the same value. Before reporting a retrieval miss as\na bug, run the same-branch canary first — write one, recall it, check the rank.\nThis is the same partitioning that killed the COR-2177 fix\n([[distill-cache-stores-hashes-not-facts]]): facts are per-branch copies, not a\nshared store. Related: [[unseen-is-not-impossible]].","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a90891dc-4019-468d-88de-f436ee95b66e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","branch":"tmp/integ6","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire.io","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"63f33d3b-a012-40e6-b50d-f136c54943cb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
