{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","id":"071de461-47ca-4992-a373-94f49a732730","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:08:30.626Z","version":"2.1.310","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"24017389debf7cd8bde5028ecf29c4ee6405c6fe767d12c483cd96a0e96b3788","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","context-1m-2025-08-07","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":64000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"65c03e9b-f018-494a-8c4c-6c43c84e880f","keep":577,"tail":["fc07a1c5126972ff417885df72c1b0a0577d0ab8e1130176fb530659522110e8","dc0dc7dd083c6519e603b93e1f2e69e4b486ec100f803e06be7e34620eb771ca","35f68a765cc802bb939cf7cca142ae5563d97a1999c63e7da1d289d7dd1e6aef"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",579,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"52098c47a054da27b5975fad859b364007ef67af2ea252d2e3b34bdad74d3dff"}
{"parentUuid":"5861f2a8-80f9-45ac-b25a-7d7a49cc5c85","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14992566 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"100707ec-5eb3-4dcf-bd3f-0b077fedfd08","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:08:30.591Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14992566 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"100707ec-5eb3-4dcf-bd3f-0b077fedfd08","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPKj4z3xkQ7eEZvYYaHS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QT39xrhCtyAQwYYMexYd4k","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv && python3 - <<'PY'\np=\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/brain-facts-are-branch-scoped.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\ns = s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\"\"\n\n## 2026-10-25: this cost me a real defect, not just time\n\nThe partition does not only hide *my own* writes — it hides **everyone's**, which\nis the expensive half. Measured on the combined-tree worktree (branch\n`tmp/integ6`), one query, `\"when may the oversize transcript sentinel be\nattached\"`:\n\n- from the working branch → **0 rows**\n- `--branch main` → **10 rows**\n\nZero, silently. No warning, no \"this branch has no fact partition\", and\n`brain status` quietly lists a `missing_branches` array. So every recall I would\nhave run from a feature-branch worktree this session was guaranteed empty, which\nis indistinguishable from \"brain knows nothing about this\".\n\nWhat it hid: a fact from an earlier agent-review finding on **the same PR**\nreading *\"entire-brain history: FOUR readers of the canonical transcript\ninventory call readHistorySessionInventoryFile, not three\"*, naming the exact\nundercount. I then fixed #483, wrote \"fixes all three errors.Is sites at once\"\nin the commit and the finding-resolve, and a reviewer caught a second producer;\nchasing that I found a third. Brain already knew the shape of that mistake.\n\n**How to apply, hardened:** pass `--branch main` on EVERY `recall`/`brief` from\na worktree, or run it from a main checkout. Treat a 0-row brain answer as\n\"wrong partition\" first and re-query with `--branch main` before concluding\nthere is no recorded evidence — an empty result is not evidence of absence\n([[unseen-is-not-impossible]]). Dedup the rows yourself: 10 rows came back as\n3-6 distinct, so the budget is partly spent on repeats.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s+\"\\n\")\nprint(\"memory updated\")\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"- [Brain facts are branch-scoped](brain-facts-are-branch-scoped.md) — branch file = FORK-TIME COPY of main; later main facts invisible; try\"\nnew=\"- [Brain facts are branch-scoped](brain-facts-are-branch-scoped.md) — recall from a worktree branch returns 0 rows SILENTLY; pass `--branch main` on every recall; it hid a fact that named my exact bug\"\nif old in s:\n    s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,\"w\").write(s); print(\"index line replaced\")\nelse:\n    print(\"index line not found verbatim; leaving as is\")\nPY","description":"Harden the branch-scope memory with today's measurement"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1347,"cache_read_input_tokens":331029,"output_tokens":1060,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1347,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1060,"cache_read_input_tokens":331029,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1347},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QT39xrhCtyAQwYYMexYd4k":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv && python3 - <<'PY'\np=\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/brain-facts-are-branch-scoped.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\ns = s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\"\"\n\n## 2026-10-25: this cost me a real defect, not just time\n\nThe partition does not only hide *my own* writes — it hides **everyone's**, which\nis the expensive half. Measured on the combined-tree worktree (branch\n`tmp/integ6`), one query, `\"when may the oversize transcript sentinel be\nattached\"`:\n\n- from the working branch → **0 rows**\n- `--branch main` → **10 rows**\n\nZero, silently. No warning, no \"this branch has no fact partition\", and\n`brain status` quietly lists a `missing_branches` array. So every recall I would\nhave run from a feature-branch worktree this session was guaranteed empty, which\nis indistinguishable from \"brain knows nothing about this\".\n\nWhat it hid: a fact from an earlier agent-review finding on **the same PR**\nreading *\"entire-brain history: FOUR readers of the canonical transcript\ninventory call readHistorySessionInventoryFile, not three\"*, naming the exact\nundercount. I then fixed #483, wrote \"fixes all three errors.Is sites at once\"\nin the commit and the finding-resolve, and a reviewer caught a second producer;\nchasing that I found a third. Brain already knew the shape of that mistake.\n\n**How to apply, hardened:** pass `--branch main` on EVERY `recall`/`brief` from\na worktree, or run it from a main checkout. Treat a 0-row brain answer as\n\"wrong partition\" first and re-query with `--branch main` before concluding\nthere is no recorded evidence — an empty result is not evidence of absence\n([[unseen-is-not-impossible]]). Dedup the rows yourself: 10 rows came back as\n3-6 distinct, so the budget is partly spent on repeats.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s+\"\\n\")\nprint(\"memory updated\")\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"- [Brain facts are branch-scoped](brain-facts-are-branch-scoped.md) — branch file = FORK-TIME COPY of main; later main facts invisible; try\"\nnew=\"- [Brain facts are branch-scoped](brain-facts-are-branch-scoped.md) — recall from a worktree branch returns 0 rows SILENTLY; pass `--branch main` on every recall; it hid a fact that named my exact bug\"\nif old in s:\n    s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,\"w\").write(s); print(\"index line replaced\")\nelse:\n    print(\"index line not found verbatim; leaving as is\")\nPY","description":"Harden the branch-scope memory with today's measurement"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"49936d3d-2f5d-4f70-9d00-a9f4303dc0ee","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPKj4gCuYAuko2BYpmZw","requestRef":"071de461-47ca-4992-a373-94f49a732730","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a274b0c-87a2-4512-b2e3-63866a30808b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:08:44.762Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
