{"parentUuid":"761139e4-5920-4a11-b0da-fda9ef8b36a2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPKkAduuygNtnxbmc8K8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W12kcAsxm6TarwkkuYSNMH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np=\"CLAUDE.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor = \"\"\"- `entire brain recall \"<question>\"`       prior decisions, rejected approaches, invariants.\n  **This, not `query`** — recall ranks decisions first; query mixes in docs and history and can\n  rank a design doc above the decision that overruled it.\"\"\"\nassert s.count(anchor)==1, \"anchor not found\"\nadded = anchor + \"\"\"\n\n**Always pass `--branch main` to `recall` and `brief` from a worktree.** Facts are\npartitioned per branch and a branch's file is a fork-time copy, so a recall from a\nfeature branch returns **0 rows silently** — measured 2026-10-25 on `tmp/integ6`:\none query gave 0 rows on the branch and 10 with `--branch main`. There is no warning;\n`brain status` only hints at it through a `missing_branches` array. Treat any empty\nbrain answer as the wrong partition FIRST and re-query with `--branch main` before\nconcluding nothing is recorded. This is not hypothetical: it hid a fact reading\n\"FOUR readers ... call readHistorySessionInventoryFile, not three\" while a #483 fix\nwas being written on the premise that there were three, which a reviewer then had to\ncatch. Rows also arrive with duplicates (10 rows, 3-6 distinct), so dedup before\njudging how much came back.\"\"\"\ns = s.replace(anchor, added)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"CLAUDE.md updated\")\nPY\ngrep -n \"Always pass \\`--branch main\\`\" CLAUDE.md","description":"Record the rule in the loaded project guidance"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1168,"cache_read_input_tokens":332376,"output_tokens":632,"outp