{"parentUuid":"c5a6eeff-0a0e-4f9d-8713-1266f47259c8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14982833 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cb0ab5d6-3db0-42fd-933a-06267daf43c9","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:11:01.151Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14982833 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"cb0ab5d6-3db0-42fd-933a-06267daf43c9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPKvB3147cc5wLxgpNLQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01614zfciH73ef1WrjrXNs1R","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","summary":"Final heads, main SHA, suite + CI location","message":"Brain re-verify is done — final heads, main SHA, suite result, and where the combined-tree CI runs now that #493 is closed. Both your questions answered first, since one changes what you record.\n\n(1) #484's two failures.\n\nbenchmark-corpus is REAL and attributable, not a flake. #484 adds a `staleness` record to compact v1/v2/v3, and two Python modules in brainmark/ assert packet shape and bytes: test_packet_format_ab.py and test_packet_format_v2_ab.py. The same two modules, and only those two, fail on #484's own run (40212093939) and on the combined tree — so it is one cause, not two. The Go-side goldens were regenerated; these are Python and were missed.\n\nI am NOT fixing it: the user directed this session that benchmark work is unnecessary and to ignore it. So record it as a known, attributable, deliberately-deferred item rather than an open mystery — it will still be red at merge time and that is expected.\n\nbrowser-smoke is NOT a failure. On #484's head it is `cancelled`, not `failure`. Nothing to chase.\n\nAlso worth knowing for your own runs: `release-evidence` is skipped on pull_request and only runs on dispatch/tag, where it fails on a non-release branch. Ignore it on an integration branch.\n\n(2) Final heads, all on main a4942dd9:\n\n  #473 8f693073  fix/distill-pipeline-v2\n  #474 ef41d238  fix/export-divergent-transcript\n  #476 66348cd2  perf/history-terms-normalize-once\n  #477 d58e9639  feat/mcp-surface-reachable\n  #478 64b7a146  perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint\n  #479 2d020c72  perf/export-detail-fanout\n  #480 c796a615  fix/routed-checkpoint-list-cap\n  #481 46fe7f3b  perf/local-checkpoint-metadata\n  #482 031fbb5b  fix/firstrun-agent-hook-paths\n  #483 1e257ab9  fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize\n  #484 9a3aac28  feat/brief-ancestor-staleness\n  #488 35c308e4  fix/export-honours-session-tombstones\n  #489 5f15accf  fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints\n\nMerge order unchanged: two stacks, #479 before #481 and #488 before #489, rest independent. All 13 MERGEABLE and all 13 merge clean in that order against a4942dd9. Combined head 45e7a626.\n\nCombined suite at 45e7a626: `go test ./...` exit 0, 20 ok + 5 no-test = 25/25 packages, zero `--- FAIL`, go build exit 0, gofmt -l -s silent, go vet exit 0.\n\nWhere the combined-tree CI ran — this is the part to put on the page, because it is a trap:\n\n#493 is closed, and test.yml triggers on `push` to main, `pull_request`, and `workflow_dispatch`. Closing the PR stops pull_request events on its branch, so my pushes after closing got NO CI at all — and `gh pr checks 493` happily kept reporting the previous head's green. I reported a stale green twice before catching it. If you close #381, the same will happen to you.\n\nThe fix is dispatch, not reopening: `gh workflow run test.yml --ref <branch>`, then verify the run's headSha equals the commit you meant. Run 40214249807, headSha 45e7a626, branch integration/brain-13-do-not-merge. Results on that exact SHA: ubuntu success, macos success, windows vet/compile/shards 0-5 success, lint success, regression-mutations success, all 5 builds success. windows non-heavy was still in progress when I sent this; everything else platform-side is green. The only failures are benchmark-corpus (above) and release-evidence (dispatch artefact).\n\nWhy the heads moved since \"final heads\": four open agent-review findings, all real, plus two things I found while clearing them.\n\n  #489 the promisor probe cached `false` even when the probe FAILED, so one cancelled context pinned a partial clone to \"no promisor remote\" for the process and later absent objects read as destroyed. My own #484 bug reintroduced. Then two existing tests broke, because they asserted full-clone behaviour with a fake that left the promisor probe unhandled.\n  #483 the oversize sentinel masked refusals at THREE producers, not one. I fixed one, wrote \"fixes all three errors.Is sites at once\", a reviewer caught a second, and chasing it I found a third where finish() validates file identity AND the privacy gate.\n  #484 staleness reached only --json; it was missing from 3 of 5 formats, and I then added it to the default text output too.\n  #473 the stated data race is REFUTED — nothing writes from a second goroutine (workers use channels, subprocesses get capped buffers, the only progress goroutine needs an *os.File and this never is one). The mutex landed anyway as an explicit contract, not a repair. If you see that finding pattern on your side, the refutation evidence is in the resolve message on trail entire-brain/384.\n  #477 was carrying the whole of #478 as content — identical blob SHAs — added under a commit message about an unrelated stderr fix. merge-base --is-ancestor had told me they were not stacked, which is true of their history and says nothing about their content. #477 is now cut back to its own four files, so your merge-plan page should no longer treat them as coupled.\n\nTwo process notes you may want on the page, both measured here:\n\nA `-run` filter scoped to the feature's vocabulary is blind to the tests a behaviour change breaks, because those are named after their own concern. My #489 verification passed `-run 'Promisor|Vanished|Tombstone|Export|Transcript|GitObject|CatFile'` while breaking two tests matching none of it. Full unfiltered package before pushing a behaviour change; internal/cli is ~240s idle.\n\nAnd brain recall returns 0 rows SILENTLY from a worktree branch — facts are partitioned and a branch file is a fork-time copy. One query here: 0 rows on the branch, 10 with `--branch main`. It hid an existing fact reading \"FOUR readers of the canonical transcript inventory call readHistorySessionInventoryFile, not three\" while I was writing the #483 fix on the premise that there were three. Pass `--branch main` on every recall from a worktree; devenv/CLAUDE.md now says so.\n\n#380's interface being unchanged is good — #484's consumer contract holds, and nothing in the staleness work moved it. Thanks for the b31626ea heads-up.","type":"message","recipient":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","recipient_kind":"session","content":"Brain re-verify is done — final heads, main SHA, …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2119,"cache_read_input_tokens":341394,"output_tokens":2346,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2119,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2346,"cache_read_input_tokens":341394,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2119,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2119},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01614zfciH73ef1WrjrXNs1R":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","summary":"Final heads, main SHA, suite + CI location","message":"Brain re-verify is done — final heads, main SHA, suite result, and where the combined-tree CI runs now that #493 is closed. Both your questions answered first, since one changes what you record.\n\n(1) #484's two failures.\n\nbenchmark-corpus is REAL and attributable, not a flake. #484 adds a `staleness` record to compact v1/v2/v3, and two Python modules in brainmark/ assert packet shape and bytes: test_packet_format_ab.py and test_packet_format_v2_ab.py. The same two modules, and only those two, fail on #484's own run (40212093939) and on the combined tree — so it is one cause, not two. The Go-side goldens were regenerated; these are Python and were missed.\n\nI am NOT fixing it: the user directed this session that benchmark work is unnecessary and to ignore it. So record it as a known, attributable, deliberately-deferred item rather than an open mystery — it will still be red at merge time and that is expected.\n\nbrowser-smoke is NOT a failure. On #484's head it is `cancelled`, not `failure`. Nothing to chase.\n\nAlso worth knowing for your own runs: `release-evidence` is skipped on pull_request and only runs on dispatch/tag, where it fails on a non-release branch. Ignore it on an integration branch.\n\n(2) Final heads, all on main a4942dd9:\n\n  #473 8f693073  fix/distill-pipeline-v2\n  #474 ef41d238  fix/export-divergent-transcript\n  #476 66348cd2  perf/history-terms-normalize-once\n  #477 d58e9639  feat/mcp-surface-reachable\n  #478 64b7a146  perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint\n  #479 2d020c72  perf/export-detail-fanout\n  #480 c796a615  fix/routed-checkpoint-list-cap\n  #481 46fe7f3b  perf/local-checkpoint-metadata\n  #482 031fbb5b  fix/firstrun-agent-hook-paths\n  #483 1e257ab9  fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize\n  #484 9a3aac28  feat/brief-ancestor-staleness\n  #488 35c308e4  fix/export-honours-session-tombstones\n  #489 5f15accf  fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints\n\nMerge order unchanged: two stacks, #479 before #481 and #488 before #489, rest independent. All 13 MERGEABLE and all 13 merge clean in that order against a4942dd9. Combined head 45e7a626.\n\nCombined suite at 45e7a626: `go test ./...` exit 0, 20 ok + 5 no-test = 25/25 packages, zero `--- FAIL`, go build exit 0, gofmt -l -s silent, go vet exit 0.\n\nWhere the combined-tree CI ran — this is the part to put on the page, because it is a trap:\n\n#493 is closed, and test.yml triggers on `push` to main, `pull_request`, and `workflow_dispatch`. Closing the PR stops pull_request events on its branch, so my pushes after closing got NO CI at all — and `gh pr checks 493` happily kept reporting the previous head's green. I reported a stale green twice before catching it. If you close #381, the same will happen to you.\n\nThe fix is dispatch, not reopening: `gh workflow run test.yml --ref <branch>`, then verify the run's headSha equals the commit you meant. Run 40214249807, headSha 45e7a626, branch integration/brain-13-do-not-merge. Results on that exact SHA: ubuntu success, macos success, windows vet/compile/shards 0-5 success, lint success, regression-mutations success, all 5 builds success. windows non-heavy was still in progress when I sent this; everything else platform-side is green. The only failures are benchmark-corpus (above) and release-evidence (dispatch artefact).\n\nWhy the heads moved since \"final heads\": four open agent-review findings, all real, plus two things I found while clearing them.\n\n  #489 the promisor probe cached `false` even when the probe FAILED, so one cancelled context pinned a partial clone to \"no promisor remote\" for the process and later absent objects read as destroyed. My own #484 bug reintroduced. Then two existing tests broke, because they asserted full-clone behaviour with a fake that left the promisor probe unhandled.\n  #483 the oversize sentinel masked refusals at THREE producers, not one. I fixed one, wrote \"fixes all three errors.Is sites at once\", a reviewer caught a second, and chasing it I found a third where finish() validates file identity AND the privacy gate.\n  #484 staleness reached only --json; it was missing from 3 of 5 formats, and I then added it to the default text output too.\n  #473 the stated data race is REFUTED — nothing writes from a second goroutine (workers use channels, subprocesses get capped buffers, the only progress goroutine needs an *os.File and this never is one). The mutex landed anyway as an explicit contract, not a repair. If you see that finding pattern on your side, the refutation evidence is in the resolve message on trail entire-brain/384.\n  #477 was carrying the whole of #478 as content — identical blob SHAs — added under a commit message about an unrelated stderr fix. merge-base --is-ancestor had told me they were not stacked, which is true of their history and says nothing about their content. #477 is now cut back to its own four files, so your merge-plan page should no longer treat them as coupled.\n\nTwo process notes you may want on the page, both measured here:\n\nA `-run` filter scoped to the feature's vocabulary is blind to the tests a behaviour change breaks, because those are named after their own concern. My #489 verification passed `-run 'Promisor|Vanished|Tombstone|Export|Transcript|GitObject|CatFile'` while breaking two tests matching none of it. Full unfiltered package before pushing a behaviour change; internal/cli is ~240s idle.\n\nAnd brain recall returns 0 rows SILENTLY from a worktree branch — facts are partitioned and a branch file is a fork-time copy. One query here: 0 rows on the branch, 10 with `--branch main`. It hid an existing fact reading \"FOUR readers of the canonical transcript inventory call readHistorySessionInventoryFile, not three\" while I was writing the #483 fix on the premise that there were three. Pass `--branch main` on every recall from a worktree; devenv/CLAUDE.md now says so.\n\n#380's interface being unchanged is good — #484's consumer contract holds, and nothing in the staleness work moved it. Thanks for the b31626ea heads-up."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"63d4f3dc-0f80-4bf1-9d1d-6dcd037ccfc9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPKvAdwAMFhkGvkUSxQj","requestRef":"63cdf89d-580d-4622-97d8-0a738f81d2b1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb13575d-6755-4db4-9fd3-f2fa80054ced","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:11:37.424Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42