{"parentUuid":"b953af25-5238-43a5-87db-2ca408a03ce0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPL9xT6oEh1pj6HEAZ5e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qs1kH16Yuqjk5bK81U8pr4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv && python3 - <<'PY'\np=\"BRAIN-HANDOFF-STATE.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nimport re\nheads = {\n \"473\":\"8f693073\",\"474\":\"ef41d238\",\"476\":\"66348cd2\",\"477\":\"d58e9639\",\"478\":\"64b7a146\",\n \"479\":\"2d020c72\",\"480\":\"c796a615\",\"481\":\"46fe7f3b\",\"482\":\"031fbb5b\",\"483\":\"1e257ab9\",\n \"484\":\"9a3aac28\",\"488\":\"35c308e4\",\"489\":\"5f15accf\"}\n# Replace the heads table wholesale with a current one.\nstart = s.index(\"| PR | branch | head |\")\nend = s.index(\"Merge order and the two stacks\")\ntable = \"\"\"| PR | branch | head | note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #473 | fix/distill-pipeline-v2 | `8f693073` | writer concurrency contract |\n| #474 | fix/export-divergent-transcript | `ef41d238` | |\n| #476 | perf/history-terms-normalize-once | `66348cd2` | |\n| #477 | feat/mcp-surface-reachable | `d58e9639` | #478's feature stripped out |\n| #478 | perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint | `64b7a146` | |\n| #479 | perf/export-detail-fanout | `2d020c72` | merge before #481 |\n| #480 | fix/routed-checkpoint-list-cap | `c796a615` | |\n| #481 | perf/local-checkpoint-metadata | `46fe7f3b` | stacked on #479 |\n| #482 | fix/firstrun-agent-hook-paths | `031fbb5b` | |\n| #483 | fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize | `1e257ab9` | sentinel masking at 3 producers |\n| #484 | feat/brief-ancestor-staleness | `9a3aac28` | staleness in all 5 formats |\n| #488 | fix/export-honours-session-tombstones | `35c308e4` | merge before #489 |\n| #489 | fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints | `5f15accf` | promisor probe + fixtures |\n\n**Combined tree `45e7a626` on `main@a4942dd9`:** all 13 merge clean in order; `go test ./...`\nexit 0, 25/25 packages, zero `--- FAIL`; build, gofmt and vet clean. CI via\n**`workflow_dispatch` run 40214249807** (headSha verified): ubuntu, macos, windows\nvet/compile/shards 0-5, lint, regression-mutations and all five builds green.\n\n**Two reds that are expected, not regressions.** `benchmark-corpus` fails because #484's new\n`staleness` record changes the compact packet, and two Python modules in `brainmark/`\n(`test_packet_format_ab.py`, `test_packet_format_v2_ab.py`) assert packet shape and bytes. You\ndirected that benchmark work is unnecessary, so it is deliberately not fixed. `release-evidence`\nruns only on dispatch/tag and fails on any non-release branch.\n\n**The closed-PR CI trap, worth knowing before you merge.** `test.yml` fires on push-to-main,\n`pull_request` and `workflow_dispatch`. Closing #493 stopped `pull_request` events on its\nbranch, so later pushes got no CI at all while `gh pr checks 493` kept reporting the PREVIOUS\nhead's green. Use `gh workflow run test.yml --ref <branch>` and verify the run's `headSha`.\n\n\"\"\"\ns = s[:start] + table + s[end:]\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"handoff updated\")\nPY\ngrep -c \"\" BRAIN-HANDOFF-STATE.md; grep -n \"45e7a626\\|1e257ab9\" BRAIN-HANDOFF-STATE.md | head -4","description":"Update the handoff doc with final heads and CI"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1364,"cache_read_input_tokens":348427,"output_tokens":1398,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1364,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1398,"cache_read_input_tokens":348427,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1364},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit