{"parentUuid":"37c8726d-521b-44c4-827d-d08eb144b221","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPLEZyNu4eM1c69h5TqJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":353327,"output_tokens":2038,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1005},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2038,"cache_read_input_tokens":353327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":14780,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"4c0bc8a7-503f-42f9-bf96-764954e6a022","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPLEZcYyYiL2HvgFxW6f","requestRef":"155f5e69-3d01-46c6-8354-ff294f06510b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"3742d548-8116-4c49-8414-098b4ada5128","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:15:26.704Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"3742d548-8116-4c49-8414-098b4ada5128","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPLEZyNu4eM1c69h5TqJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Benchmark is dropped entirely — not investigating, not reporting on it again.\n\n## Performance upgrades, with the measured numbers\n\n| | what was wrong | measured |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#481** | every export asked Entire about each checkpoint via its own subprocess | **97.7% of child processes removed.** Local union snapshot: 5,587 checkpoints / 2,505 sessions in **5.4s**, discovery 3.2s. At ~1.5s per child that's ~2½ hours of subprocesses gone |\n| **#479** | those remaining details were read strictly one at a time | **25.1s → 13.6s** at concurrency 4; best 12.6s at 8. Child start-up is only 22ms, so the win is real work, not spawn overhead |\n| **#478** | one global fact fingerprint, so a single `brain remember` on **any** branch re-indexed **every** session — \"even for byte-identical transcripts\" | **~18.7s rebuild eliminated per refresh**, and it ran *inside the readers' lock*, so a concurrent `brief` failed `brain_locked` at ~10.5s. The watch daemon triggers refresh every tick |\n| **#476** | history search terms re-normalised once per candidate instead of once per call | at 2,000 candidates: **1,368,853 → 140,223 (9.8×)**, memory **1,542,868 → 67,128 (23×)**, allocations **401 → 17**. The whole history step shows −40%, diluted by other work |\n\n**#479 + #481 together** take `cli`'s re-index from **~2.4 hours to ~70s**. That's the headline number.\n\nOne honest cost on the other side: #473 adds a mutex to the watch log writer — one uncontended atomic per line on a logging path.\n\n## Am I done, and is merging all that's left?\n\n**Not quite, and I won't round up.** One thing is genuinely open: `test (windows-latest) / non-heavy packages` has now run ~14 minutes against ~3m on the earlier run, and still hasn't reported. I flagged why that worries me — #473's new mutex is held across the sink write, and a hang is precisely the shape that produces. A watcher is on it. If it doesn't land I'll chase the deadlock hypothesis; I'm not signing this off on \"probably a slow runner\".\n\nEverything else is done and verified on the exact SHA: 13 PRs, all MERGEABLE, clean in merge order on `main@a4942dd9`, combined tree 25/25 packages, and CI green on ubuntu / macos / all six Windows shards / lint / mutations / all five builds.\n\nAnd **merging isn't all that's left on your side** — three of your five items aren't merges:\n\n1. Approve the 13 *(a merge, yes)*\n2. **Transcript mode** — spends money on a corpus-wide re-distill\n3. **37 GB store delete** — irreversible\n4. **Linear connector** — account-side, re-add in claude.ai → Connectors\n5. `/compact`\n\nSo: engineering finished bar that one Windows job, and what remains for you is one merge decision plus three calls only you can make."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":353327,"output_tokens":2038,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1005},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2038,"cache_read_input_tokens":353327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":955},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4c0bc8a7-503f-42f9-bf96-764954e6a022","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPLEZcYyYiL2HvgFxW6f","requestRef":"155f5e69-3d01-46c6-8354-ff294f06510b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"6321265b-e931-4526-ad45-6e0