{"parentUuid":"dee8dc79-3131-4c5a-a042-737c6e06451c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPLPAUm2kA9gJTpaL5ve","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":906,"cache_read_input_tokens":359704,"output_tokens":2658,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1492},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":906,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2658,"cache_read_input_tokens":359704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":906},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":20937,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"0c809ce5-c7e0-4475-a20f-c274ca91c267","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPLPAAQu2ozgR7koDxqF","requestRef":"029749d6-6f40-4ccb-8795-5b8e638e860a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"c362b436-e60f-4b11-93c4-567444ab62c1","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:17:29.522Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"c362b436-e60f-4b11-93c4-567444ab62c1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPLPAUm2kA9gJTpaL5ve","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hang hypothesis **retired by evidence, not by waiting**: `run_other.py` runs \"every target-Windows package outside the compiled shard set\", and `internal/cli` — where #473's mutex lives — is heavy, so it runs in the shards. All six shards passed. The job has a 40-minute timeout and is simply slow; nothing of mine is unexercised.\n\n## How the gains were obtained, and did quality drop?\n\n**No — and in one case I refused a bigger speedup to avoid it.**\n\n**#476 is pure hoisting.** The normalisation was recomputed per candidate; it's now computed once per call. Identical results, asserted: `TestHistoryTermsIsByteIdenticalAfterHoisting`, plus `TestNormalizedHistoryTermCandidatesStayAligned` holding the arrays in step and `TestHistoryTermsRawArmIsRedundant` proving the arm I removed was genuinely redundant.\n\n**#478 removed over-invalidation, not work that mattered.** Episodes are linked from `factsByBranch[s.Branch]`, so a fact on branch X can *never* enrich a session on branch Y — the single global fingerprint was strictly more conservative than the actual data dependency. `TestFactOnABranchStillReindexesThatBranchsSessions` proves invalidation still fires where it must. **And this is where I declined the bigger win:** building outside the brain lock and swapping would have removed the ~18.7s from the lock entirely, but it would have retired `TestPatternCorpusBuildCannotPublishAfterTombstoneLinearizes` — a privacy invariant that a tombstone cannot linearize mid-publish. Rewriting a privacy test so a performance change passes is the move that looks green and removes a guarantee, so I left the lock alone and put the decision in your hands instead.\n\n**#479 is concurrency only.** Same subprocesses, same data, bounded fanout. No semantic change.\n\n**#481 is the one that deserves scrutiny**, because it genuinely changes where data comes from — the local checkpoint store instead of asking Entire. The protection is that an incomplete local catalog **refuses** rather than publishing a smaller corpus, and that guard is exactly what two of the other PRs harden: #480 (the routed list silently capping at 100 and calling itself complete) and #489 (telling an unfetched object apart from a deleted one). The speed came from skipping *metadata* fetches, not from trusting less.\n\nNow running the review pass over all 13 before merging."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":906,"cache_read_input_tokens":359704,"output_tokens":2658,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1492},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":906,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2658,"cache_read_input_tokens":359704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":906},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0c809ce5-c7e0-4475-a20f-c274ca91c267","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPLPAAQu2ozgR7koDxqF","requestRef":"029749d6-6f40-4ccb-8795-5b8e638e860a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f0cec52-812d-4651-bfe0-57a660de0b4a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:17:39.643Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discover