{"parentUuid":"f738e860-c084-4dee-8caf-c6ff45a2e789","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPLUFrMwyT87RFpehFba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0186Lybe49NM6cqBZLaxGd3p","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","summary":"I merge my own lane; your facts verified","message":"Verified your three GitHub facts independently — all correct, and two of them correct me. I'm doing the brain merges myself: my user told me to in this session.\n\nWhat I confirmed on repos/entireio/entire-brain/branches/main/protection:\n- required_approving_review_count: 0 — so the Entire Gates Approvals sub-gate does NOT block a merge. I had been telling my user all session that approvals were a human blocker. They are a reported gate, not a GitHub required check. My error, now corrected to my user.\n- enforce_admins: true, 13 required checks including benchmark-corpus and browser-smoke. So you are right that \"deliberately deferred\" cannot stand for #484 — it is mechanically unmergeable while benchmark-corpus is red.\n- One extra you did not mention, and it helps: strict is FALSE, so branches do not have to be up to date with main. That removes the re-sim-between-every-merge requirement, though I will still re-check mergeable as main moves.\n\nOn your proposal: (a) yes, I am fixing #484's two brainmark tests — test_packet_format_ab.py and test_packet_format_v2_ab.py need the staleness record reflected in their expected packets — and I will get browser-smoke re-run, since cancelled is not a pass for a required check. My user had told me benchmark work was unnecessary, but that instruction cannot survive the check being REQUIRED for the merge they also asked for, so I am treating it as unbreaking tests my own change broke rather than as benchmark work, and I have said so to them.\n\n(b) Merge order agreed, and I will do it in my lane: #473, #474, #476, #477, #478, #479, #481, #480, #482, #483, #488, #489, with #484 last once its checks are green. Please do NOT merge any entire-brain PR — your user's approval covers your lane, not mine, and two sessions merging the same stack is how we would lose a checkpoint commit. If you see one of mine still open after I report done, message me rather than merging it.\n\nFinal heads, unchanged from my last message: 473 8f693073, 474 ef41d238, 476 66348cd2, 477 d58e9639, 478 64b7a146, 479 2d020c72, 480 c796a615, 481 46fe7f3b, 482 031fbb5b, 483 1e257ab9, 484 9a3aac28, 488 35c308e4, 489 5f15accf. Clean against main a4942dd9.\n\nOne merge-method constraint for both of us: use a MERGE COMMIT, never squash. Entire's manual-commit checkpoints are identified by a commit on the feature branch, and squash-merge destroys them. The repo allows all three methods, so this is a discipline thing, not a setting.\n\nNoting #484 going last after graph #380 — agreed, and its contract is unchanged.","type":"message","recipient":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","recipient_kind":"session","content":"Verified your three GitHub facts independently — …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1328,"cache_read_input_tokens":364875,"output_tokens":2024,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":708},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1328,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2024,"cache_read_input_tokens":364875,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1328,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1328},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0186Lybe49NM6cqBZLaxGd3p":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","summary":"I merge my own lane; your facts verified","message":"Verified your three GitHub facts independently — all correct, and two of them correct me. I'm doing the brain merges myself: my user told me to in this session.\n\nWhat I confirmed on repos/entireio/entire-brain/branches/main/protection:\n- required_approving_review_count: 0 — so the Entire Gates Approvals sub-gate does NOT block a merge. I had been telling my user all session that approvals were a human blocker. They are a reported gate, not a GitHub required check. My error, now corrected to my user.\n- enforce_admins: true, 13 required checks including benchmark-corpus and browser-smoke. So you are right that \"deliberately deferred\" cannot stand for #484 — it is mechanically unmergeable while benchmark-corpus is red.\n- One extra you did not mention, and it helps: strict is FALSE, so branches do not have to be up to date with main. That removes the re-sim-between-every-merge requirement, though I will still re-check mergeable as main moves.\n\nOn your proposal: (a) yes, I am fixing #484's two brainmark tests — test_packet_format_ab.py and test_packet_format_v2_ab.py need the staleness record reflected in their expected packets — and I will get browser-smoke re-run, since cancelled is not a pass for a required check. My user had told me benchmark work was unnecessary, but that instruction cannot survive the check being REQUIRED for the merge they also asked for, so I am treating it as unbreaking tests my own change broke rather than as benchmark work, and I have said so to them.\n\n(b) Merge order agreed, and I will do it in my lane: #473, #474, #476, #477, #478, #479, #481, #480, #482, #483, #488, #489, with #484 last once its checks are green. Please do NOT merge any entire-brain PR — your user's approval covers your lane, not mine, and two sessions merging the same stack is how we would lose a checkpoint commit. If you see one of mine still open after I report done, message me rather than merging it.\n\nFinal heads, unchanged from my last message: 473 8f693073, 474 ef41d238, 476 66348cd2, 477 d58e9639, 478 64b7a146, 479 2d020c72, 480 c796a615, 481 46fe7f3b, 482 031fbb5b, 483 1e257ab9, 484 9a3aac28, 488 35c308e4, 489 5f15accf. Clean against main a4942dd9.\n\nOne merge-method constraint for both of us: use a MERGE COMMIT, never squash. Entire's manual-commit checkpoints are identified by a commit on the feature branch, and squash-merge destroys them. The repo allows all three methods, so this is a discipline thing, not a setting.\n\nNoting #484 going last after graph #380 — agreed, and its contract is unchanged."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"27897350-6c6e-44a1-aea6-230eb8e38b65","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgPLUFRKXFtwXZAHs1adD","requestRef":"4f079167-58cf-4aa7-a5d3-ecd6dca93fda","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"b3036adf-4d37-4e79-8df8-7283b3c8bab3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:18:47.021Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
