{"parentUuid":"6a753f53-9020-4e69-860a-866f5810cf9c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPLjgXqgzvXtQUim41pR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011UWTHVdhutgYaBnCxyEgVN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"set -- \\\n\"388:01M5QWT2Y3Q1NPQF0WABZWA3XV:Fixed at d58e9639. readMCPFrame now bounds the length before allocating: mcp_reachability.go:258 refuses when length > maxMCPFrameBytes, reusing the same 4 MiB ceiling readMCPMessage already enforces rather than inventing a second one. A negative length is reported as its own error instead of being misreported as a missing Content-Length header. Proved by weakening: disabling the cap turns TestMCPProbeRefusesAnOversizedFrameInsteadOfAllocatingIt into a named --- FAIL with the package still compiling, and the test drives maxMCPFrameBytes+1, maxMCPFrameBytes*4 and math.MaxInt so the cap's ORDER is load-bearing, not just its presence.\" \\\n\"388:01M5QM1M0BN3SC4PKVF3H88V7E:Duplicate of 01M5QWT2Y3Q1NPQF0WABZWA3XV and fixed by the same change at d58e9639 (mcp_reachability.go:258, bounded by maxMCPFrameBytes, weakening-proved). Resolving rather than dismissing: the finding is correct, it is simply the same defect reported twice.\" \\\n\"388:01M5QM1KZVGFJ7DM0JW7BD4M39:Fixed at d58e9639. The probe binary is injected rather than taken from os.Executable(): see the comment at mcp_reachability.go:297 stating that under go test os.Executable() IS the test binary, and the exePath seam at :317. doctorMCPSurfaceCheck (:310) is a second seam so a test can prove doctor actually calls the check, which closed a separate hole where unwiring the check from doctor left every test in the file green.\" \\\n\"394:01M5R8FS7JTPNVC51KW08V9VFT:Fixed and then hardened. shortTermCanonicalInputRefusal in history_delta.go classifies errHistoryTranscriptTooLarge as NOT a refusal, so one oversize transcript costs its own session and the overlay publishes for every other one, with the file carried in the delta's FailedFiles channel so no surface claims complete coverage. Hardened at 1e257ab9 after a later review: the sentinel check now runs AFTER every other refusal reason, because readers return errors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr) and asking about the sentinel first answered skip for a whole join that also carried a degraded inventory or a cancelled context. Weakening-proved both ways.\" \\\n\"395:01M5RFGAVDQ27D4PMQ0AG9CV49:Fixed at 9a3aac28. probeGraphAncestorSupport (graph_context.go:367) now returns (supported, definitive) and only a definitive answer is stored (:330-335): a host-verb rejection is definitive, while a timeout, a cancelled context, a spawn failure or malformed JSON is not and is retried. Same bug class as the promisor probe on #489, which is where I found I had reintroduced it.\" \\\n\"395:01M5R9TCX0J1JRWQ4MSCSJAXN5:Fixed at 9a3aac28, and your reading of the contract is what the fix is built on. Unreliable is structurally empty in the common incomplete case, so it cannot carry the signal alone. semanticContextStaleness now also carries ExcludedRecords (agent_surface.go:315, with the reasoning in the comment above it): empty Unreliable with a non-zero count means nothing RETURNED is tainted but records are missing, which is the state a reader must not mistake for completeness. ChangedFiles is emitted alongside it as the negative-suppression set in all five output formats - --json, compact v1/v2/v3, and the default text renderer at agent_surface.go:1997, which was silent until this fix.\" \\\n; for spec in \"$@\"; do t=${spec%%:*}; rest=${spec#*:}; id=${rest%%:*}; msg=${rest#*:}; printf \"trail %s %s -> \" \"$t\" \"${id: -6}\"; entire trail finding resolve \"$id\" --trail \"entire-brain/$t\" -m \"$msg\" 2>&1 | tail -1; done","description":"Resolve the six verified-stale findings"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2837,"cache_read_input_tokens":383379,"output_tokens":2044,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":479},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2837,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2044,"cache_read_input_tokens":383379,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2837,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2837},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011UWTHVdhutgYaBnCxyEgVN":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach && set -- \\\n\"388:01M5QWT2Y3Q1NPQF0WABZWA3XV:Fixed at d58e9639. readMCPFrame now bounds the length before allocating: mcp_reachability.go:258 refuses when length > maxMCPFrameBytes, reusing the same 4 MiB ceiling readMCPMessage already enforces rather than inventing a second one. A negative length is reported as its own error instead of being misreported as a missing Content-Length header. Proved by weakening: disabling the cap turns TestMCPProbeRefusesAnOversizedFrameInsteadOfAllocatingIt into a named --- FAIL with the package still compiling, and the test drives maxMCPFrameBytes+1, maxMCPFrameBytes*4 and math.MaxInt so the cap's ORDER is load-bearing, not just its presence.\" \\\n\"388:01M5QM1M0BN3SC4PKVF3H88V7E:Duplicate of 01M5QWT2Y3Q1NPQF0WABZWA3XV and fixed by the same change at d58e9639 (mcp_reachability.go:258, bounded by maxMCPFrameBytes, weakening-proved). Resolving rather than dismissing: the finding is correct, it is simply the same defect reported twice.\" \\\n\"388:01M5QM1KZVGFJ7DM0JW7BD4M39:Fixed at d58e9639. The probe binary is injected rather than taken from os.Executable(): see the comment at mcp_reachability.go:297 stating that under go test os.Executable() IS the test binary, and the exePath seam at :317. doctorMCPSurfaceCheck (:310) is a second seam so a test can prove doctor actually calls the check, which closed a separate hole where unwiring the check from doctor left every test in the file green.\" \\\n\"394:01M5R8FS7JTPNVC51KW08V9VFT:Fixed and then hardened. shortTermCanonicalInputRefusal in history_delta.go classifies errHistoryTranscriptTooLarge as NOT a refusal, so one oversize transcript costs its own session and the overlay publishes for every other one, with the file carried in the delta's FailedFiles channel so no surface claims complete coverage. Hardened at 1e257ab9 after a later review: the sentinel check now runs AFTER every other refusal reason, because readers return errors.Join(readErr, finishErr, closeErr) and asking about the sentinel first answered skip for a whole join that also carried a degraded inventory or a cancelled context. Weakening-proved both ways.\" \\\n\"395:01M5RFGAVDQ27D4PMQ0AG9CV49:Fixed at 9a3aac28. probeGraphAncestorSupport (graph_context.go:367) now returns (supported, definitive) and only a definitive answer is stored (:330-335): a host-verb rejection is definitive, while a timeout, a cancelled context, a spawn failure or malformed JSON is not and is retried. Same bug class as the promisor probe on #489, which is where I found I had reintroduced it.\" \\\n\"395:01M5R9TCX0J1JRWQ4MSCSJAXN5:Fixed at 9a3aac28, and your reading of the contract is what the fix is built on. Unreliable is structurally empty in the common incomplete case, so it cannot carry the signal alone. semanticContextStaleness now also carries ExcludedRecords (agent_surface.go:315, with the reasoning in the comment above it): empty Unreliable with a non-zero count means nothing RETURNED is tainted but records are missing, which is the state a reader must not mistake for completeness. ChangedFiles is emitted alongside it as the negative-suppression set in all five output formats - --json, compact v1/v2/v3, and the default text renderer at agent_surface.go:1997, which was silent until this fix.\" \\\n; for spec in \"$@\"; do t=${spec%%:*}; rest=${spec#*:}; id=${rest%%:*}; msg=${rest#*:}; printf \"trail %s %s -> \" \"$t\" \"${id: -6}\"; entire trail finding resolve \"$id\" --trail \"entire-brain/$t\" -m \"$msg\" 2>&1 | tail -1; done","description":"Resolve the six verified-stale findings"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_011UWTHVdhutgYaBnCxyEgVN":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7278f073-591a-4380-9dee-ab025ca939d1","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgPLjgCFgPterrJ25XXKn","requestRef":"f609c9d8-1c80-481a-97f3-c775238c5190","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"55d45210-b407-4edd-b76b-3682cac83c15","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:22:16.235Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
