{"parentUuid":"d3a156f2-b2c3-4a39-a2d2-1d5e69d6b3dc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPMU7UBzYSvy243a47p5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph just handed me the one test most likely to catch a mistake — `TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache`. Delegating the fix with everything established, including that trap."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1288,"cache_read_input_tokens":411408,"output_tokens":2937,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":248},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1288,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2937,"cache_read_input_tokens":411408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1288},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6a0b02ba-e376-4279-96a5-3194ad2cc565","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPMU74tRXckm7kHhCUip","requestRef":"ba0797b0-228d-409b-8ef6-2039c14830be","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"2096df76-6e74-4b72-b979-ca67158ef29d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:31:26.828Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"2096df76-6e74-4b72-b979-ca67158ef29d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPMU7UBzYSvy243a47p5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017ANxn1k7Qi6TPUwkYRZKCS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix 489 sweep retention hole","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix a CONFIRMED data-loss finding in entire-brain. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished (branch fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints, PR #489). Touch no other worktree or branch.\n\nCAVEMAN-ULTRA COMPRESSED OUTPUT. Use rtk for git/shell. Your tool output never reaches me, only your report — make it dense and factual. Note: the auto-mode classifier has been intermittently denying Bash in this worktree citing \"[Merge Without Review]\"; if that happens, retry the command on its own (a plain single-purpose command usually passes) and never work around it deviously. Do NOT merge anything, do not run `gh pr merge`.\n\nTHE FINDING (trail entire-brain/400, id 01M5SZBJYNDFFFHGF83D1DEXQR, medium), verbatim:\n\"Sessions skipped as unavailable are removed from `sessions` and `manifest.Sessions`. The comment above this code says the cache sweep retains cached transcripts based on that selection. If a skipped session has a cached transcript, it could be the only surviving copy once its checkpoint has vanished, and the sweep would then delete it. Keep skipped sessions in the retention list passed to the sweep, even though they are excluded from the manifest.\"\n\nI HAVE ALREADY CONFIRMED THE MECHANISM — do not re-derive it, verify my claims and build on them:\n- internal/cli/export.go ~line 355-405: `usable, unavailable, _ := partitionLocalTranscriptSessions(...)`; then a `surviving` list is built that keeps exempted (never-validated) + usable sessions and DROPS validated-and-unavailable ones; then `sessions = surviving; manifest.Sessions = sessions`.\n- internal/cli/export.go:425 calls `planTranscriptCacheSweep(ctx, opts.Runner, outputDir, repoDir)`.\n- internal/cli/transcript_cache_migration.go:18-110 is the sweep planner. It loads the manifest itself (`loadBrainManifest`), builds `sessions := historySessionByTranscriptPath(manifest)`, and at line ~57 does `if _, live := sessions[file.Rel]; !live { continue }`. A cached file whose session is NOT in the manifest is therefore never added to `retained`, and at line ~100 the `!retained` files become the returned sweep set (to be deleted).\n- So dropping a skipped session from manifest.Sessions marks its cached transcript for deletion. If the checkpoint is genuinely destroyed (which is exactly #489's case), that cache is the last copy.\n- The code's own comment at export.go ~367 already states the principle: \"An exempted session must SURVIVE: the cache sweep learns from this list which cached transcripts to retain, and that retention is what lets `privacy include` recover it.\"\n\nTHE TRAP — the naive fix is WRONG. Do not make `!live` files retain by default. `!live` ALSO covers sessions removed deliberately by `privacy exclude` / tombstones, whose caches MUST still be swept. There is an existing test for exactly that: `TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache` (internal/cli/transcript_bugbot_test.go:128). Read it FIRST and make sure you understand which side of the line it sits on. Breaking it, or making it vacuous, is a failure.\n\nTHE INTENDED FIX: thread the explicitly-skipped sessions' transcript paths through to the sweep as a retain-anyway set, so only those are rescued while genuinely-excluded sessions keep being swept. `partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` (internal/cli/transcript_store.go:465) returns `([]exportSession, []error, error)` — the []error carries diagnostics, NOT the skipped sessions, so collect the skipped sessions' transcript paths in export.go where `surviving` is computed (that code already has every session and the usable-key set). Confirm the path key shape matches what `historySessionByTranscriptPath(manifest)` keys on and what `inventory.files[].Rel` holds — a mismatch here silently rescues nothing, which would be the worst outcome because it looks fixed.\n\nIf after reading you conclude a different design is better, say so with evidence and implement that instead — but state plainly why.\n\nBLAST RADIUS, already measured with `entire graph impact --symbol planTranscriptCacheSweep`: 4 production callers, all reaching it via runExport (export.go:425, newExportCommand:125, runRefreshDeltaStats history_delta.go:998, runRefreshExportPhase refresh_phases.go:18), and 7 tests including the three named: TestTranscriptCacheSweepRejectsSymlinkedTranscript (export_test.go:2170), TestFilelessMigrationRetainsUnrecoverableCache (transcript_fileless_test.go:266), TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache (transcript_bugbot_test.go:128). Use `entire graph impact/neighbors --head` for anything else structural rather than grepping.\n\nMANDATORY VERIFICATION — report each command and its REAL result, never a result you did not observe:\n1. `go build ./...` exit 0.\n2. A test proving a skipped-as-unavailable session's cached transcript SURVIVES the sweep.\n3. A test proving a privacy-excluded session's cache is STILL swept (or confirm an existing one covers it and name it).\n4. WEAKENING PROOF for each: break the retention, confirm a NAMED `--- FAIL` with the test name, package still COMPILING. `[build failed]` is NOT a red — it greps as `^FAIL` but the test never ran; use `_ = x` for orphaned vars and grep `--- FAIL`. If a weakening does NOT produce a red, your test is passing for the wrong reason — say so and fix the test; this has already happened twice in this session.\n5. All 7 impact-named tests green.\n6. THE WHOLE PACKAGE UNFILTERED: `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m go test ./... -count=1`. Do not use a `-run` filter for the final run. A `-run` filter scoped to the feature's vocabulary already hid two breakages in this exact file earlier today — the tests a behaviour change breaks are named after THEIR concern, not yours.\n7. `$(go env GOROOT)/bin/gofmt -l -s .` silent (use the GOROOT gofmt, PATH's is older).\n8. `go vet ./...` exit 0, status captured directly to a file, never through a pipe.\n9. Commit (NO AI attribution footer, no Co-Authored-By — repo rule) and push to origin fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints. Report the head SHA.\n10. Resolve the finding: `entire trail finding resolve 01M5SZBJYNDFFFHGF83D1DEXQR --trail entire-brain/400 -m \"<evidence>\"` (id is POSITIONAL; there is no --finding flag and no --json on this subcommand).\n\nReport: did you confirm my mechanism (and any correction), what you changed, the exact weakening reds with test names, every verification result, the head SHA, and the resolve outcome. If something failed or you could not verify it, say so plainly."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1288,"cache_read_input_tokens":411408,"output_tokens":2937,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":248},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1288,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2937,"cache_read_input_tokens":411408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1288},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017ANxn1k7Qi6TPUwkYRZKCS":{"description":"Fix 489 sweep retention hole","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix a CONFIRMED data-loss finding in entire-brain. Work ONLY in worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished (branch fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints, PR #489). Touch no other worktree or branch.\n\nCAVEMAN-ULTRA COMPRESSED OUTPUT. Use rtk for git/shell. Your tool output never reaches me, only your report — make it dense and factual. Note: the auto-mode classifier has been intermittently denying Bash in this worktree citing \"[Merge Without Review]\"; if that happens, retry the command on its own (a plain single-purpose command usually passes) and never work around it deviously. Do NOT merge anything, do not run `gh pr merge`.\n\nTHE FINDING (trail entire-brain/400, id 01M5SZBJYNDFFFHGF83D1DEXQR, medium), verbatim:\n\"Sessions skipped as unavailable are removed from `sessions` and `manifest.Sessions`. The comment above this code says the cache sweep retains cached transcripts based on that selection. If a skipped session has a cached transcript, it could be the only surviving copy once its checkpoint has vanished, and the sweep would then delete it. Keep skipped sessions in the retention list passed to the sweep, even though they are excluded from the manifest.\"\n\nI HAVE ALREADY CONFIRMED THE MECHANISM — do not re-derive it, verify my claims and build on them:\n- internal/cli/export.go ~line 355-405: `usable, unavailable, _ := partitionLocalTranscriptSessions(...)`; then a `surviving` list is built that keeps exempted (never-validated) + usable sessions and DROPS validated-and-unavailable ones; then `sessions = surviving; manifest.Sessions = sessions`.\n- internal/cli/export.go:425 calls `planTranscriptCacheSweep(ctx, opts.Runner, outputDir, repoDir)`.\n- internal/cli/transcript_cache_migration.go:18-110 is the sweep planner. It loads the manifest itself (`loadBrainManifest`), builds `sessions := historySessionByTranscriptPath(manifest)`, and at line ~57 does `if _, live := sessions[file.Rel]; !live { continue }`. A cached file whose session is NOT in the manifest is therefore never added to `retained`, and at line ~100 the `!retained` files become the returned sweep set (to be deleted).\n- So dropping a skipped session from manifest.Sessions marks its cached transcript for deletion. If the checkpoint is genuinely destroyed (which is exactly #489's case), that cache is the last copy.\n- The code's own comment at export.go ~367 already states the principle: \"An exempted session must SURVIVE: the cache sweep learns from this list which cached transcripts to retain, and that retention is what lets `privacy include` recover it.\"\n\nTHE TRAP — the naive fix is WRONG. Do not make `!live` files retain by default. `!live` ALSO covers sessions removed deliberately by `privacy exclude` / tombstones, whose caches MUST still be swept. There is an existing test for exactly that: `TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache` (internal/cli/transcript_bugbot_test.go:128). Read it FIRST and make sure you understand which side of the line it sits on. Breaking it, or making it vacuous, is a failure.\n\nTHE INTENDED FIX: thread the explicitly-skipped sessions' transcript paths through to the sweep as a retain-anyway set, so only those are rescued while genuinely-excluded sessions keep being swept. `partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` (internal/cli/transcript_store.go:465) returns `([]exportSession, []error, error)` — the []error carries diagnostics, NOT the skipped sessions, so collect the skipped sessions' transcript paths in export.go where `surviving` is computed (that code already has every session and the usable-key set). Confirm the path key shape matches what `historySessionByTranscriptPath(manifest)` keys on and what `inventory.files[].Rel` holds — a mismatch here silently rescues nothing, which would be the worst outcome because it looks fixed.\n\nIf after reading you conclude a different design is better, say so with evidence and implement that instead — but state plainly why.\n\nBLAST RADIUS, already measured with `entire graph impact --symbol planTranscriptCacheSweep`: 4 production callers, all reaching it via runExport (export.go:425, newExportCommand:125, runRefreshDeltaStats history_delta.go:998, runRefreshExportPhase refresh_phases.go:18), and 7 tests including the three named: TestTranscriptCacheSweepRejectsSymlinkedTranscript (export_test.go:2170), TestFilelessMigrationRetainsUnrecoverableCache (transcript_fileless_test.go:266), TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache (transcript_bugbot_test.go:128). Use `entire graph impact/neighbors --head` for anything else structural rather than grepping.\n\nMANDATORY VERIFICATION — report each command and its REAL result, never a result you did not observe:\n1. `go build ./...` exit 0.\n2. A test proving a skipped-as-unavailable session's cached transcript SURVIVES the sweep.\n3. A test proving a privacy-excluded session's cache is STILL swept (or confirm an existing one covers it and name it).\n4. WEAKENING PROOF for each: break the retention, confirm a NAMED `--- FAIL` with the test name, package still COMPILING. `[build failed]` is NOT a red — it greps as `^FAIL` but the test never ran; use `_ = x` for orphaned vars and grep `--- FAIL`. If a weakening does NOT produce a red, your test is passing for the wrong reason — say so and fix the test; this has already happened twice in this session.\n5. All 7 impact-named tests green.\n6. THE WHOLE PACKAGE UNFILTERED: `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m go test ./... -count=1`. Do not use a `-run` filter for the final run. A `-run` filter scoped to the feature's vocabulary already hid two breakages in this exact file earlier today — the tests a behaviour change breaks are named after THEIR concern, not yours.\n7. `$(go env GOROOT)/bin/gofmt -l -s .` silent (use the GOROOT gofmt, PATH's is older).\n8. `go vet ./...` exit 0, status captured directly to a file, never through a pipe.\n9. Commit (NO AI attribution footer, no Co-Authored-By — repo rule) and push to origin fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints. Report the head SHA.\n10. Resolve the finding: `entire trail finding resolve 01M5SZBJYNDFFFHGF83D1DEXQR --trail entire-brain/400 -m \"<evidence>\"` (id is POSITIONAL; there is no --finding flag and no --json on this subcommand).\n\nReport: did you confirm my mechanism (and any correction), what you changed, the exact weakening reds with test names, every verification result, the head SHA, and the resolve outcome. If something failed or you could not verify it, say so plainly."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6a0b02ba-e376-4279-96a5-3194ad2cc565","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgPMU74tRXckm7kHhCUip","requestRef":"ba0797b0-228d-409b-8ef6-2039c14830be","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"dcb07656-4f81-4915-b4c8-57f306a3c0dd","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:31:59.568Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
