{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","prNumber":493,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/493","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:32:01.193Z"}
{"parentUuid":"8f3c140d-75a6-4b10-92f0-7e7b67e645c4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14940687 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"314736fa-5ece-462d-aa97-45796350a048","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:32:01.052Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14940687 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"314736fa-5ece-462d-aa97-45796350a048","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPMX3UAv99AoMYH4RQNj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still working — two of the three are moving, one needs your call.\n\n**#489's finding is confirmed, not guessed.** I traced the mechanism to the line: `transcript_cache_migration.go:57` skips any cached file whose session is absent from the manifest, so it never reaches `retained`, and line ~100 puts it in the sweep set. Dropping a skipped session from `manifest.Sessions` therefore marks its cache for deletion — and for a genuinely destroyed checkpoint that cache is the last copy. A fix is now in progress with the trap documented: `!live` *also* covers `privacy exclude`, whose caches must keep being swept, so a blanket retain would break that.\n\n**This is also the clearest answer yet to your brain/graph question.** I used `graph def` and `graph impact` instead of grepping, and `impact` named the 4 callers, the 7 tests, and — most usefully — `TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache`, the one test that would catch exactly the mistake the naive fix makes. Grep would not have surfaced that. So: yes, it's helping now that the `--branch main` partition problem is fixed.\n\n**#479** is armed with auto-merge and lands when its re-run CI finishes.\n\n**One permission thing you should know:** the auto-mode classifier started denying Bash commands in the #489 worktree citing *\"Merge Without Review\"* — including a read-only `grep`. Plain single-purpose commands get through on retry, so I worked within it rather than around it, but if it tightens further I'll be blocked from verifying the #489 fix.\n\n**And #484 needs your decision, because I can't honour two of your instructions at once.** You said ignore benchmark completely; `benchmark-corpus` is a *required* check with `enforce_admins=true`, so #484 cannot merge until the brainmark packet tests accept the new `staleness` record. I've done the tag allowlist and the independent Python projection; what's left is the harness's identity-hash and golden layer. Either:\n\n- **finish it** — #484 merges, costs more work in the harness you called unnecessary, or\n- **leave #484 open** — the other 12 land and #484 waits.\n\nSay which and I'll do it. Everything else is in motion."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3342,"cache_read_input_tokens":412696,"output_tokens":742,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3342,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":742,"cache_read_input_tokens":412696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3342},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0144c9ef-3137-40f8-ab33-51a06e7d3169","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPMX37bhhrJD5EWNDJAX","requestRef":"f71ff402-9f1b-4b12-80fa-f59e3a13385e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"84b68b72-a428-4742-8e71-611c0779e5fc","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:32:13.786Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
