ip a vacuous test). A session whose transcript path is absent from the catalog tip TREE never reaches partitionLocalTranscriptSessions at all: the snapshot loader drops it with `checkpoint_scope_incomplete: skipped unreadable local checkpoint bbb222bbb222 skipped 1 session metadata entries with no transcript bytes in refs/heads/entire/checkpoints/v1`. My first fixture had exactly that shape; the rescue set was empty and the test failed for the wrong reason. Only a **missing blob with an intact tree path** (hasSnapshotTranscript checks tree paths, not objects) reaches the per-session unavailability classification. The fixture now deletes the loose object `.git/objects/xx/yyy` after a real export has materialized the cache.\n  \n  CORRECTION 3 (the trap's rationale is wrong, though the narrow design is right). `!live` does NOT cover privacy-excluded/tombstoned sessions: those are exempt from validation and SURVIVE in manifest.Sessions, so they stay `live` and keep the full recovery proof. What `!live` actually covers is stale export leftovers. Consequence: the naive fix (retain every `!live` file) produces **no red** in the 21-test cache/export subset — TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache passes under it. I kept the narrow design anyway (retaining stale leftovers forever defeats \"Unlisted files are stale exports\"), but the guard you cited is not what stops the naive fix.\n  \n  == WHAT CHANGED (4 files prod+test, 207 insertions) ==\n  - transcript_cache_migration.go: `planTranscriptCacheSweep(..., retainSkipped map[string]bool)`; first thing in the file loop, `if retainSkipped[file.Rel] { retain(...); continue }` — retained with no recovery proof (the vanished source cannot supply one). Doc comment states the on-disk-liveness timing and that excluded/tombstoned sessions are deliberately NOT in the set.\n  - export.go: `var skippedTranscriptCache map[string]bool` declared in the persistentBrain block; populated in the surviving loop (validated && !usable); passed to the sweep. Nil map when nothing was skipped (safe lookup).\n  - export.go: new `sessionTranscriptRel(session, branchDirs)` is now the single definition of the address, used by BOTH the manifest writer and the rescue set. Key shape verified against historySessionByTranscriptPath (filepath.ToSlash(TrimSpace(TranscriptPath))) and inventory.files[].Rel (slash, \"sessions/...\"-prefixed). buildBranchDirectories is a pure function of branch name + defaultBranch (no set-dependent collision suffixing), so a recomputed path matches what an earlier export wrote.\n  - 2 test call sites updated with `nil`.\n  \n  == VERIFICATION (every command run, real results) ==\n  1. `go build ./...` -> BUILD_EXIT=0.\n  2. NEW `TestVanishedSessionKeepsItsLastCachedTranscript` (internal/cli/export_vanished_checkpoint_test.go): 2-session fixture, disk export, divergent-cache migration to checkpoint storage, blob destroyed, then 2 persistent exports; asserts the skipped session is NOT recorded and its cached bytes are byte-identical after each round. PASS.\n  3. Privacy-excluded still swept — existing coverage, named: **TestFilelessMigrationRecoversExcludedSessionAfterInclude** (internal/cli/transcript_bugbot_test.go:193, \"recoverable cache was not swept\"). Also TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache (unrecoverable-excluded -> refuse, cache preserved) and TestFilelessMigrationSweepsCacheBehindCheckpoint. All PASS. My own test additionally asserts the servable session's cache IS swept, so it is not a one-sided retain test.\n  4. WEAKENING REDS (all compiled; `--- FAIL` grepped, not `^FAIL`):\n     - A, rescue branch -> `if false` (+ `_ = retainSkipped`): `--- FAIL: TestVanishedSessionKeepsItsLastCachedTranscript` — \"round 2 destroyed the only surviving copy ... no such file or directory\".\n     - B, stop populating the map (`_ = sessionTranscriptRel(...)`): same named FAIL, round 2.\n     - C, sessionTranscriptRel returns the bare file name: same named FAIL, round 1.\n     - C2, near-miss rescue key only (`\"./\"+rel`, manifest writer untouched): same named FAIL, round 2 — key shape is load-bearing.\n     - E, never sweep a live file: `--- FAIL` on TestFilelessMigrationRecoversExcludedSessionAfterInclude (\"recoverable cache was not swept\"), TestFilelessMigrationSweepsCacheBehindCheckpoint (\"stale cache prefix not swept\"), TestFilelessMigrationRetainsDivergentCache, TestFilelessMigrationAndStandaloneBundle, TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache, TestFilelessMigrationRetainsUnrecoverableCache, and my own test's sweep assertion.\n     - D, the naive fix (retain every `!live`): NO red in the 21-test subset — reported above as correction 3, not hidden.\n     All weakenings reverted from a pristine copy; final `git diff` reviewed.\n  5. All 7 impact-named tests + the excluded/include test + the new one: PASS (incl. subtests of TestFilelessRefreshRejectsMissingTranscriptObjects 9/9, TestFilelessRoutedCatalogUsesLocalIdentities 2/2, TestFilelessRefreshPreparesHistoryOutsideWriteLock 2/2, TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache 2/2).\n  6. WHOLE MODULE UNFILTERED `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m go test ./... -count=1` -> **FULL_EXIT=0, zero FAIL lines**. Two process notes, both my fault and both resolved: (a) my first attempt was invalid because a leftover `internal/cli/zz_debug_test.go` (a diagnostic with t.Fail()) was still on disk — deleted, and it is NOT in the commit; (b) two runs then shared one output file and garbled it, so I killed both (TaskStop, not pkill) and re-ran clean to a fresh path.\n  7. `$(go env GOROOT)/bin/gofmt -l -s .` -> 0 bytes.\n  8. `go vet ./...` redirected to a file with status appended -> VET_EXIT=0.\n  10. `entire trail finding resolve 01M5SZBJYNDFFFHGF83D1DEXQR --trail entire-brain/400 -m \"<evidence>\"` -> \"Updated finding 01M5SZBJYNDFFFHGF83D1DEXQR: open → resolved\". `entire trail finding list --trail entire-brain/400` -> \"No findings found\" (0 open).\n  \n  == ADJACENT GAP, NOT FIXED (flagging, not silently expanding scope) ==\n  The snapshot-time drop in correction 2 is a SECOND instance of the same loss: a session dropped by the snapshot loader (\"skipped N session metadata entries with no transcript bytes\") never appears in `unavailable`, so it cannot enter the rescue set, and its cached transcript is swept on the following export exactly as before. Fixing it means surfacing those dropped identities out of the snapshot loader into runExport — a bigger change than this finding, and worth its own finding/PR. Everything else is clean: tree clean, brain memory recorded (`fact:428d4facb06a75e9879b61cd`, architecture.export.gotcha) documenting the on-disk-liveness off-by-one and the two reachability shapes. Prior-decision check via `entire brain recall` found PR #474 (\"retain instead of aborting\") and the squash-merge decision behind #489 — this change continues both rather than reversing either. Preflight: graph v0.5.1-nightly.202610240614.d4a0c186, brain v0.2.0-nightly.202610240625.318e4b05, entire CLI 0.11.5-nightly (2026-10-24 build, post-snake_case), all current.","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"DONE. Fix committed + pushed, finding resolved. Worked only in /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished on fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints. Nothing merged.\n\nHEAD = 5d68e1d9d53deeaafb1cce16be349bca43ff1df6 (\"fix(export): keep a skipped session's last cached transcript\"), pushed 5f15accf..5d68e1d9. No AI footer.\n\n== YOUR MECHANISM: CONFIRMED, with 3 corrections ==\nConfirmed by observation (not reading): surviving-list drop at internal/cli/export.go ~365-405; sweep call (now export.go:443); internal/cli/transcript_cache_migration.go `!live` -> continue -> never in `retained` -> returned as the delete set; sweepTranscriptCache does `inventory.root.Remove`. I reproduced the actual deletion.\n\nCORRECTION 1 (timing, off by one export). planTranscriptCacheSweep calls loadBrainManifest(brainDir) itself, and `manifest.Sessions = sessions` only reaches disk later inside withBrainWriteLock (export.go ~458/491). So the export that DROPS the session still finds it listed: the file is live, store.lookupLocation fails, and on a checkpoint-backed brain it is retained. It becomes `!live` and is swept on the NEXT export. Proven: with the retain check disabled the file is deleted at **round 2** of two consecutive exports, not round 1. My test therefore runs two exports and checks after each.\n\nCORRECTION 2 (reachability — this nearly made me ship a vacuous test). A session whose transcript path is absent from the catalog tip TREE never reaches partitionLocalTranscriptSessions at all: the snapshot loader drops it with `checkpoint_scope_incomplete: skipped unreadable local checkpoint bbb222bbb222 skipped 1 session metadata entries with no transcript bytes in refs/heads/entire/checkpoints/v1`. My first fixture had exactly that shape; the rescue set was empty and the test failed for the wrong reason. Only a **missing blob with an intact tree path** (hasSnapshotTranscript checks tree paths, not objects) reaches the per-session unavailability classification. The fixture now deletes the loose object `.git/objects/xx/yyy` after a real export has materialized the cache.\n\nCORRECTION 3 (the trap's rationale is wrong, though the narrow design is right). `!live` does NOT cover privacy-excluded/tombstoned sessions: those are exempt from validation and SURVIVE in manifest.Sessions, so they stay `live` and keep the full recovery proof. What `!live` actually covers is stale export leftovers. Consequence: the naive fix (retain every `!live` file) produces **no red** in the 21-test cache/export subset — TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache passes under it. I kept the narrow design anyway (retaining stale leftovers forever defeats \"Unlisted files are stale exports\"), but the guard you cited is not what stops the naive fix.\n\n== WHAT CHANGED (4 files prod+test, 207 insertions) ==\n- transcript_cache_migration.go: `planTranscriptCacheSweep(..., retainSkipped map[string]bool)`; first thing in the file loop, `if retainSkipped[file.Rel] { retain(...); continue }` — retained with no recovery proof (the vanished source cannot supply one). Doc comment states the on-disk-liveness timing and that excluded/tombstoned sessions are deliberately NOT in the set.\n- export.go: `var skippedTranscriptCache map[string]bool` declared in the persistentBrain block; populated in the surviving loop (validated && !usable); passed to the sweep. Nil map when nothing was skipped (safe lookup).\n- export.go: new `sessionTranscriptRel(session, branchDirs)` is now the single definition of the address, used by BOTH the manifest writer and the rescue set. Key shape verified against historySessionByTranscriptPath (filepath.ToSlash(TrimSpace(TranscriptPath))) and inventory.files[].Rel (slash, \"sessions/...\"-prefixed). buildBranchDirectories is a pure function of branch name + defaultBranch (no set-dependent collision suffixing), so a recomputed path matches what an earlier export wrote.\n- 2 test call sites updated with `nil`.\n\n== VERIFICATION (every command run, real results) ==\n1. `go build ./...` -> BUILD_EXIT=0.\n2. NEW `TestVanishedSessionKeepsItsLastCachedTranscript` (internal/cli/export_vanished_checkpoint_test.go): 2-session fixture, disk export, divergent-cache migration to checkpoint storage, blob destroyed, then 2 persistent exports; asserts the skipped session is NOT recorded and its cached bytes are byte-identical after each round. PASS.\n3. Privacy-excluded still swept — existing coverage, named: **TestFilelessMigrationRecoversExcludedSessionAfterInclude** (internal/cli/transcript_bugbot_test.go:193, \"recoverable cache was not swept\"). Also TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache (unrecoverable-excluded -> refuse, cache preserved) and TestFilelessMigrationSweepsCacheBehindCheckpoint. All PASS. My own test additionally asserts the servable session's cache IS swept, so it is not a one-sided retain test.\n4. WEAKENING REDS (all compiled; `--- FAIL` grepped, not `^FAIL`):\n   - A, rescue branch -> `if false` (+ `_ = retainSkipped`): `--- FAIL: TestVanishedSessionKeepsItsLastCachedTranscript` — \"round 2 destroyed the only surviving copy ... no such file or directory\".\n   - B, stop populating the map (`_ = sessionTranscriptRel(...)`): same named FAIL, round 2.\n   - C, sessionTranscriptRel returns the bare file name: same named FAIL, round 1.\n   - C2, near-miss rescue key only (`\"./\"+rel`, manifest writer untouched): same named FAIL, round 2 — key shape is load-bearing.\n   - E, never sweep a live file: `--- FAIL` on TestFilelessMigrationRecoversExcludedSessionAfterInclude (\"recoverable cache was not swept\"), TestFilelessMigrationSweepsCacheBehindCheckpoint (\"stale cache prefix not swept\"), TestFilelessMigrationRetainsDivergentCache, TestFilelessMigrationAndStandaloneBundle, TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache, TestFilelessMigrationRetainsUnrecoverableCache, and my own test's sweep assertion.\n   - D, the naive fix (retain every `!live`): NO red in the 21-test subset — reported above as correction 3, not hidden.\n   All weakenings reverted from a pristine copy; final `git diff` reviewed.\n5. All 7 impact-named tests + the excluded/include test + the new one: PASS (incl. subtests of TestFilelessRefreshRejectsMissingTranscriptObjects 9/9, TestFilelessRoutedCatalogUsesLocalIdentities 2/2, TestFilelessRefreshPreparesHistoryOutsideWriteLock 2/2, TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache 2/2).\n6. WHOLE MODULE UNFILTERED `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m go test ./... -count=1` -> **FULL_EXIT=0, zero FAIL lines**. Two process notes, both my fault and both resolved: (a) my first attempt was invalid because a leftover `internal/cli/zz_debug_test.go` (a diagnostic with t.Fail()) was still on disk — deleted, and it is NOT in the commit; (b) two runs then shared one output file and garbled it, so I killed both (TaskStop, not pkill) and re-ran clean to a fresh path.\n7. `$(go env GOROOT)/bin/gofmt -l -s .` -> 0 bytes.\n8. `go vet ./...` redirected to a file with status appended -> VET_EXIT=0.\n10. `entire trail finding resolve 01M5SZBJYNDFFFHGF83D1DEXQR --trail entire-brain/400 -m \"<evidence>\"` -> \"Updated finding 01M5SZBJYNDFFFHGF83D1DEXQR: open → resolved\". `entire trail finding list --trail entire-brain/400` -> \"No findings found\" (0 open).\n\n== ADJACENT GAP, NOT FIXED (flagging, not silently expanding scope) ==\nThe snapshot-time drop in correction 2 is a SECOND instance of the same loss: a session dropped by the snapshot loader (\"skipped N session metadata entries with no transcript bytes\") never appears in `unavailable`, so it cannot enter the rescue set, and its cached transcript is swept on the following export exactly as before. Fixing it means surfacing those dropped identities out of the snapshot loader into runExport — a bigger change than this finding, and worth its own finding/PR. Everything else is clean: tree clean, brain memory recorded (`fact:428d4facb06a75e9879b61cd`, architecture.export.gotcha) documenting the on-disk-liveness off-by-one and the two reachability shapes. Prior-decision check via `entire brain recall` found PR #474 (\"retain instead of aborting\") and the squash-merge decision behind #489 — this change continues both rather than reversing either. Preflight: graph v0.5.1-nightly.202610240614.d4a0c186, brain v0.2.0-nightly.202610240625.318e4b05, entire CLI 0.11.5-nightly (2026-10-24 build, post-snake_case), all current."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
