{"parentUuid":"98c840c7-2692-4998-99b9-ed3d3f2ae663","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPPC4h3PJZzNJNpqBaoW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RKSLkUnTfkNqW7PCfbHXWV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"for spec in \\\n\"01M5RK2YNSW8BMCZAFRQ7KBXSK:Fixed, and this is the finding the current design is built around. localObjectType errors are no longer all read as unavailable: an absence is classified from git's exit code via localObjectMissingConfirmed (git_catfile_batch.go), where 0 means present, 1 silent means resolved-but-absent and 128 means unresolvable, and a cancelled or expired context returns false rather than evidence. Runner, context and spawn errors are returned as hard errors. Reproduced against real git 2.54.0 rather than only a fake runner. Hardened twice since: the partial-clone case now FAILS instead of dropping a session, because under GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH an unfetched blob is indistinguishable from a destroyed one (gitDirHasPromisorRemote), and that probe only caches a definitive answer so one transient config-read failure cannot pin a partial clone to no-promisor for the process. Final head 5d68e1d9.\" \\\n\"01M5RHZZR905AS4ZGV8Y822HA3:Duplicate of 01M5RK2YNSW8BMCZAFRQ7KBXSK and fixed by the same change. Only a definitive object-missing result is skipped; transient runner and context errors are returned as errors. Resolving rather than dismissing: the finding is correct, it is the same defect reported twice. Final head 5d68e1d9.\" \\\n; do id=${spec%%:*}; msg=${spec#*:}; printf \"%s -> \" \"${id: -6}\"; entire trail finding resolve \"$id\" --trail entire-brain/400 -m \"$msg\" 2>&1 | tail -1; done","description":"Resolve the two fixed-but-unresolved findings"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1097,"cache_read_input_tokens":422920,"output_toke