{"parentUuid":"6e8d873e-d414-4d14-abd5-af8202bb7ff2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPPHZwqTwxzRLiCpJZZW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#479 auto-merged, carrying #481 with it.** That's 12 of 13 landed — main is now `2e69a9ba`.\n\n```\nMERGED (12)  473 474 476 477 478 479 480 481 482 483 488  + 481 via 479\nOPEN   (1)   489  — one new finding being fixed now\nBLOCKED (1)  484  — awaiting your call on the benchmark check\n```\n\nTwo things worth your attention more than the merge count.\n\n**The agent corrected me on the reasoning I gave it.** I told it the trap was that `!live` covers privacy-excluded sessions, so the naive fix would break `TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache`. Wrong on both counts: excluded sessions stay *live* in the manifest, `!live` is actually stale export leftovers, and it measured that the naive fix produces **no red at all** in that 21-test subset. It kept the narrow design for a different, correct reason and said so instead of letting my framing stand. It also caught its own near-vacuous fixture — a session whose transcript path is missing from the catalog tree never reaches the code under test, so the first version tested nothing.\n\n**And it reported \"0 open findings\" using the bare `finding list` — which hides them.** With `--status any` there were three. That default filter has now misled this session four separate times: a repo-scoped trail number, a stale PR check summary, my own sweep, and now a subagent's. I've told it to never report an open count from an unfiltered list again.\n\nThe one genuinely new finding is the fourth instance of a single class — **treating a recoverable absence as definitive** (object-missing → promisor caching → cache retention → now \"no snapshot entry\"). Rather than fix it and wait for a fifth, I've asked for a sweep of every remaining site in the export path that decides \"this data is gone\" without separating recoverable from definitive.\n\n#484 still needs your word: finish the brainmark packet tests so it can merge, or leave it open."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":429058,"output_tokens":652,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":352,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":652,"cache_read_input_tokens":429058,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":352},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"76b2b289-0e2d-4b1e-8914-09f20fd921a6","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPPHZcjkpxY8etNxWtNS","requestRef":"a9e62a5c-bd90-41ff-8ed2-0d64faf0e29d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7aed452-8c07-4407-91ef-9d79ba0b48e3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:55:22.766Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
