{"parentUuid":"aa4d801a-f4ff-4413-8b24-892085ab894f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPQ5xbtH7xtT3znYseK5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm going to stop here and report rather than keep going, for a specific reason.\n\n**v1 is fully green** (18 passed) — the tag allowlist, the independent Python projection, the fixture (which I first put under `status.semantic`, where the projection never looks), and the record count.\n\n**v2 is a chain of deliberately frozen anchors**, and I've now hit the fourth: `COMPACT_V2_GOLDEN_SHA256` (re-anchored, with evidence), then the positional schema + tag, and now `test_frozen_schema_is_exact_and_natural_language_cannot_reference` plus runner-identity and legend/footer integrity pins.\n\nEach of those pins exists to catch *unintended* golden drift. Re-anchoring one with a stated reason is defensible. **Re-anchoring four in a row so my own change passes is the exact move I've refused all session** — it's the same shape as rewriting a privacy test to let a performance change through, which is why I left #478's lock alone and handed you that decision instead.\n\nSo this needs your eyes, not my judgement:\n\n- **\"finish it\"** — I re-anchor the remaining v2 pins to the reviewed golden (the Go side proves it via `TestBrainBriefCompactV2GoldenAndExactProjectionParity`), #484 becomes mergeable, and I'll list every pin I moved so it's auditable.\n- **\"leave #484\"** — 12 of 13 are merged; #484 stays open with the cause documented, and nothing is silently loosened.\n\nFor what it's worth my recommendation is **finish it**: the golden genuinely changed on purpose, the Go side independently verifies it, and the v1 suite passing proves the new record is consistent across two implementations. But it's your call because it's your fail-closed contract.\n\nMeanwhile **#489's agent is still working** on the no-snapshot-entry fix plus the sweep for any remaining \"recoverable absence treated as definitive\" sites — I'll report when it lands."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1208,"cache_read_input_tokens":447635,"output_tokens":1250,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":600},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1208,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1250,"cache_read_input_tokens":447635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1208},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5e3fe8de-f10e-470a-9ea2-aa3af868ff91","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPQ5xDKFQ6djt4K32HCz","requestRef":"d67f3beb-1667-47d8-b73b-8273f43b60d5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"9b5e7240-0065-4247-8705-5ba4f732af08","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:06:01.976Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
