{"parentUuid":"d5e20c70-b78d-4a36-bc79-49178cefe866","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14902497 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"daa571a2-7c37-46b1-a232-a3d052a28924","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:10:04.589Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14902497 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"daa571a2-7c37-46b1-a232-a3d052a28924","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01PZMwfj6StSaZzAHuHnMHTy","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"99196436-8e1b-4109-b1da-a19a59fee463","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:10:15.219Z","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"99196436-8e1b-4109-b1da-a19a59fee463","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPQRNuQdFZHKhsb8Ucks","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#489's second fix landed** — `6e6d31bf`, *\"a missing snapshot entry is not proof the bytes are gone\"*. Trail 400 is **0 open**, confirmed with `--status any --freshness any`. I'm re-running the full unfiltered suite myself rather than taking it on trust, since no report reached me.\n\nThe diffstat tells the story: `transcript_store.go` +101 and `export_vanished_checkpoint_test.go` +359 — the guard plus substantial tests, which is the right ratio for a data-loss fix.\n\n**Where everything stands:**\n\n```\nMERGED   12  473 474 476 477 478 479 480 481 482 483 488  (main 2e69a9ba)\nREADY     1  489  — 0 open findings; verifying, then needs CI on its new head\nBLOCKED   1  484  — waiting on your call about the frozen v2 pins\n```\n\n**The pattern this turn is the thing worth keeping.** #489 took four fixes, each the same defect class — *treating a recoverable absence as definitive*. Object-missing, then promisor caching, then cache retention, now a missing snapshot entry. Each one was found only after the previous fix was pushed and re-reviewed. That's why I asked for a sweep of every remaining site that decides \"this data is gone\" without separating recoverable from definitive, instead of waiting for a fifth.\n\nAnd one of those four corrected a claim I'd made confidently: I'd argued that a destroyed checkpoint \"has no snapshot entry, so it's classified from data and never reaches git\" — which is exactly what an unsynced partial clone also looks like.\n\n**Two things still need you:**\n\n1. **#484's v2 pins** — finish re-anchoring them (my recommendation, since the Go side independently verifies the golden and v1 now passes across two implementations), or leave #484 open. I won't move four fail-closed anchors to make my own change pass without you saying so.\n2. Your three originals: transcript mode, the 37 GB delete, the Linear connector."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":504,"cache_read_input_tokens":453504,"output_tokens":665,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":504,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":665,"cache_read_input_tokens":453504,"cache_creation_input_tokens":504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":504},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4c8994ea-352f-45ec-b758-a6ff3ebacd81","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPQRNSNvBzpMaTa98h6d","requestRef":"22d6273a-47e0-49a7-b355-7d09ee01f4d2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"9102c46c-e90e-4f17-b149-19bbbe22797e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:10:15.218Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
