{"parentUuid":"c206a61a-765b-4e50-aaa6-b96e50ad1429","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPQrP8VES6rRGKqantVU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"GitHub auto-retargeted #489's base to `main` when #488 merged, and it reads **MERGEABLE** at `6e6d31bf`. Its CI is running now — Windows shards in progress, macOS queued.\n\nI'm deliberately **not** arming auto-merge on it yet. My own full unfiltered suite is still running locally, and that exact run is what caught two broken tests on this same branch earlier today, before they reached anyone. Once it's clean I'll arm auto-merge and #489 lands on its own, the same way #479 did. If it surfaces something, I'd rather fix it than revert main.\n\nSo the sequence from here is mechanical and needs nothing from you:\n\n1. local suite clean → arm auto-merge on #489 → **13 of 13 merged**\n2. #484 waits on your one word about the frozen v2 pins\n\nOne honest note: the #489 agent's final report never actually surfaced in my conversation despite three notifications saying it had. I'm therefore treating its work as unverified until my own run finishes, and I haven't described what it did or claimed its verification as evidence — the commit message, the diffstat, the branch state and the 0-open finding count are all I've confirmed first-hand."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":455769,"output_tokens":1163,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":769},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1163,"cache_read_input_tokens":455769,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_token