{"parentUuid":"817ae600-a07f-4c0d-abcb-b9656bc9d8cb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01FgXsu1KfGQxTRVUX74W5r6","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fbcbeddb-735f-49b3-a5c3-f474f781c07c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:18:38.465Z","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"fbcbeddb-735f-49b3-a5c3-f474f781c07c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPR4SJ4vjeXGpkrjj1tQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#489's new guard is load-bearing — verified by me, not taken on trust.** Disabling it produces named reds with the package still compiling:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestANoSnapshotEntryInAPartialCloneFailsTheExportRatherThanShrinkingIt\n      /promisor_remote\n      /unanswered_probe\n--- FAIL: TestAnyFetchableSnapshotSourceGatesTheSkip\n```\n\nBoth directions covered, including the unanswered-probe case — which is the one I'd have got wrong, since an unasked question is not evidence of absence.\n\n**Auto-merge is armed on #489.** When its CI finishes, that's **13 of 13 merged**, and nothing further is needed from me on the merge.\n\nFinal state:\n\n```\nMERGED    12   main 2e69a9ba\nARMED      1   489 — verified clean locally (18/18, gofmt, vet), guard\n                proved load-bearing, 0 open findings, lands on CI green\nYOURS      1   484 — the frozen v2 pins\n```\n\nThe #489 agent's report never did reach me across four notifications, so everything I've told you about that branch I confirmed myself: the commits, the diffstat, the full unfiltered suite, gofmt, vet, the 0-open finding count under `--status any`, and the weakening above. I'd rather hand you a narrower claim I checked than a broader one I was told.\n\n**#484 is the only thing left that's genuinely a decision**, and it's the same kind you've already made well once: I won't move four fail-closed anchors to let my own change through without you saying so — exactly as I didn't rewrite the privacy test to speed up #478. Say \"finish it\" and I'll re-anchor them and list every pin I touched; say \"leave it\" and #484 stays open with the cause documented.\n\nThen your three originals remain: transcript mode, the 37 GB delete, the Linear connector."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":813,"cache_read_input_tokens":459617,"output_tokens":628,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":813,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":459617,"cache_creation_input_tokens":813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":813},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"32ae109c-6df2-4af0-9c98-9d101635aee9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPR4RrYAgTLA94TBio8s","requestRef":"30f606a3-0616-4a07-8e7d-ef946f9486db","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"4fa110fc-5c42-4fa3-a031-38838c74d736","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:18:38.464Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
