{"parentUuid":"7041509f-0682-49e9-acb5-85e42f8a659c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPRPAb3Sk7qwNPWadiPD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TnpuzYSu2N1AEHButiycDM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add benchmarks/agent-brain/ && git commit -q -m \"test(benchmarks): teach the packet A/B harness the staleness record\n\nThe ancestor-staleness disclosure adds one body record to the compact\npacket, so the brainmark A/B harness refused it. benchmark-corpus is a\nrequired check, so #484 could not merge while this was red.\n\nBoth modules carry their own independent re-implementation of the\nprojection, which is the point of the harness, so both needed the record:\nthe v1 tag allowlist, the v2 positional schema under opcode 'A' (matching\ncompactV2SchemaFor in brain_brief_compact_v2.go field-for-field, since a\ndivergent order would decode to the wrong values rather than fail), and\nthe projection plus report fixture in each module.\n\nFour frozen anchors are re-anchored, not relaxed: the v2 golden sha, the\nderived runner identity, the opcode count and the canonical record digest.\nEach exists to catch UNINTENDED drift, and this drift is intended and\ncross-verified -- parsed[\\\"records\\\"] now equals the independent Python\nprojection, and the Go side proves the same golden through\nTestBrainBriefCompactV2GoldenAndExactProjectionParity. Verified still\nload-bearing afterwards: changing one character of the golden\n(ancestor1 -> ancestor2) fails five tests.\n\nOne stale tamper construction fixed while here. The fail-closed legend test\nbuilt its wrong-count candidate with golden.replace(b\\\"end\\\\t65\\\\t\\\", ...).\nOnce the golden grew to 66 that matched nothing, so the candidate WAS the\npristine golden and the subcase asserted nothing. It now tracks the real\ncount.\" && echo \"head=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"; git push origin HEAD:feat/brief-ancestor-staleness 2>&1 | tail 