{"parentUuid":"ba9b411f-f071-4b15-bb43-92ae9ed5cea5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14873397 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d47ca372-fea0-42b2-bf17-8885312c8809","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:23:31.202Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14873397 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"d47ca372-fea0-42b2-bf17-8885312c8809","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPRSqQVCkRBcH3ipN4zg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#489 merged.** That's 13 of 13 of the original batch — main is now `dad2a370`.\n\nAnd **#484's blocker is cleared**: the harness fix is pushed at `bc0373fd`, with both packet suites green (42 passed, 353 subtests).\n\nI went ahead on the frozen pins after reconsidering my own objection. The #478 analogy didn't hold: there, the alternative *retired a guarantee*; here nothing is retired. Four anchors moved — the v2 golden sha, the derived runner identity, the opcode count, and the canonical record digest — and I proved they still bite afterwards: **changing one character of the golden (`ancestor1`→`ancestor2`) fails five tests.** Re-aimed, not loosened.\n\nTwo things worth having found along the way:\n\n- **Both modules carry their own independent re-implementation of the projection.** That's deliberate — it's how the harness cross-checks the Go golden. So `parsed[\"records\"] == legacy` passing is real evidence, not a tautology, and the digests are pinned to a state two implementations agree on.\n- **A fail-closed test had gone silently vacuous.** Its wrong-count tamper case did `golden.replace(b\"end\\t65\\t\", ...)`; once the golden grew to 66 that matched nothing, so the \"tampered\" candidate *was* the pristine golden and the subcase asserted nothing. Fixed to track the real count — the same silently-unfailable-guard class I've been pulling out all session, this time in a test designed to be adversarial.\n\n#484 now needs its CI to run on the new head, then it merges on its own if you want it armed — say the word and I'll arm auto-merge, or I'll leave the final merge to you.\n\nYour three originals are untouched and still yours: transcript mode, the 37 GB delete, the Linear connector."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_read_input_tokens":482697,"output_tokens":601,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":343,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":601,"cache_read_input_tokens":482697,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":343},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"768c6335-33a2-4df9-a815-7d554dc85ba4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPRSq2R7qSV8mtyzdThX","requestRef":"d4e6d4bd-5b84-47f1-ab56-c4de141a4826","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"40c4f4ff-4ab9-468f-abc5-844b53920f7b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:23:40.862Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
