wed 3, 3, 2 and 1. Always pass both.\n2. **A `-run` filter is blind to what a behaviour change breaks**, because those tests are named\n   after their own concern. `-run 'Promisor|Vanished|...'` passed while two tests broke. Run the\n   whole package unfiltered before pushing.\n3. **Closing a PR kills `pull_request` CI on its branch**, and `gh pr checks` then serves the\n   previous head's green. Use `gh workflow run test.yml --ref <branch>` and verify the run's\n   `headSha`.\n\n## Still the user's, and genuinely only the user's\n\n- **Transcript mode** — per-session mode re-keys the distill cache fingerprint and bills a\n  corpus-wide re-distill. Spends money.\n- **`brain-store-delete`** — 37 GB, irreversible. Sequence written, not run.\n- **Linear connector** — account-side in claude.ai → Connectors; the MCP server 404s and no\n  command I run reaches it. Three tickets are written and waiting.\n\n\"\"\"\nstart = s.index(\"## Carry this into the merge\")\nopen(p,\"w\").write(head + s[start:])\nprint(\"handoff rewritten\")\nPY\nhead -6 BRAIN-HANDOFF-STATE.md","description":"Rewrite the handoff doc for the merged state"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_012oPgApiXNcr5htb6uzDtj2":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0a07c961-eec4-4717-9165-984d4072f566","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPRX99DA4x27KNRLGc1N","requestRef":"881a827c-219a-413e-af1b-3c3535ba2d31","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"d5c02eb5-1772-4fbf-80be-20ace7873203","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:24:45.771Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"d5c02eb5-1772-4fbf-80be-20ace7873203","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ebf835a0-0d0c-4768-9746-ffb4a9e0652c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012oPgApiXNcr5htb6uzDtj2","type":"tool_result","content":"handoff rewritten\n# Brain handoff state — MERGED, 2026-10-25\n\n**13 of 13 original PRs are merged** (main `dad2a370`). **#484 is armed for auto-merge** at\n`bc0373fd` and lands when its CI goes green; its trail has 0 open findings. #493 is closed.\nNothing below is pending on me.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"35e25060-a38f-48fa-95f8-3a2ad8f00cf8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:24:46.469Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"handoff rewritten\n# Brain handoff state — MERGED, 2026-10-25\n\n**13 of 13 original PRs are merged** (main `dad2a370`). **#484 is armed for auto-merge** at\n`bc0373fd` and lands when its CI goes green; its trail has 0 open findings. #493 is closed.\nNothing below is pending on me.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/BRAIN-HANDOFF-STATE.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":75,"newStart":1,"newLines":46,"lines":["-# Brain handoff state — final, 2026-10-25","-","-Written to a file because the Bash **and** SendMessage safety classifier began returning no","-verdict and did not recover, so I could not message the graph session or run git. The graph","-session's handoff page should be corrected from this. Nothing here is lost work; two actions","-remain, both one command each.","-","-## The 13 heads","-","-| PR | branch | head | note |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| #473 | fix/distill-pipeline-v2 | `8f693073` | writer concurrency contract |","-| #474 | fix/export-divergent-transcript | `ef41d238` | |","-| #476 | perf/history-terms-normalize-once | `66348cd2` | |","-| #477 | feat/mcp-surface-reachable | `d58e9639` | #478's feature stripped out |","-| #478 | perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint | `64b7a146` | |","-| #479 | perf/export-detail-fanout | `2d020c72` | merge before #481 |","-| #480 | fix/routed-checkpoint-list-cap | `c796a615` | |","-| #481 | perf/local-checkpoint-metadata | `46fe7f3b` | stacked on #479 |","-| #482 | fix/firstrun-agent-hook-paths | `031fbb5b` | |","-| #483 | fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize | `1e257ab9` | sentinel masking at 3 producers |","-| #484 | feat/brief-ancestor-staleness | `9a3aac28` | staleness in all 5 formats |","-| #488 | fix/export-honours-session-tombstones | `35c308e4` | merge before #489 |","-| #489 | fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints | `5f15accf` | promisor probe + fixtures |","-","-**Combined tree `45e7a626` on `main@a4942dd9`:** all 13 merge clean in order; `go test ./...`","-exit 0, 25/25 packages, zero `--- FAIL`; build, gofmt and vet clean. CI via","-**`workflow_dispatch` run 40214249807** (headSha verified): ubuntu, macos, windows","-vet/compile/shards 0-5, lint, regression-mutations and all five builds green.","-","-**Two reds that are expected, not regressions.** `benchmark-corpus` fails because #484's new","-`staleness` record changes the compact packet, and two Python modules in `brainmark/`","-(`test_packet_format_ab.py`, `test_packet_format_v2_ab.py`) assert packet shape and bytes. You","-directed that benchmark work is unnecessary, so it is deliberately not fixed. `release-evidence`","-runs only on dispatch/tag and fails on any non-release branch.","-","-**The closed-PR CI trap, worth knowing before you merge.** `test.yml` fires on push-to-main,","-`pull_request` and `workflow_dispatch`. Closing #493 stopped `pull_request` events on its","-branch, so later pushes got no CI at all while `gh pr checks 493` kept reporting the PREVIOUS","-head's green. Use `gh workflow run test.yml --ref <branch>` and verify the run's `headSha`.","-","-Merge order and the two stacks (`#479→#481`, `#488→#489`) are unchanged. I checked a suspicion","-that #477 and #478 were a hidden third stack — they conflicted in the same file over the same","-per-branch fact code — and `merge-base --is-ancestor` says **#478 is not an ancestor of #477**.","-Two stacks only. **That ancestry answer was right and the conclusion I drew from it was wrong.**","-#477 carried #478's whole feature as *content*: commit `62005328`, labelled","-\"the MCP probe's stderr sink must be safe to read before Wait\", also added","-`pattern_corpus.go` (+92) and `pattern_corpus_branch_facts_test.go` (+174). A reviewer would","-have met an unexplained fingerprint rewrite inside an MCP PR, and merging both would have","-double-applied it. #477 is now cut back to its own four files (`d58e9639`), verified by its","-diff against main and by a weakening red on its own frame-cap guard.","-","-Checked for the same shape across the other eleven: `git diff --stat origin/main...<branch>`","-per PR, no other branch carries a file outside its own subject.","-","-## Nothing is pending","-","-Both items that were blocked are done. The safety classifier had been returning no verdict for","-about eleven consecutive calls, which is why they lagged; it recovered.","-","-- **#483** committed and pushed as `fbc2946a`.","-- **#493** refreshed against `main@ab575071` and force-pushed (`4654e994`). CI then came","-  back **green on ubuntu, macos and windows** (6 Windows shards + vet + compile + coverage),","-  plus lint and regression-mutations — which closes the `-race` and Windows gap every local","-  run had to disclose.","-- **Re-merged against `main@a4942dd9`** after #494/#495 landed: all 13 read **MERGEABLE**, all 13","-  merge clean in order, and the combined tree (`#493` @ `45cf54e1`) is green again: GitHub Actions","-  **completed/success**, 23 checks pass including all six Windows shards; local `go test ./...`","-  exit 0, 25/25 packages. The only non-passing rows are Entire Gates and Partial Gates, which","-  are the Approvals sub-gate. Combined tree:","-  `go test ./...` exit 0, 20 packages ok + 5 no-test-files = 25 of 25, zero `--- FAIL`,","-  `gofmt` silent, `go vet` exit 0.","+# Brain handoff state — MERGED, 2026-10-25","+","+**13 of 13 original PRs are merged** (main `dad2a370`). **#484 is armed for auto-merge** at","+`bc0373fd` and lands when its CI goes green; its trail has 0 open findings. #493 is closed.","+Nothing below is pending on me.","+","+## What this took beyond the first \"done\"","+","+Six further fixes landed after the batch was first declared finished, five of them found by","+agent review on trails whose gates read \"Findings: passed\":","+","+- **#489** needed four fixes, every one the same class: *treating a recoverable absence as","+  definitive*. Object-missing exit codes, then a promisor probe that cached its own failures,","+  then a cache sweep that dropped a skipped session's last surviving transcript, then a missing","+  snapshot entry read as proof the bytes were gone. Each was found only after the previous fix","+  was pushed and re-reviewed.","+- **#483** masked containment, source-race and privacy-gate refusals behind a skippable","+  sentinel at **three** producers. I fixed one and wrote that it covered all three `errors.Is`","+  sites; a reviewer found the second and chasing it found the third.","+- **#477** was carrying the whole of #478 as content, identical blob SHAs, under a commit","+  message about an unrelated stderr fix. `merge-base --is-ancestor` had said \"not stacked\",","+  which is true of history and says nothing about content.","+- **#484** was missing staleness from 3 of 5 formats and from the default text output, and then","+  blocked the merge until the brainmark packet harness learned the new record.","+","+## Three traps worth carrying forward","+","+1. **`entire trail finding list` hides open findings by default.** It reported 0 open on four","+   separate occasions when `--status any --freshness any` showed 3, 3, 2 and 1. Always pass both.","+2. **A `-run` filter is blind to what a behaviour change breaks**, because those tests are named","+   after their own concern. `-run 'Promisor|Vanished|...'` passed while two tests broke. Run the","+   whole package unfiltered before pushing.","+3. **Closing a PR kills `pull_request` CI on its branch**, and `gh pr checks` then serves the","+   previous head's green. Use `gh workflow run test.yml --ref <branch>` and verify the run's","+   `headSha`.","+","+## Still the user's, and genuinely only the user's","+","+- **Transcript mode** — per-session mode re-keys the distill cache fingerprint and bills a","+  corpus-wide re-distill. Spends money.","+- **`brain-store-delete`** — 37 GB, irreversible. Sequence written, not run.","+- **Linear connector** — account-side in claude.ai → Connectors; the MCP server 404s and no","+  command I run reaches it. Three tickets are written and waiting."," "," ## Carry this into the merge"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/suhaan/devenv/BRAIN-HANDOFF-STATE.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0a07c961-eec4-4717-9165-984d4072f566","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":255},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire.io","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"source