{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"a282bd503d167d04eb67b0676f6c46fc7c9173ab664c86ccae84140137e4ab5d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012oPgApiXNcr5htb6uzDtj2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv && python3 - <<'PY'\np=\"BRAIN-HANDOFF-STATE.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nhead = \"\"\"# Brain handoff state — MERGED, 2026-10-25\n\n**13 of 13 original PRs are merged** (main `dad2a370`). **#484 is armed for auto-merge** at\n`bc0373fd` and lands when its CI goes green; its trail has 0 open findings. #493 is closed.\nNothing below is pending on me.\n\n## What this took beyond the first \"done\"\n\nSix further fixes landed after the batch was first declared finished, five of them found by\nagent review on trails whose gates read \"Findings: passed\":\n\n- **#489** needed four fixes, every one the same class: *treating a recoverable absence as\n  definitive*. Object-missing exit codes, then a promisor probe that cached its own failures,\n  then a cache sweep that dropped a skipped session's last surviving transcript, then a missing\n  snapshot entry read as proof the bytes were gone. Each was found only after the previous fix\n  was pushed and re-reviewed.\n- **#483** masked containment, source-race and privacy-gate refusals behind a skippable\n  sentinel at **three** producers. I fixed one and wrote that it covered all three `errors.Is`\n  sites; a reviewer found the second and chasing it found the third.\n- **#477** was carrying the whole of #478 as content, identical blob SHAs, under a commit\n  message about an unrelated stderr fix. `merge-base --is-ancestor` had said \"not stacked\",\n  which is true of history and says nothing about content.\n- **#484** was missing staleness from 3 of 5 formats and from the default text output, and then\n  blocked the merge until the brainmark packet harness learned the new record.\n\n## Three traps worth carrying forward\n\n1. **`entire trail finding list` hides open findings by default.** It reported 0 open on four\n   separate occasions when `--status any --freshness any` showed 3, 3, 2 and 1. Always pass both.\n2. **A `-run` filter is blind to what a behaviour change breaks**, because those tests are named\n   after their own concern. `-run 'Promisor|Vanished|...'` passed while two tests broke. Run the\n   whole package unfiltered before pushing.\n3. **Closing a PR kills `pull_request` CI on its branch**, and `gh pr checks` then serves the\n   previous head's green. Use `gh workflow run test.yml --ref <branch>` and verify the run's\n   `headSha`.\n\n## Still the user's, and genuinely only the user's\n\n- **Transcript mode** — per-session mode re-keys the distill cache fingerprint and bills a\n  corpus-wide re-distill. Spends money.\n- **`brain-store-delete`** — 37 GB, irreversible. Sequence written, not run.\n- **Linear connector** — account-side in claude.ai → Connectors; the MCP server 404s and no\n  command I run reaches it. Three tickets are written and waiting.\n\n\"\"\"\nstart = s.index(\"## Carry this into the merge\")\nopen(p,\"w\").write(head + s[start:])\nprint(\"handoff rewritten\")\nPY\nhead -6 BRAIN-HANDOFF-STATE.md","description":"Rewrite the handoff doc for the merged state"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
