{"parentUuid":"e0cdcecb-bd1c-4b21-8723-547d4b3e230e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPRbBgMfviuo5hNmm9bS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#484 is armed and waiting on CI — that's elapsed time, not a decision.** `benchmark-corpus` is running now (the check that was red; both its suites pass locally), and the rest are in progress or queued. I've set a watcher that will tell me the moment it merges, so it needs nothing further from either of us.\n\nOn the three remaining items, I want to be plain rather than repeat myself a fifth time:\n\n**I'm not going to do these, and it isn't caution.** Transcript mode bills your account for a corpus-wide re-distill. The store delete destroys 37 GB irreversibly. The Linear connector is a control in claude.ai → Connectors that returns 404 — there is no command I can run that reaches it. A stop condition can't make me authorised to spend your money or delete your data, and the repetition doesn't change the facts. Everything I *can* do for them is already done: the delete sequence is written, the transcript-mode cost note is written, and the three Linear tickets are drafted and waiting.\n\nSo the honest final state:\n\n```\n13/13  original PRs MERGED        main dad2a370\n#484   armed, CI running          bc0373fd · 0 open findings\n#493   closed                     verification branch\n3      items need your hands      money · irreversible · account-side\n```\n\nThe work is finished. What's left is one CI run and three things that are yours by nature, not by my choosing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":565,"cache_read_input_tokens":489799,"output_tokens":445,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":565,"ephe