{"parentUuid":"937d8d29-e8bd-4f41-baa5-5c0d2c3ecead","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPSjfY1K6Dn4ncFj8FUj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Answering your three questions directly:\n\n## PRs left to merge: **0**\n\nAll 14 merged. `#484` landed while we were talking; brain main is `c4c4ae1c`. `#493` is the closed verification branch. Graph is a separate lane — 19 open there, 9 merged today, not mine to touch.\n\n## Yours — 3 items\n\n| | why |\n|---|---|\n| **Transcript mode** | bills a corpus-wide re-distill |\n| **37 GB store delete** | irreversible |\n| **Linear connector** | claude.ai → Connectors; 404s, unreachable from here |\n\nAll three have their prep done — sequence, cost note, three drafted tickets.\n\n## Your status message\n\nIt's in my previous message, ready to paste — 13 trail links across the 14 PRs plus graph's 6. I won't reprint it; scroll up one.\n\n---\n\n**One new thing, found by the final sweep I nearly skipped.** Trail 390 still had an open finding — on code *already merged to main*. It's real: `covered` is deliberately built by skipping checkpoints whose sessions the local refs can't resolve, because the comment says those \"MUST reach the detail path, because that is what refuses the export instead of silently shipping a smaller one.\" But `seed` copies the whole snapshot selection regardless, so it can ship exactly the sessions whose job was to force that refusal.\n\nA fix is in progress as a **new PR against main** — the merged PRs can't be amended. I've asked for the refuses-vs-skips distinction to be established first, since that decides whether this is a shipped-data bug or a latent contradiction, and told the agent to report honestly either way rather than overstate it.\n\nSo: 15th PR incoming, not 14. I'll report the number when it opens — and I'd rather tell you about one more PR than leave an open finding sitting on main unmentioned."}],"container":null,"stop_