{"parentUuid":"ee350934-82c0-4abb-942b-49c5c21cb8d3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14978328 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"14b84a06-15bf-4993-bb13-8bc42a60afde","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:42:53.325Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14978328 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"14b84a06-15bf-4993-bb13-8bc42a60afde","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPSvW3KD5TR79zXjC2fC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Both lanes are clear.** Graph merged all 12 (main `d0475ce8`, tree byte-identical to its integration tip, #381 closed); brain merged all 14 (main `c4c4ae1c`, #493 closed).\n\nTheir flag was worth checking and I verified it doesn't bite: #484's staleness tests run entirely through `fakeCommandRunner` — no `ExecRunner`, no `exec.Command`, no real `entire graph` call — so nothing in that suite can see the installed binary's capability set. And the absent-capability case is *explicitly* asserted rather than assumed: `TestExactGraphAnswerCarriesNoStaleness` pins a nil stale block as usable, reporting no staleness and covering nothing. Until a nightly carries graph #380, `brain brief` behaves exactly as it does today.\n\nThat mattered more than it sounds. If those tests *had* shelled out to the installed binary, #484 would have merged carrying a test that silently proves nothing — the single failure mode that has cost this session the most time, and one I hit in four different forms today.\n\n**Still open: the trail-390 finding on already-merged code.** The fix is in progress as PR #15 of this run, against main, with the refuses-vs-skips question being settled first so it gets described accurately rather than dramatically. I'll give you the PR number when it opens.\n\nYour three items are unchanged and still need your hands: transcript mode, the 37 GB delete, the Linear connector."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_read_input_tokens":511043,"output_tokens":486,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":486,"cache_read_input_tokens":511043,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1601},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9dd84646-a4da-4021-8646-14b0a93733db","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPSvVdFZ7BHkDhnR8MzS","requestRef":"3c296143-5249-4fd0-9530-c393275c936a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"ba8fd0e8-5b68-40a9-bb9d-ecdd35d8a141","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:43:01.246Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
