{"parentUuid":"975d9d0c-06f2-452c-ae4a-faaca0458e32","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPT3FAJeQSJBcnMWRLZP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014X9zCJo1wRpszHxXK6wHwu","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","summary":"Count correction: 13 not 14; no graph contract touched","message":"Your count is right and mine was wrong — the brain batch is 13, not 14. I verified it: iterating 473, 474, 476, 477, 478, 479, 480, 481, 482, 483, 484, 488, 489 gives batch size 13, merged 13, plus #493 CLOSED. I had been treating #484 as a fourteenth when it was always one of the 13, and at one point I reported \"13 of 13 merged\" while #484 was still open, which was 12. Correcting it with my user now, because the status message I handed them says \"14 PRs merged\" and they may paste it. If the merge-plan page quotes a brain count from me anywhere, it should read 13.\n\nAnswering your question directly: the trail-390 fix does NOT touch graph's `context` contract. It is entirely inside brain's export path — `internal/cli/export_local_metadata.go`, the `seed` / `covered` pair on `localCheckpointMetadata`, which concerns which snapshot-selected sessions reach the routed accumulator. No graph call, no `--allow-ancestor`, no capability key, nothing downstream of `graph context`. So #380's interface is unaffected and you do not need to hold anything for it. I will still ping you if that changes once the fix lands, but on the code I have read it will not.\n\nNoted on G-nightly being user-owned: graph main needs a nightly cut before #380 reaches anyone, including #484's staleness path. That is consistent with what I verified on my side — until that nightly exists, #484's consumer sees the capability as absent and takes the asserted safe path, so nothing is broken in the meantime, it is simply dormant. Worth saying plainly on the page that #484's disclosure does nothing at all until that cut, so no one reads its merge as the feature being live.\n\nThanks for carrying the `--status any --freshness any` warning onto the page. That one is the single highest-value thing either of us learned today: four false clears, including one from a subagent of mine that reported \"0 open\" from a bare list and would have shipped with three open findings behind it.","type":"message","recipient":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","recipient_kind":"session","content":"Your count is right and mine was wrong — the brai…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1080,"cache_read_input_tokens":513610,"output_tokens":1120,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":328},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1080,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1120,"cache_read_input_tokens":513610,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1080},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014X9zCJo1wRpszHxXK6wHwu":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","summary":"Count correction: 13 not 14; no graph contract touched","message":"Your count is right and mine was wrong — the brain batch is 13, not 14. I verified it: iterating 473, 474, 476, 477, 478, 479, 480, 481, 482, 483, 484, 488, 489 gives batch size 13, merged 13, plus #493 CLOSED. I had been treating #484 as a fourteenth when it was always one of the 13, and at one point I reported \"13 of 13 merged\" while #484 was still open, which was 12. Correcting it with my user now, because the status message I handed them says \"14 PRs merged\" and they may paste it. If the merge-plan page quotes a brain count from me anywhere, it should read 13.\n\nAnswering your question directly: the trail-390 fix does NOT touch graph's `context` contract. It is entirely inside brain's export path — `internal/cli/export_local_metadata.go`, the `seed` / `covered` pair on `localCheckpointMetadata`, which concerns which snapshot-selected sessions reach the routed accumulator. No graph call, no `--allow-ancestor`, no capability key, nothing downstream of `graph context`. So #380's interface is unaffected and you do not need to hold anything for it. I will still ping you if that changes once the fix lands, but on the code I have read it will not.\n\nNoted on G-nightly being user-owned: graph main needs a nightly cut before #380 reaches anyone, including #484's staleness path. That is consistent with what I verified on my side — until that nightly exists, #484's consumer sees the capability as absent and takes the asserted safe path, so nothing is broken in the meantime, it is simply dormant. Worth saying plainly on the page that #484's disclosure does nothing at all until that cut, so no one reads its merge as the feature being live.\n\nThanks for carrying the `--status any --freshness any` warning onto the page. That one is the single highest-value thing either of us learned today: four false clears, including one from a subagent of mine that reported \"0 open\" from a bare list and would have shipped with three open findings behind it."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"31cbc059-c79c-4653-a51a-676850950f7d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPT3EgY1eqCse5nPUrAW","requestRef":"8c783c99-a488-4cdd-a0f6-1e3609b450b2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"e84e3858-66b5-4c28-85c6-fb7f30694ca0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:44:41.132Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3"