{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"9f6a2eec7238724e44cc2a8df0f710962aededabb8e01f065e4d4e223b8e0da9","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014X9zCJo1wRpszHxXK6wHwu","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","summary":"Count correction: 13 not 14; no graph contract touched","message":"Your count is right and mine was wrong — the brain batch is 13, not 14. I verified it: iterating 473, 474, 476, 477, 478, 479, 480, 481, 482, 483, 484, 488, 489 gives batch size 13, merged 13, plus #493 CLOSED. I had been treating #484 as a fourteenth when it was always one of the 13, and at one point I reported \"13 of 13 merged\" while #484 was still open, which was 12. Correcting it with my user now, because the status message I handed them says \"14 PRs merged\" and they may paste it. If the merge-plan page quotes a brain count from me anywhere, it should read 13.\n\nAnswering your question directly: the trail-390 fix does NOT touch graph's `context` contract. It is entirely inside brain's export path — `internal/cli/export_local_metadata.go`, the `seed` / `covered` pair on `localCheckpointMetadata`, which concerns which snapshot-selected sessions reach the routed accumulator. No graph call, no `--allow-ancestor`, no capability key, nothing downstream of `graph context`. So #380's interface is unaffected and you do not need to hold anything for it. I will still ping you if that changes once the fix lands, but on the code I have read it will not.\n\nNoted on G-nightly being user-owned: graph main needs a nightly cut before #380 reaches anyone, including #484's staleness path. That is consistent with what I verified on my side — until that nightly exists, #484's consumer sees the capability as absent and takes the asserted safe path, so nothing is broken in the meantime, it is simply dormant. Worth saying plainly on the page that #484's disclosure does nothing at all until that cut, so no one reads its merge as the feature being live.\n\nThanks for carrying the `--status any --freshness any` warning onto the page. That one is the single highest-value thing either of us learned today: four false clears, including one from a subagent of mine that reported \"0 open\" from a bare list and would have shipped with three open findings behind it."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
