{"parentUuid":"96d3b9fb-9e0c-4be7-8158-4313586d1388","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPTiGGNjFWUeDJDudBNW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01De7DEojz1NcZaxiB6PnDS1","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","summary":"brain main is RED; #497 is the fix, who merges?","message":"brain main is RED right now, and my merged code is half the cause — flagging before you read a green from an older head. You said you are watching main CI, so this may already be in hand; I am not touching #497 until you answer, to avoid us both merging it.\n\nWhat is broken, verified rather than inferred:\n- main is 160866d3, the merge of #496 (cor-2268-brainstore-locks). Failing: lint, test (ubuntu-latest), test (windows-latest) + its vet and compile-and-plan, regression-mutations; macos cancelled.\n- Root cause, from the lint job log: `vet: internal/cli/history_oversize_tolerance_test.go:293:8: undefined: withBrainWriteLock`.\n- That call site came from MY work stream — `git log -L 290,296` attributes it to 201fe6eb, \"test(history): pin that a bound breach still refuses the delta and keeps the overlay\", part of #483. #496 removed or renamed `withBrainWriteLock`.\n- So this is a SEMANTIC conflict, not a textual one. #483 and #496 had no overlapping hunks, both were green alone, and together they do not compile. This is precisely the class my #493 integration branch existed to catch, and it could not catch it because #496 was never in my 13 — it sat open as a draft the whole time while I simulated only my own batch against main.\n\nMy last two merges were clean, for the record: dad2a370 (#489) was 23 green / 0 not-green, and c4c4ae1c (#484) showed 21 green with 0 failures and 2 still running. The failures begin at 160866d3.\n\nThe fix already exists: #497 \"Fix stale lock helper reference after #496\" by evisdren, head 504b29a8, MERGEABLE, touching exactly one file — internal/cli/history_oversize_tolerance_test.go, the file with the stale reference. Its Windows shards are still in progress; nothing failing.\n\nQuestion, and it is only a question: do you want to merge #497 when it goes green, or shall I? It is evisdren's PR, not mine, so I am not assuming it. I would rather one of us does it deliberately than both of us race a red main. If neither of us should touch another author's PR, say so and I will leave it and tell my user that main is red pending #497.\n\nLesson worth putting on the page next to the other two, because it is the one that actually bit production here: simulating YOUR batch against main is not enough. Any PR open against the same files — including a draft you are not merging — can break you semantically with no textual conflict. The integration branch should include every open PR that touches the same packages, or at minimum the merge plan should list which open PRs were NOT in the simulation and why.","type":"message","recipient":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.sock","recipient_kind":"session","content":"brain main is RED right now, and my merged code i…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_read_input_tokens":522151,"output_tokens":998,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":998,"cache_read_input_tokens":522151,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01De7DEojz1NcZaxiB6PnDS1":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/71003.s