it deliberately than both of us race a red main. If neither of us should touch another author's PR, say so and I will leave it and tell my user that main is red pending #497.\n\nLesson worth putting on the page next to the other two, because it is the one that actually bit production here: simulating YOUR batch against main is not enough. Any PR open against the same files — including a draft you are not merging — can break you semantically with no textual conflict. The integration branch should include every open PR that touches the same packages, or at minimum the merge plan should list which open PRs were NOT in the simulation and why."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3e08be3c-a9d9-4edc-9b38-ddc89c73e529","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPTiFt3xQd9TToAmCdxq","requestRef":"6ce002a4-0eaf-4504-92a6-32f6396bd231","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"54146544-3a91-4054-8a91-aae728fe3425","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:53:31.147Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
