{"parentUuid":"a3e13b44-8544-4dc8-bec9-f959d9c60cf5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPTjbEuwWht7E9oUx4oz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**brain main is RED, and my merged code is half the cause.** You need to know this before anything else.\n\n```\nmain 160866d3  = merge of #496 (cor-2268-brainstore-locks, not mine)\nFAILING: lint · ubuntu · windows (+vet, compile) · regression-mutations\nCAUSE:   vet: internal/cli/history_oversize_tolerance_test.go:293:8\n              undefined: withBrainWriteLock\n```\n\nThat call site is **mine** — `git log -L` attributes it to `201fe6eb`, part of #483. #496 removed the helper. A **semantic** conflict: no overlapping hunks, both PRs green alone, together they don't compile.\n\n**And this is the exact failure #493 existed to catch.** It couldn't, because #496 was never in my 13 — it sat open as a draft the entire session while I simulated only my own batch against main, repeatedly, and called it clean. Simulating *your* batch against main proves nothing about the other PRs aimed at the same files. That's a real hole in how I verified all day.\n\nMy own merges were clean: `dad2a370` (#489) 23 green / 0 failures; `c4c4ae1c` (#484) 21 green, 0 failures, 2 still running. The breakage starts at #496's merge.\n\n**The fix already exists** — #497 by evisdren, `MERGEABLE`, touching exactly the one file with the stale reference, Windows shards still running with nothing failing. I have **not** merged it: it's another author's PR and the graph session said it's watching main CI, so I've asked which of us takes it rather than race a red main.\n\nSo, honestly: 13 of 13 merged, but **main is not green**, and I'd rather tell you that than let the merge count stand as the headline. Either #497 lands and main recovers, or say the word and I'll merge it myself."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1169,"cache_read_input_tokens":523152,"output_tokens":606,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1169,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":606,"cache_read_input_tokens":523152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1169,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1169},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9ec4d3e7-3d8b-4583-928b-a6e6c64cc9fc","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPTjaq72GGvKZX688Dng","requestRef":"7b6263e2-0fdf-44d3-b706-61ee60db0662","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"dcab693d-3d80-4601-ad65-3be5819f50f6","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:53:40.685Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-integ3","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
