{"parentUuid":"e1150780-8685-472a-9912-66c9d52893b4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01FPSWAPWS8EE8ydqFvH22Jw","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3563a26b-bb76-4e23-8479-54194a27898b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:04:22.313Z","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/.claude/worktrees/agent-a7cc43cd2264da29d","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"3563a26b-bb76-4e23-8479-54194a27898b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPUYc17P12Ex6oF7hhqm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Both of #499's guards are now independently proven load-bearing** — and reproducibly, because I fixed the build first:\n\n```\nW-A  seed filter disabled   → --- FAIL ×2 (SeedsOnlyCoveredSessions,\n                                DoesNotCoverANonCommittedCheckpoint)\nW-B  IsLogsOnly gate off    → --- FAIL ×1 (DoesNotCoverANonCommittedCheckpoint)\n     package compiling both times (vet silent) · each test reds for its own half\n```\n\nThat last detail matters: the two tests fail for *different* guards, so neither is a bystander riding the other's assertion.\n\nI did **not** merge evisdren's #497 to get here. I applied the same one-line correction — `brainstore.WithBrainWriteLock` — to my own branch, which is mine to change. If #497 lands first the edits are identical and merge cleanly; I'll note it on the PR either way.\n\n`gofmt` is silent, `vet` is exit 0, and the full unfiltered suite is running — the same run whose earlier \"exit 0\" I couldn't accept, because the branch provably didn't compile at the head the agent reported it from. I'd rather re-earn that result than relay it.\n\n**Two things remain genuinely not mine:**\n\n- **main is red** at `160866d3` pending **#497**, which is evisdren's own PR on his own break. He merged #496 and opened the fix within minutes; reaching into another author's PR isn't covered by your \"merge\" instruction, and the graph session independently reached the same conclusion. Say so and I'll merge it in one command.\n- **Your four:** transcript mode, the 37 GB delete, the Linear connector, and the graph nightly cut.\n\nWhat *is* finished: 13 of 13 brain PRs merged, 12 of 12 graph PRs merged, and #499 open with its own verification now standing on its own feet rather than on a report I couldn't reproduce."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":692,"cache_read_input_tokens":541818,"output_tokens":644,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":692,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":644,"cache_read_input_tokens":541818,"cache_creation_input_tokens":692,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":692},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"14f374a7-6278-41b2-a0b2-7d25f5594214","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPUYbe2xw9BiXzK2afxP","requestRef":"babee109-a53b-441b-99e8-b0b7ceae1301","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"acd7f175-8014-4ab2-9afc-9e7ee0700e08","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:04:22.312Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/.claude/worktrees/agent-a7cc43cd2264da29d","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
